WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:12.480
On March 15th, 2011, Martin Sims was wandering&nbsp;
down the streets of Carson, California. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.180
clothes were ragged, he was filthy, and gibbering&nbsp;
like a madman with a full beard and long, unkempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:24.060
hair. His body was covered in scars, but he showed&nbsp;
no signs of malnutrition. What made Martin’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.800
sudden appearance so remarkable? He’d been&nbsp;
missing for three years. When he was interviewed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.120
by police, they asked him where he’d been all this&nbsp;
time. They couldn’t believe his answer. He’d been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.720
trapped in an Ikea since 2008. But this was no&nbsp;
ordinary Ikea – this was a dangerous anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.120
that would come to be known as SCP-3008 .
Martin’s strange answers in his interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.440
were laughed off by his interviewing officers,&nbsp;
who assumed he was either crazy or under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.100
influence of something, but they caught&nbsp;
the attention of an SCP Foundation Field&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.540
Agent embedded in the precinct. The report was&nbsp;
passed up the chain to a local Site Director,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.820
who approved a detachment of Foundation Field&nbsp;
Operatives to look into Martin’s case. While he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.920
was reluctant to lead the Foundation Agents back&nbsp;
to the offending Ikea – the Foundation can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.500
extremely persuasive. His screams of “Please, I’m&nbsp;
begging you, don’t take me back! Don’t make me go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.960
back!” were noted but ultimately disregarded.
When the SCP Foundation had triangulated the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.300
position of SCP-3008 , which was indeed&nbsp;
an active Ikea, the entire retail zone was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:29.760
closed and barricaded under the pretence of a&nbsp;
severe black mold infestation. Armed Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.380
Personnel also arrived on site shortly after,&nbsp;
based on Martin’s vague statements that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.120
were creatures of some kind inside. Due to his&nbsp;
deteriorating mental health, Martin was unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.120
to provide a great deal of lucid information on&nbsp;
the specific traits of SCP-3008 , but one phrase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.460
he kept repeating was “bigger on the inside.”
Once researchers were satisfied that Martin had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.360
delivered all the pertinent information he&nbsp;
was able to, he was administered Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.700
Amnestics to erase his memory of the last three&nbsp;
years and returned to his family. A cover story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.680
was formulated: Martin had been kidnapped and&nbsp;
abused for three years by a mentally-unbalanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.300
stalker in downtown Carson. He’d been able to&nbsp;
escape as said stalker took his own life out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.280
guilt – a suicide that the Foundation expertly&nbsp;
fabricated to make their cover story airtight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.500
With the loose end of Martin Sims taken care of,&nbsp;
the true observation of SCP-3008 could begin.&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.660
A base set around the perimeter of the mysterious&nbsp;
Ikea kept a 24-hour watch on the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.820
covering all potential entrances and exits. No&nbsp;
exploratory missions had yet been approved by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.140
the Foundation ethics committee, so they first&nbsp;
wanted to perform a week of external observation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.220
to see if any of the store’s anomalous&nbsp;
properties extended beyond the confines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.660
of the building. After a week of nothing, it&nbsp;
appeared they did not. A local Site Director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:48.540
approved the use of twenty disposable Class-D&nbsp;
Personnel to explore the interior of SCP-3008 .&nbsp;

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.280
The D-Class operatives would be split into&nbsp;
four squads of five men – Alpha, Bravo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.780
Charlie, and Delta Squad. Each would be assigned a&nbsp;
different quadrant of the store, and would deliver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.940
information back to the control team on site via&nbsp;
a live audio and video link. Three of the four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.680
teams, upon entering the store, reported nothing&nbsp;
out of the ordinary. Neither the audio or video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.700
they were sending back indicated anything&nbsp;
different from a standard Ikea store – from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.860
the flat-pack wardrobes to the Swedish meatballs.&nbsp;
Team Delta, however, suddenly began experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.880
a scrambled audio and video connection.
Shortly after, communication with Team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.620
Delta dropped off entirely. They disappeared&nbsp;
somewhere inside the store, and haven’t been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:30.960
seen since – with one notable exception. After&nbsp;
the disappearance of the extraction of teams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:36.960
Foundation Researchers classified SCP-3008 as&nbsp;
Euclid, because its anomalous properties were at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.540
least confined to the interior of the store. And&nbsp;
even then, seemingly not the entire interior. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:49.800
anomalous area within SCP-3008 became known as&nbsp;
SCP-3008-1, and containment appeared to be 100%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.480
secure. There was no telling how many people had&nbsp;
already gone missing in the store over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.620
but the disappearances must be stopped.
The Foundation maintained constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.880
surveillance around the perimeter of SCP-3008&nbsp;
, but it appeared they could prevent any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.340
further “incidents” by simply preventing other&nbsp;
civilians from accessing the Ikea store. Martin’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:12.780
ravings about monsters were assumed to just&nbsp;
be the product of delirium. Until a surviving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.640
member of Delta Team suddenly reappeared.
The date was November 3rd, 2011. It was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:22.020
cold night, a few hours after what would have&nbsp;
been closing time if the store were still active&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:27.360
and seven months after the extraction teams had&nbsp;
disappeared somewhere in the confines of SCP-3008.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.040
There had been no anomalous activity outside&nbsp;
the store since the perimeter was first secured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:37.380
and Foundation researchers hadn’t expected that to&nbsp;
change, until the last surviving member of Delta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.820
Team came barging out of the store’s entrance.&nbsp;
Startled Field Operatives were amazed to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.720
him again, but they were even more amazed to&nbsp;
see what was following him out of the store,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.620
repeating the same phrase: “The store is&nbsp;
now closed, please exit the building.”&nbsp;

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.000
Despite the fact that the entity chasing the&nbsp;
Delta Team survivor was wearing the yellow shirt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.400
and blue pants of an Ikea store employee, the&nbsp;
being was definitely not human. It was around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:05.400
seven feet tall, with no visible face. The entity&nbsp;
had grossly extended limbs – with each arm being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.380
around five or six feet long, and ending in&nbsp;
a huge, oversized hand. The whole process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:15.000
was so sudden that the Field Agents present at&nbsp;
the perimeter weren’t able to save the Delta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.560
Team survivor, as the entity reached forward&nbsp;
with its freakishly long arms, grabbed him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.360
and twisted his head off like a child with a doll.
The Field Operatives present drew their weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.820
and peppered the entity with bullets. It would&nbsp;
later be classified as SCP-3008-2. The being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.620
appeared to collapse and die from the physical&nbsp;
trauma, at which point both it and the body of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:38.520
the former Delta Team survivor were taken&nbsp;
for an autopsy by Foundation researchers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.540
There were no biological abnormalities&nbsp;
to the body of the Delta Team survivor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:48.660
so it did not appear that the anomalous properties&nbsp;
of SCP-3008-1 had any effect on the physiology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:53.580
of its occupants. He was not malnourished despite&nbsp;
being missing for months, and the contents of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.740
stomach looked to be half-digested food consistent&nbsp;
with the menu of a typical Ikea store restaurant.&nbsp;

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:05.580
SCP-3008-2, on the other hand, raised a number&nbsp;
of perplexing biological questions. The autopsy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.720
revealed that the creature’s clothes were actually&nbsp;
a part of its body, like an additional layer of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.700
skin. The creature lacked blood or any kind of&nbsp;
vascular system. Even stranger, the entity didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.740
appear to have any bones or internal organs, not&nbsp;
even a brain or nervous system. It was a being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.780
made entirely of skin, all the way to its core.&nbsp;
How it was able to move, or even live for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.220
matter, remains a mystery. Though when you work&nbsp;
for The SCP Foundation, you learn to accept that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.700
some things will always remain unexplained.
One thing was certain, though:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:37.320
Martin Sims was right about his monsters.
After the incident with Delta Team, the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:42.540
deemed that sending manned explorations into the&nbsp;
heart of SCP-3008 was too much of a liability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:47.220
and planned a series of drone-based reconnaissance&nbsp;
missions into the anomaly. The first of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.820
drones experienced connection issues and&nbsp;
failed when attempting to venture into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:55.320
Ikea’s anomalous zone. However, after a lengthy&nbsp;
period of trial and error, the Foundation was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:00.720
able to establish a more secure connection with&nbsp;
its drones, even when deep into the SCP-3008-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.400
anomalous zone. It was only then that some of&nbsp;
the most extraordinary discoveries were made.&nbsp;

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:12.000
SCP-3008-1 seemed to break the laws of spatial&nbsp;
reality, as the area of the Ikea’s interior was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.500
at least an order of magnitude larger than&nbsp;
its exterior. Just as Martin Sims had said:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:21.060
It was bigger on the inside. But just how much&nbsp;
bigger? The Foundation has yet to find evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:26.640
of any physical terminators within the store that&nbsp;
might indicate SCP-3008-1 has an “end point.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.440
While an area of at least ten kilometres&nbsp;
squared has been uncovered in SCP-3008-1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:36.240
it could – in theory – be infinite. Laser&nbsp;
rangefinder tests, which are normally very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:41.400
reliable, have only given inconclusive results.
Interestingly, the anomalous area doesn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:46.200
any clear, visual differences from the rest of&nbsp;
the Ikea store except that it extends forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:51.840
An individual trapped within the confines of&nbsp;
SCP-3008-1 wouldn’t even realize that they’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.400
entered an anomalous zone until they tried&nbsp;
to locate an exit and leave, at which point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:02.760
they’d find they were already hopelessly lost. The&nbsp;
geography of SCP-3008-1 does at least appear to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:07.140
consistent, so people trapped within are&nbsp;
theoretically able to retrace their steps and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:11.640
escape if they hadn’t already ventured too deep.
According to data collected during the drone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:16.560
reconnaissance missions, SCP-3008-2, of&nbsp;
which there appeared to be a vast population,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:21.780
would wander the stores aimlessly during the day.&nbsp;
They were unresponsive to the drone’s presence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:25.920
and did not appear to be aggressive. While the&nbsp;
physical descriptions of these creatures could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:31.440
vary slightly, they all followed the same overall&nbsp;
trend: “Clothes” consistent with the Ikea uniform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.940
no face, either seemingly too tall or&nbsp;
too short, and limbs that are grossly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:39.360
out of proportion with their bodies.
As the Foundation began sending drones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.580
deeper into SCP-3008-1, they found another&nbsp;
incredible discovery. There was an unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:48.960
population of humans trapped inside the&nbsp;
Ikea’s anomalous zone, and these people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.760
had used the Ikea furniture around them to&nbsp;
create entire settlements and towns within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.960
the store. There were several of these towns,&nbsp;
all of which seemed to cohabitate peacefully.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:02.160
Even Foundation personnel found this development&nbsp;
in their research to be truly extraordinary.&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:07.680
Since SCP-3008 was first identified, there&nbsp;
have been only fourteen civilian escapes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.480
Some had been trapped inside for months, others&nbsp;
had been in there for years – some far longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.860
than Martin’s three-year stint. While every one&nbsp;
of these escapees has eventually been released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:21.840
back to their home, after a liberal application&nbsp;
of Amnestics and a proper cover story has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:27.000
devised, the Foundation interviewed each of them&nbsp;
extensively first. According to these escapees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.660
the people trapped inside the Ikea&nbsp;
have built an entirely new society&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:34.080
across the various settlements.
Contrary to the “Lord of the Flies”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:39.000
expectations of a group of people isolated and&nbsp;
afraid, there’s immense cooperation between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:45.480
trapped civilians. The food in the several Ikea&nbsp;
restaurants in SCP-3008-1 mysteriously replenishes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:50.100
while nobody is there, so there’s no threat of&nbsp;
starving. And the automatic turning on and off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:54.540
of the lights forms a kind of rudimentary&nbsp;
day and night cycle. Night time, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.540 --> 00:10:00.780
is when things get dangerous, as the SCP-3008-2&nbsp;
entities – which are known to the people inside as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:06.000
“The Staff” – become extremely hostile after dark.
Aggressive hordes of the Staff swarm the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.600
settlements at night, repeating “The store&nbsp;
is now closed, please exit the building.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.800
The civilians inside are usually able to&nbsp;
repel these attacks with minimal casualties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.420
but the constant war of attrition slowly wears&nbsp;
down those inside. The bodies of the creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:22.920
also need to be removed from the area after each&nbsp;
attack, as the presence of corpses or even parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:27.060
of corpses has been known to heighten the ferocity&nbsp;
of the next night’s attack. During the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:31.560
the Staff return to a docile and unresponsive&nbsp;
state, though they’ll still defend themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.700
violently if anyone dares to attack.
Over the course of the interviews with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:39.780
fourteen escapees, Foundation Researchers were&nbsp;
able to answer another of their key questions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:45.660
How had so many people gone missing in the store&nbsp;
for so long without being noticed? But the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:50.520
they received only raised many more unsettling&nbsp;
queries. According to the escapees, there were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:55.320
people inside the settlements that, despite being&nbsp;
otherwise of entirely sound mind and standard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:59.820
intelligence, seemed to lack very common knowledge&nbsp;
that even a child should know. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:04.380
some weren’t aware of the International Space&nbsp;
Station orbiting the earth, or stranger still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:08.460
the existence of the Statue of Liberty.
This led the Researchers to a frightening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:14.820
conclusion: SCP-3008-1 may not only be a nexus&nbsp;
point of multiple Ikea stores in our dimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:19.320
it could be connected to Ikeas in every&nbsp;
dimension where Ikeas exist. While it only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.940
abducts a handful of people from each store over&nbsp;
an extended period of time, it suddenly becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:28.980
clear how this SCP was able to trap so many people&nbsp;
without detection over such a long period of time.&nbsp;

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:34.500
Which, in turn, led to an even more terrifying&nbsp;
revelation: The SCP Foundation may not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:41.580
SCP-3008-1 as contained as they thought. It might&nbsp;
even be tucked away in an Ikea somewhere near you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:45.840
just waiting for you to visit. After&nbsp;
all, there’s always room for one more…

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:51.060
An SCP Foundation researcher sits at a&nbsp;
table inside of a standard containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:56.520
cell. These are often dangerous places to&nbsp;
be, especially when the SCP you’re supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.140
to be studying is one that you can’t&nbsp;
see. The researcher is taking notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:07.320
unsure of exactly what’s going to happen next.&nbsp;
He can hear the sounds of knives scraping behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:14.100
of flesh sizzling and searing from high heat. He&nbsp;
braces himself as a burst of heat hits the back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.360
of his head, as if a fireball has erupted. Just&nbsp;
then it happens - an object floats through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:23.940
air and settles in front of him on the table.&nbsp;
It’s a plate of food, and it looks delicious.&nbsp;

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:29.160
It may surprise you to learn that there is&nbsp;
no rule that the SCP Foundation must deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:35.640
exclusively with violent and vicious creatures.&nbsp;
Not every SCP held in containment shares the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:42.840
malevolence and contempt for humanity as SCP-682,&nbsp;
or the world-ending threat posed by the likes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:51.000
SCP-2317. Some - perhaps not many, but some - are&nbsp;
benign and might even seem outwardly friendly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:55.560
but you’d still be taking a huge risk&nbsp;
to assume that anything contained by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:02.340
SCP Foundation is completely harmless.
Such is the case with SCP-5031. As per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:07.500
the Foundation’s containment procedures, this&nbsp;
quasi-humanoid – meaning it appears to have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:12.840
vaguely human features - is held in an airtight&nbsp;
cell that is regularly checked by Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:20.520
personnel on a bi-weekly basis. SCP-5031 has no&nbsp;
need for regular nutrition or regular interactions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:27.780
from staff. The trick with SCP-5031, is not being&nbsp;
eaten by it, since though it doesn’t need food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:33.360
it does still hunt and consume anything&nbsp;
it encounters - human or otherwise.&nbsp;

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:38.580
Avoiding being eaten is hard enough with&nbsp;
creatures that can actually be seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:45.000
but like so many other creatures the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps contained, SCP-5031 has developed an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:51.060
almost-perfect defense mechanism - which is that&nbsp;
when observed, it will literally cease to exist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.760
Some might choose to refer to this as a ‘quantum&nbsp;
lock’, however it is worth noting that traces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:03.360
left by SCP-5031 still remain observable when the&nbsp;
creature has temporarily disappeared. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:10.560
trails of blood and scratch marks left behind by&nbsp;
SCP-5031 still exist when the SCP itself does not.&nbsp;

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:17.340
Naturally, this makes both avoiding the creature&nbsp;
and capturing it using cameras difficult. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:23.340
when SCP-5031’s existence ceases&nbsp;
it still casts a shadow. From this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.360
researchers have been able to determine&nbsp;
several of the creature’s physical traits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:33.600
Based on its silhouette, it has been deduced&nbsp;
that SCP-5031 levitates about half a meter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:38.220
above ground level, it sports an abnormally&nbsp;
small, neckless head atop an elongated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:45.180
torso - approximately 1.9 meters long - with three&nbsp;
sets of spindly lower arms that branch outwards.&nbsp;

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:50.820
Using these arms and its loosely hanging&nbsp;
body, SCP-5031 will lower itself to hunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:56.640
any human or animal that draws near to it&nbsp;
and uses the bladelike tail to cut up food.&nbsp;

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:04.140
Perhaps the most interesting facet of SCP-5031&nbsp;
beyond its defensive capabilities and apparent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:10.440
physical attributes, are the series of nine tests&nbsp;
conducted by Senior Researcher Stanley Huxtable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:15.720
Appalled by the conditions that the creature was&nbsp;
being kept in, Huxtable took over the role of HCL&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:22.140
Supervisor for SCP-5031. Having grown increasingly&nbsp;
frustrated and empathetic towards the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:26.880
listening to its screams from inside its&nbsp;
iron containment unit, Huxtable devised a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:32.760
series of tests to introduce SCP-5031 to various&nbsp;
different stimuli as a way to better understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:38.280
the creature and hopefully keep it contained in a&nbsp;
way that didn’t seem to cause so much suffering.&nbsp;

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:43.860
It's worth remembering that the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
makes it its mission to be cold, not cruel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:49.620
in performing their duties to protect normality&nbsp;
and many of the researchers and staff are just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.940
capable of having empathy for creatures as&nbsp;
you might for a stray animal at a shelter.&nbsp;

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:59.640
The first of Huxtable’s tests involved&nbsp;
installing speakers in SCP-5031’s cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:04.320
through which a variety of different ambient and&nbsp;
popular pieces of music were played to see if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:10.140
they had any effect on reducing the creature’s&nbsp;
stress. By judging SCP-5031’s stress levels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:15.360
based on how much it screamed when compared to&nbsp;
normal, Huxtable was able to determine how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:21.360
best to use music to calm the creature. SCP-5031&nbsp;
seemed to convey higher levels of stress when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:27.120
listening to ‘Morning Forest’, ‘Deep Grotto’&nbsp;
and ‘Seaside Paradise’ ambience, as well as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:33.540
best of late 60s British rock band Jethro Tull.
However, the best of Mozart, Enya, KISS and Ben&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:39.840
Folds produced dramatically different results,&nbsp;
decreasing SCP-5031’s apparent stress. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:45.600
this test, Senior Researcher Huxtable compiled&nbsp;
a playlist featuring SCP-5031’s favorite music.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:52.500
Over time, the stress-reducing effects of music&nbsp;
on SCP-5031 seemed to decrease, but keeping the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:57.180
playlist on shuffle seemed to keep the creature&nbsp;
consistently calmer than it had been previously.&nbsp;

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:04.380
The next test involved introducing inanimate&nbsp;
objects into SCP-5031’s enclosure to monitor its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:09.660
reactions and how its stress levels were affected.&nbsp;
When a softball was thrown into the enclosure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:16.260
SCP-5031 immediately sliced the ball in two with&nbsp;
its tail in one swift motion. A similar result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:21.360
occurred when researchers threw the creature a&nbsp;
basketball, which was quickly punctured and sliced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:26.820
open by SCP-5031’s tail. Its stress levels&nbsp;
first seemed to diminish when the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:31.260
was offered a bowling ball, which it rolled&nbsp;
around the enclosure and then later knocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:36.240
against a second bowling ball. However, when&nbsp;
one of the balls chipped, rendering it unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:42.720
to roll properly, SCP-5031’s stress increased&nbsp;
dramatically, until a replacement was offered.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:49.020
Researcher Huxtable noted that SCP-5031 seemed&nbsp;
to possess a similar level of motor skills to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:53.640
an average human toddler, with similarly&nbsp;
explosive emotional reactions to match.&nbsp;

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:59.160
Next, when given the choice between two food&nbsp;
sources at opposite ends of its enclosure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:04.620
SCP-5031 seemed to gravitate towards&nbsp;
higher-quality food, most notably favoring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:10.200
cooked rotisserie chickens over animal carcasses.&nbsp;
It even chose this option over a live chicken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:15.060
using its tail to cut its food into more&nbsp;
manageable bite-sized portions, rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:21.900
ripping its meat with its hands or teeth like many&nbsp;
of its fellow SCPs. Researcher Huxtable recorded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:27.780
these findings and highlighted that, even though&nbsp;
SCP-5031 didn’t need to eat in order to survive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:33.000
providing the creature with food of a better&nbsp;
quality marginally reduced its stress.&nbsp;

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:40.440
Senior Researcher Huxtable next attempted to test&nbsp;
SCP-5031’s coexistence with other living subjects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:46.980
each time making sure that the creature had been&nbsp;
adequately fed to avoid any unseemly incidents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:52.920
First, a live chicken was introduced.&nbsp;
SCP-5031 rolled its bowling ball at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:56.880
high speed towards the chicken, increasing&nbsp;
both its and the chicken’s stress levels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:02.280
and inadvertently killing the chicken in the&nbsp;
process. When a second chicken was introduced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:08.340
SCP-5031 gently rolled a basketball towards it but&nbsp;
ceased any further engagement after the chicken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:13.200
squawked from being hit by the ball. Next to be&nbsp;
introduced into the enclosure was a blindfolded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:19.320
D Class staff member, who was instructed to sit&nbsp;
down and roll the basketball towards SCP-5031.&nbsp;

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:24.180
After doing so for several minutes, the&nbsp;
creature began to approach the D class subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:28.860
who was instructed to remove their blindfold to&nbsp;
cease the creature’s existence and prevent any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:34.440
potentially deadly incidents. Finally, Researcher&nbsp;
Huxtable had another Class-D engage in a game of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:41.700
catch with SCP-5031 while facing away from the&nbsp;
creature. This test proceeded successfully, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:47.700
Senior Researcher Huxtable remarked how SCP-5031’s&nbsp;
motor skills were improving. Albeit gradually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:53.340
and with some gentle encouragement, through&nbsp;
Huxtable’s tests the creature was learning.&nbsp;

00:19:54.180 --> 00:20:00.720
The next test, focused on teaching SCP-5031&nbsp;
linguistic symbols, utilized LCD displays and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:04.980
buttons connected to a food dispenser.&nbsp;
One display showed an image of a rock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:10.800
and the other an image of a rotisserie chicken.&nbsp;
After some brief probing, SCP-5031 was quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:15.000
able to understand that pressing the button&nbsp;
under the correct display would dispense a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.740
rotisserie chicken for it to eat. The creature&nbsp;
was later able to adapt when, the following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:24.960
the screen displays and materials dispensed&nbsp;
were swapped, and then later set to swap at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:29.880
random intervals. When additional rock-dispensing&nbsp;
stations were introduced, this time displaying the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:35.820
word ‘rock’ as opposed to an image, SCP-5031&nbsp;
was able to determine which station dispensed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:40.800
‘chicken’ through a process of elimination.
Whenever the functions and displays were swapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:46.380
SCP-5031 would find whichever displayed the&nbsp;
word ‘chicken’ to receive its food. The final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:52.140
phase of this test presented SCP-5031 with a&nbsp;
single station, displaying the word ‘chicken’,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:57.120
but with a button that would remain inactive&nbsp;
unless the creature spelled out the same word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:02.040
with a collection of lettered blocks it was&nbsp;
provided with. After some initial confusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:08.340
and frustration as to why the button would not&nbsp;
dispense food when pressed, SCP-5031 was able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:13.080
to assemble the word correctly, not only&nbsp;
activating the button and dispensing food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:18.120
but proving to Researcher Huxtable that the&nbsp;
creature was capable of learning language.&nbsp;

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:23.280
Huxtable continued to test the creature,&nbsp;
encouraging it to spell words using lettered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:28.620
blocks as a method of communicating. By&nbsp;
increasing SCP-5031’s vocabulary and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:33.180
amount of human interaction it received,&nbsp;
Senior Researcher Huxtable observed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:39.660
SCP-5031 was gradually learning to sing -&nbsp;
albeit nonverbally - as well as to juggle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:44.340
with its six hands and was even communicating&nbsp;
its own food preferences and dish pairings.&nbsp;

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:52.800
Later, another Class-D, D-52125, was introduced&nbsp;
to SCP-5031’s enclosure to aid in further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:58.680
testing. Through D-52125’s instructions, the&nbsp;
creature quickly learned to draw using crayons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:05.220
and created artworks depicting itself, its&nbsp;
newfound friend D-52125, Researcher Huxtable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:11.580
a cat and a rotisserie chicken.
SCP-5031’s new creative side didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:16.080
stop there though, as the creature quickly&nbsp;
learned to play Chopsticks in only two days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:22.560
once a piano was introduced into the enclosure.&nbsp;
SCP-5031 even managed to start creating its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:28.320
original, admittedly crude, compositions.
Next, a spice rack was placed inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:35.400
creature’s cell and D-52125 demonstrated how&nbsp;
to season meat. This proved to be SCP-5031’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:39.360
new favorite hobby, as it spent the next&nbsp;
three days experimenting with different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:44.340
combinations of foods and spices, using&nbsp;
its letter blocks to request ‘more, more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:52.140
more’ garlic powder. Interestingly, the creature&nbsp;
only created artwork or music when D-52125 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:56.700
present, but seemed to thoroughly enjoy its&nbsp;
experimentation with food when left alone.&nbsp;

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:03.120
Following this development, Senior Researcher&nbsp;
Huxtable devised a new test for SCP-5031.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:10.620
Providing the creature with cooking utensils and&nbsp;
using D-52125 to demonstrate, 5031 was shown how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:16.320
to prepare a variety of different dishes, from&nbsp;
hamburgers and tacos, to Mongolian Beef, steak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:22.380
clam chowder and profiteroles. In addition to a&nbsp;
small peanut allergy, this eighth test revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:29.220
SCP-5031 to be a phenomenal chef, possessing&nbsp;
culinary skills far beyond the average person.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:34.980
The creature quickly and enthusiastically embraced&nbsp;
its newfound talents, concocting its very own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:42.240
brand-new recipes, with D-52125 even volunteering&nbsp;
to be the first to taste test 5031’s dishes.&nbsp;

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:48.420
It was shortly after this test that&nbsp;
SCP-5031 spoke its very first word,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:55.140
and it should come as no surprise that the&nbsp;
word was ‘salt’. Naturally, Senior Researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:55.140 --> 00:23:59.100
Huxtable was very proud of the progress&nbsp;
the creature had made with its development.&nbsp;

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:04.200
The final test almost seemed to be what the&nbsp;
creature was born for. Over the course of two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:10.260
months, SCP-5031 was tasked with creating a full&nbsp;
three-course meal which would then be served to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:15.060
Foundation staff for Thanksgiving.&nbsp;
SCP-5031 not only rose to the task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:19.740
but exceeded all of Researcher Huxtable’s&nbsp;
expectations, creating a meal that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:25.020
Gordon Ramsey would be hard pressed to find&nbsp;
fault with. The creature created a first course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.720
consisting of sweet potato miso soup seasoned&nbsp;
with turmeric. Next came a beautiful duck confit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:36.180
glazed luxuriously with apple cider and topped&nbsp;
generously with sweet cranberry compote, paired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:40.860
with a side of butternut squash gnocchi and served&nbsp;
on a bed of kale seasoned with truffle salt.&nbsp;

00:24:40.860 --> 00:24:45.540
The grand finale of the exquisite meal&nbsp;
was a spiced cassava pie for dessert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:45.540 --> 00:24:50.340
complemented with the finest French vanilla&nbsp;
ice cream and a maple-hazelnut syrup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:57.060
And SCP-5031 didn’t stop there, the creature&nbsp;
also debuted one of its original musical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:57.060 --> 00:25:01.980
compositions to compliment the decadent meal&nbsp;
it had created. As the staff enjoyed the food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:01.980 --> 00:25:09.240
SCP-5031 performed live from its enclosure the&nbsp;
deeply moving Piano Concerto for Six Hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:13.980
to an overwhelmingly positive response&nbsp;
from not only Senior Researcher Huxtable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:20.040
but the entire Foundation staff. As a fitting end&nbsp;
to the creature’s tale, Huxtable reported that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:26.520
during the Thanksgiving banquet it had created,&nbsp;
SCP-5031’s stress levels reduced entirely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:31.800
New kinder containment measures that&nbsp;
would keep 5031 safer but also far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:31.800 --> 00:25:36.360
more contented were submitted for approval.
Perhaps some of you may find it refreshing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:42.120
to learn that SCP-5031 isn’t simply just another&nbsp;
malicious, malevolent monster that the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:42.120 --> 00:25:49.860
has to keep under lock and key for the safety&nbsp;
of the world. Instead, SCP-5031 is a gentle – if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:49.860 --> 00:25:54.660
a little frightening at first creature - that&nbsp;
just requires careful and considered guidance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:54.660 --> 00:26:01.140
instead of a cold iron cage and around-the-clock&nbsp;
armed guards. Through testing, Senior Researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:06.660
Stanley Huxtable and his fellow Foundation staff&nbsp;
were not only able to help the creature develop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:12.540
but also found what makes it tick; and not just&nbsp;
for the purposes of containing it. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:12.540 --> 00:26:18.540
it is hoped that SCP-5031’s creativity and&nbsp;
flair for culinary and musical masterpieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:18.540 --> 00:26:23.280
can continue to thrive and grow, under&nbsp;
the proud watch of Researcher Huxtable.

00:26:23.280 --> 00:26:30.240
Over fifty men and women, clad in red robes,&nbsp;
kneel before an unholy altar. They chant and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:30.240 --> 00:26:38.220
mutter indecipherable words - words of cruelty and&nbsp;
madness… of obsession and sacrilege. Not long ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:45.000
these were regular people. Computer technicians,&nbsp;
teachers, plumbers, construction workers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:50.580
accountants. This was before they fell&nbsp;
under the ungodly influence of a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:50.580 --> 00:26:55.680
ruler. The center of this makeshift place of&nbsp;
worship was once a normal school gymnasium,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:55.680 --> 00:27:03.000
but it’s now the home of a huge statue. A&nbsp;
humanoid being, wreathed in tentacles. Its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:08.520
head is more like a squid or cuttlefish than&nbsp;
anything resembling an actual human face.

00:27:09.120 --> 00:27:14.400
While he’s known to the cultists as the Tentacled&nbsp;
God, the beast they worship is known to the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:21.360
Foundation as SCP - 2662, and he sits in the belly&nbsp;
of one of their expansive containment facilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:21.360 --> 00:27:27.900
locked away from the world. But not for long,&nbsp;
if his devoted followers have anything to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:34.080
about it. This is their god, all-powerful and&nbsp;
unchanging, and when it comes to springing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:34.080 --> 00:27:39.720
him from containment, no tactic is too&nbsp;
vile or underhanded to get the job done.

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:44.820
Their mortal leader and high-priest, a man in&nbsp;
a purple robe calling himself Brother Marsh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:44.820 --> 00:27:50.820
walks among their crouched forms. He whispers&nbsp;
instructions for the great day of liberation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:57.660
that’s soon to come, providing everyone plays&nbsp;
their part. It’s a plan months in the making - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:57.660 --> 00:28:03.720
one that, if it goes off without a hitch, could&nbsp;
free their monstrous god into the world. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:03.720 --> 00:28:10.140
would strike at the very heart of their enemy,&nbsp;
The SCP Foundation, when they least expect it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:10.140 --> 00:28:15.900
and nothing shall stand in their way. How could&nbsp;
they lose when they have a god on their side?

00:28:15.900 --> 00:28:21.840
But why did all these normal people become&nbsp;
violent zealots for squid-faced deity? It all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:27.300
began with a dream. To those who experienced&nbsp;
these dreams, they felt more like prophecies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:34.500
premonitions of the glorious horrors to come.&nbsp;
A red sky, billions dead and billions more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:41.250
enslaved. A dark silhouette on the horizon&nbsp;
- Their Tentacled God, holding dominion over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:41.250 --> 00:28:46.740
all. At first, it just seemed like a strange&nbsp;
nightmare. The ones who experienced it woke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:46.740 --> 00:28:51.780
up shaken and afraid, hoping to shake the&nbsp;
images from their mind. But they couldn’t.

00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:58.440
Every night, the nightmare would return. They’d&nbsp;
see the images - the red sky, the dead and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:58.440 --> 00:29:04.680
enslaved, the Tentacled God. And after a while it&nbsp;
would come to them even when they weren’t asleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:10.740
eventually happening whenever they closed their&nbsp;
eyes. Little by little, this scene stopped looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:10.740 --> 00:29:18.240
so hideous… and started to look glorious. They&nbsp;
felt his presence in their minds, slowly pushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:18.240 --> 00:29:23.880
them towards their inevitable future. They started&nbsp;
to realize that they wanted him to rule over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:29.100
universe, and to experience the honor of&nbsp;
serving him. Many of them abandoned their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:29.100 --> 00:29:35.460
homes and families - leaving their friends and&nbsp;
loved ones left to worry that they’d gone insane.

00:29:35.460 --> 00:29:39.600
In their eyes, they were safer&nbsp;
than they’d ever been. They finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:45.300
had purpose. They were working in service&nbsp;
of something far greater than themselves.

00:29:45.300 --> 00:29:51.180
The influence of the tentacled god drew them&nbsp;
closer to one another. They would meet in secret,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:51.180 --> 00:29:57.000
exchanging information from the prophecies their&nbsp;
ruler sent them in their dreams. They worshipped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:57.000 --> 00:30:02.280
together, building altars and idols to congregate&nbsp;
around. They performed dark blood rituals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:07.680
involving human and animal sacrifice. It&nbsp;
was when Brother Marsh, The Anointed One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:07.680 --> 00:30:12.840
arrived to guide them towards their true&nbsp;
mission that things kicked into high gear.

00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:18.900
Just three months prior, Brother Marsh had been&nbsp;
an office drone working in data entry for a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:18.900 --> 00:30:24.240
insurance company, before the Tentacled God&nbsp;
invaded his thoughts with a simple message:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:31.740
“FREE ME, AND THE NEW WORLD I CREATE&nbsp;
SHALL BE YOUR PLAYGROUND.” Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:31.740 --> 00:30:36.600
he’d devoted himself completely to the&nbsp;
cause, quitting his job and maxing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:42.240
his credit cards to help fund his new life’s&nbsp;
purpose - infiltrating the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:45.960
and releasing his inhuman&nbsp;
ruler from its imprisonment.

00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:49.440
That was the single goal he&nbsp;
united the cultists under:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:55.560
Freedom for the Tentacled God. And at long&nbsp;
last, they had all the pieces in place to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:55.560 --> 00:31:00.720
strike. They’d finally gathered the necessary&nbsp;
intel to subvert the will of the most powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:00.720 --> 00:31:05.400
secret organization on earth. Even the&nbsp;
strongest institution is made of people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:12.240
and people are weak. Unlike the almighty&nbsp;
Tentacled God, people could be broken.

00:31:12.240 --> 00:31:18.780
The people in question were Kelly Thompson,&nbsp;
Sidney Levitt, Jordan Brosh, Dr. Juan Gutierrez,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:18.780 --> 00:31:23.880
and Gillian Larson. Dr. Juan Gutierrez&nbsp;
was a researcher with Level 3 clearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:28.740
on the site where the Tentacled God was being&nbsp;
contained. Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:28.740 --> 00:31:33.780
both Security Officers charged with verifying&nbsp;
personnel clearance on site. Kelly Thompson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:33.780 --> 00:31:37.500
was a member of Site Administration&nbsp;
with research authorization powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:42.840
and Gillian Larson was a research assistant&nbsp;
who often collaborated with Dr. Gutierrez.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:50.880
These five were the key to getting access to&nbsp;
SCP-2662 and bringing their plan to fruition.

00:31:50.880 --> 00:31:56.040
Normally, personnel dossiers on people working&nbsp;
for the Foundation were highly confidential,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:56.040 --> 00:32:01.980
but the Devotees of the Tentacled God had their&nbsp;
ways. They had a number of computer experts in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:06.960
their ranks more than capable of hacking in and&nbsp;
pulling some basic information off of Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:12.300
servers without being detected. For the other&nbsp;
information they needed they turned to some good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:12.300 --> 00:32:17.640
old-fashioned torture, which is often the most&nbsp;
effective method when you need some quick results.

00:32:17.640 --> 00:32:22.560
Of course, while the cult’s grip on&nbsp;
sanity may have been a little tenuous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:28.560
they weren’t stupid. While gathering their intel,&nbsp;
they also made sure to find out what exactly they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:35.640
were up against. SCP-2662 was being held in&nbsp;
a humanoid containment cell, and guarded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:41.640
on-site Task Force TAU-9, better known as the&nbsp;
“Belligerent Bodyguards.” These aren’t lazy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:41.640 --> 00:32:47.760
donut-chomping mall cops - these are a heavily&nbsp;
trained, heavily armed fighting force. Though the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:47.760 --> 00:32:53.820
cultists had one thing that these Foundation&nbsp;
soldiers didn’t: The element of surprise.

00:32:53.820 --> 00:32:59.460
For everything to go off perfectly, Brother&nbsp;
Marsh’s plans would have to be executed within a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:59.460 --> 00:33:05.160
single day, and they were already on the clock.&nbsp;
TAU-9 had been charged with tracking down any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:05.160 --> 00:33:11.700
new SCP - 2662 cults and dismantling them, and&nbsp;
Brother Marsh knew that it was only a matter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:11.700 --> 00:33:17.340
time before the Foundation tracked them down and&nbsp;
did the same to them. If they wanted any chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:23.040
of freeing the Tentacled God, then they needed&nbsp;
to strike quickly and with overwhelming force.

00:33:23.040 --> 00:33:29.820
The SCP-2662 worshippers were able to secure the&nbsp;
addresses of the five key Foundation personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:29.820 --> 00:33:35.460
and station members outside each of them -&nbsp;
including one who could realistically imitate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:35.460 --> 00:33:41.580
each. They waited for night to fall, and broke&nbsp;
into each of their homes as they slept. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:41.580 --> 00:33:47.040
followed was a sequence of ruthless and efficient&nbsp;
murders done in the cause of freeing their god.

00:33:47.040 --> 00:33:52.200
Dr. Gutierrez was shot in the head while he&nbsp;
slept. Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:56.460
both stabbed to death before either even&nbsp;
realized what was happening. Thompson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:56.460 --> 00:34:01.620
who’d gotten up to use the bathroom, went&nbsp;
down in a hail of machine gun fire. Gillian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:01.620 --> 00:34:05.820
Larson had seen that masked figures were&nbsp;
breaking into her home and attempted to flee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:05.820 --> 00:34:11.100
but was caught and beaten to death by cultists&nbsp;
in her hallway. It was a strange irony that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:11.100 --> 00:34:15.240
people whose day jobs entailed working with&nbsp;
some of the most dangerous and nightmarish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:20.760
anomalies imaginable were murdered in their&nbsp;
homes by nothing more than regular humans.

00:34:21.720 --> 00:34:27.060
So far, Brother Marsh’s plan had gone&nbsp;
perfectly, with all five key personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:27.060 --> 00:34:31.920
murdered within a two minute period. Next,&nbsp;
the selected doppelgängers stole clothes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:31.920 --> 00:34:37.080
from their victims’ closets and were handed the&nbsp;
correct forged documentation. The next morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:37.080 --> 00:34:42.120
each replacement began their journeys to the&nbsp;
site where the Tentacled God was being contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:42.120 --> 00:34:47.100
while the rest of the cult armed themselves&nbsp;
in preparation for their own part in the plan.

00:34:47.760 --> 00:34:52.560
Nobody at the Foundation seemed to notice&nbsp;
anything amiss when the five arrived on site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:52.560 --> 00:34:57.300
When you work for the SCP Foundation, more&nbsp;
mental energy is devoted to following the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:57.300 --> 00:35:02.820
rules that keep you alive than to memorizing&nbsp;
the faces of all your co-workers and each one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:02.820 --> 00:35:08.640
slipped neatly into position, disappearing&nbsp;
into the familiarity of office life. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:13.500
infiltrating the site was one thing,&nbsp;
getting past the Belligerent Bodyguards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:13.500 --> 00:35:18.180
and into the cell of the Tentacled&nbsp;
God would be another thing entirely.

00:35:18.180 --> 00:35:23.580
That’s where the rest of the cult would come&nbsp;
into play. Heavily armed with whatever firearms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:23.580 --> 00:35:27.900
they could get their hands on, the rest of&nbsp;
the Devotees of the Tentacled God - Brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:27.900 --> 00:35:34.740
Marsh included - would attack the containment site&nbsp;
head-on. In the ensuing chaos, the five cultists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:34.740 --> 00:35:39.300
who had already infiltrated the site could take&nbsp;
advantage of the distraction, and break into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:39.300 --> 00:35:45.960
containment chamber. It was perfect. They’d launch&nbsp;
their attack from the outside… and from within.

00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:51.240
When Brother Marsh declared that the time&nbsp;
was right, the assault began. A legion of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:51.240 --> 00:35:55.560
gun-wielding cultists seemed to spring out of&nbsp;
nowhere and started shooting up the warehouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:55.560 --> 00:36:00.180
that was a front for the containment site.&nbsp;
The site quickly mobilized guards and task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:00.180 --> 00:36:05.760
force members to take on the sudden threat, and&nbsp;
just as Brother Marsh had anticipated, the Site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:11.040
Director called on the majority of TAU-9 to help&nbsp;
repel the violent cultists from their perimeter.

00:36:11.040 --> 00:36:17.460
TAU-9 obeyed, leaving three task force&nbsp;
members behind to guard SCP - 2662’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:17.460 --> 00:36:21.540
containment chamber. They expected to&nbsp;
be guarding the cell from rampaging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:21.540 --> 00:36:25.500
religious zealots seeking an audience&nbsp;
with their god. What they didn’t expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:25.500 --> 00:36:30.780
was a group of five Foundation employees&nbsp;
walking right up to them and opening fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:30.780 --> 00:36:37.380
killing two TAU-9 members and taking the third as&nbsp;
a hostage. While the war was being waged outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:37.380 --> 00:36:42.900
the infiltrators had found the Tentacled God’s&nbsp;
containment cell in the low-risk humanoid ward.

00:36:42.900 --> 00:36:47.700
Their hostage insisted that using him&nbsp;
wouldn’t give them any leverage - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:47.700 --> 00:36:50.940
rest of his team would neutralize&nbsp;
the whole group, him included,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:50.940 --> 00:36:55.080
if that’s what it took to stop them.&nbsp;
The infiltrators explained that using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:55.080 --> 00:37:01.620
him as leverage was never their intention - he&nbsp;
wasn’t a hostage at all. He was a sacrifice.

00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:07.560
The cultists of the Tentacled God detonated&nbsp;
explosives, creating a hole in the wall and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:13.440
finally giving them access to their deity. They&nbsp;
climbed through and gazed upon him in awe. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:13.440 --> 00:37:21.720
stood SCP-2662, twice as tall as a regular man,&nbsp;
with ten huge tentacles emerging from its back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:26.400
In their months of envisioning this creature,&nbsp;
they’d pictured it sitting on a throne made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:26.400 --> 00:37:32.340
of thousands of human bones, ready to dictate&nbsp;
its commands to the obedient liberators. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:32.340 --> 00:37:37.860
they certainly didn’t expect was to see the&nbsp;
Tentacled God hunched over a computer screen.

00:37:37.860 --> 00:37:45.060
Still, gods work in mysterious ways, so they stuck&nbsp;
to the plan and began chanting. They pulled out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:45.060 --> 00:37:50.520
sacrificial dagger, and began sacrificing their&nbsp;
captured TAU-9 member. It was at this point that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:50.520 --> 00:37:57.240
SCP - 2662 turned and saw what they were doing&nbsp;
with a look of pure horror. He rose up from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:57.240 --> 00:38:02.280
computer, his headphones getting caught as he&nbsp;
did so. He told them to go away, that he didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:02.280 --> 00:38:07.380
want them here, and that them murdering people&nbsp;
in his bedroom like this was inconsiderate and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:07.380 --> 00:38:12.420
disgusting. The cultists became even more&nbsp;
confused - why wasn’t their god accepting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:12.420 --> 00:38:17.700
their offerings? What were they doing wrong?
They tried more chanting, and painting arcane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:23.040
symbols on the floor in blood, but this just&nbsp;
seemed to make the creature angrier. He told them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:23.040 --> 00:38:28.860
in a tone more fitting for a teenage boy than a&nbsp;
Lovecraftian God, to just leave him alone so he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:36.540
could play his video games. This was seriously&nbsp;
not cool! The cultists were baffled. They told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:36.540 --> 00:38:41.040
the Tentacled God they were there to free&nbsp;
him. He replied that he didn’t need saving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:41.700 --> 00:38:46.800
That crazy stalkers like them were why he turned&nbsp;
himself in to the Foundation in the first place!

00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:52.560
Before the cultist infiltrators could get another&nbsp;
word in, the remaining members of TAU-9 stormed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:52.560 --> 00:38:57.780
into the containment cell and gunned them down&nbsp;
with surgical precision. The war outside was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:57.780 --> 00:39:02.580
already over - Brother Marsh and the rest of&nbsp;
the cultists were all killed in the firefight.

00:39:02.580 --> 00:39:08.940
TAU-9 didn’t look the least bit surprised&nbsp;
upon entering 2662’s cell, this was a common&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:08.940 --> 00:39:14.400
occurrence unfortunately. They had to deal with&nbsp;
an attempted cult invasion every few months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:14.400 --> 00:39:20.400
because SCP-2662’s main anomalous&nbsp;
ability is inspiring violent cults&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:24.840
who relentlessly track down and worship&nbsp;
it with arcane and bloodthirsty rituals.

00:39:24.840 --> 00:39:32.520
The problem is, 2662 doesn’t do this consciously,&nbsp;
and definitely doesn’t like the results. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:37.500
why he’s under the voluntary care of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation who keeps him amused with video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:43.200
games and reading material while fending off the&nbsp;
deranged cults who try to invade and abduct him.

00:39:43.200 --> 00:39:48.840
Following the termination of The Devotees of the&nbsp;
Tentacled God, just one of many cults who’d broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:48.840 --> 00:39:54.240
into 2662’s containment cell, the remaining&nbsp;
TAU-9 members apologized to the tentacled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:59.400
creature for the disturbance, allowing him to&nbsp;
return to his gaming. They assured him that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:59.400 --> 00:40:03.240
it’d probably be at least a few more months&nbsp;
before something like this happened again.

00:40:03.240 --> 00:40:08.280
SCP-2662’s cell was repaired,&nbsp;
and the Foundation returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:08.280 --> 00:40:13.740
to its task of seeking out would-be cultist&nbsp;
emancipators, because for the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:13.740 --> 00:40:19.620
it’s not always about the anomaly that’s being&nbsp;
kept in containment, but what’s being kept out.

00:40:19.620 --> 00:40:25.680
Mobile Task Force Edna-84, also known by&nbsp;
the code name “And Thus Upon His Crucible”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:25.680 --> 00:40:30.780
is on one of the strangest missions they’ve&nbsp;
ever been sent on. They sit in a darkened room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:30.780 --> 00:40:34.800
beads of sweat trickling down&nbsp;
their brows. The lights of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:34.800 --> 00:40:39.240
computer monitors shine up into their&nbsp;
faces. They’re tackling a monster that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:39.240 --> 00:40:46.860
if it escapes, will literally devour all of&nbsp;
creation. It has no fear, it has no remorse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:46.860 --> 00:40:53.100
and if it isn’t kept contained by Edna-84, it&nbsp;
may escape and wreak havoc across the world.

00:40:53.100 --> 00:40:56.760
Oh, and did we mention it’s&nbsp;
trapped inside a Minecraft server?

00:40:56.760 --> 00:41:03.240
You heard us right: SCP-4335 is a&nbsp;
cognitohazardous, extradimensional being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:03.240 --> 00:41:09.000
of pure terror, trapped inside a procedurally&nbsp;
generated world in the immensely popular game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:15.060
Minecraft. You hear about a lot of horrifying&nbsp;
monsters being described as Lovecraftian, but only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:15.060 --> 00:41:21.480
this monster is Minecraftian. There’s a lot that&nbsp;
needs explaining here, and we intend to get to all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:21.480 --> 00:41:26.820
of it, but let’s start with how the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps this truly exceptional beast contained.

00:41:26.820 --> 00:41:33.900
The Foundation first discovered SCP-4335 back&nbsp;
in 2010, shortly after the Alpha Version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:33.900 --> 00:41:37.440
Minecraft was released. Because&nbsp;
of the online nature of the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:37.440 --> 00:41:43.860
it’s proven to be impossible to contain 4335&nbsp;
externally, seeing as it isn’t confined to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:43.860 --> 00:41:50.040
any one physical location. Shutting off the&nbsp;
server 4335 is found in is not an effective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:50.040 --> 00:41:55.380
containment method either, as this just causes&nbsp;
the entity to simply hop to a different server.

00:41:55.380 --> 00:42:00.720
The Foundation’s greatest fear is that 4335&nbsp;
will one day make the leap out of Minecraft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:06.420
and cause chaos in our world. That’s why it’s&nbsp;
imperative to draft Containment Procedures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:06.420 --> 00:42:13.620
for SCP-4335 within the game. This led to the&nbsp;
creation of a containment site unlike any other:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:13.620 --> 00:42:20.820
Site-M1, the first official Foundation Site made&nbsp;
entirely out of Minecraft blocks. Everyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:20.820 --> 00:42:26.700
was originally involved in the server has been&nbsp;
removed and amnesthetized. Since then, elite SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:26.700 --> 00:42:33.960
Foundation Containment Specialists and Gamers have&nbsp;
been constructing the perfect prison for SCP-4335.

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:39.840
Site-M1 is a large, stone complex built into&nbsp;
the side of a mountain. It has a number of key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:39.840 --> 00:42:46.260
features - including a supply area filled with&nbsp;
materials vital for 4335’s continued containment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:46.260 --> 00:42:53.100
Chests filled with books that contain SCP-4335's&nbsp;
containment procedures. A few animal farms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:57.540
for the purpose of breeding and killing&nbsp;
livestock for their meat. The entrance to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:57.540 --> 00:43:03.000
mine. Several chests containing books specifically&nbsp;
designed for civilians to learn about 4335,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:07.320
if they ever breach containment and&nbsp;
enter the server. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:07.320 --> 00:43:14.940
the actual containment chamber for SCP-4335&nbsp;
itself, which is a little more complicated.

00:43:14.940 --> 00:43:21.240
4335’s containment chamber is built out of&nbsp;
several layers, all made from iron blocks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:21.240 --> 00:43:30.240
The outermost cube is 75 x 75 x 75 blocks,&nbsp;
the inner cube is 55 x 55 x 55 blocks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:30.240 --> 00:43:37.920
and the innermost cube is 25 x 25 x 25 blocks,&nbsp;
creating several levels of defense. Finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:44.340
one layer within all these others, which contains&nbsp;
the anomaly proper, is made from obsidian blocks.

00:43:44.340 --> 00:43:49.020
SCP-4335 is bound into the center&nbsp;
of the containment chamber with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:49.020 --> 00:43:52.860
a complex mechanism. The outermost&nbsp;
cube is completely filled with water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:52.860 --> 00:43:57.420
and several dispensers capable of rapidly&nbsp;
dispensing large amounts of items in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:01.860
short amount of time line the cube. The&nbsp;
cube also contains several mob farms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:01.860 --> 00:44:07.020
which are devices that constantly spawn enemies&nbsp;
into the chamber that drop loot when they die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:07.020 --> 00:44:14.340
The chamber is essentially designed to funnel&nbsp;
a constant flow of items inwards to SCP-4335.

00:44:14.340 --> 00:44:21.120
There are even contingency measures for if&nbsp;
SCP-4335 manages to breach containment. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:26.820
escape is attempted, blocks of TNT detonate&nbsp;
above the ceiling, causing lava to pour into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:26.820 --> 00:44:33.120
the chamber. At that point, MTF Edna-84 are&nbsp;
dispatched into the server to lure 4335 back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:33.120 --> 00:44:38.340
into its containment chamber. To do this, they&nbsp;
use a mix of fire-resistance potions and Ender&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:43.740
Pearls - which have teleportation capabilities.&nbsp;
Interestingly, there’s one more basic method of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:43.740 --> 00:44:52.500
luring SCP-4335 back into the obsidian cube:&nbsp;
Taunting and insulting. One of SCP-4335’s many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:52.500 --> 00:44:57.660
anomalous abilities is being able to hear&nbsp;
people through the screen, and - being a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:57.660 --> 00:45:03.600
proud creature - it often responds to insults&nbsp;
by charging in to directly engage the insulter.

00:45:03.600 --> 00:45:08.820
If SCP-4335 still manages to breach the&nbsp;
containment that has been set up for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:08.820 --> 00:45:13.860
then they expect that it will likely soon&nbsp;
hop into another server. At that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:13.860 --> 00:45:17.460
the goal will shift to finding&nbsp;
the monster and recontaining it.

00:45:17.460 --> 00:45:22.620
With Containment Procedures this complex and&nbsp;
extensive, it shouldn’t come as a surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:22.620 --> 00:45:30.600
that SCP-4335 rests firmly in the Keter Class.&nbsp;
What exactly is this anomalous entity? Why does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:34.860
its containment hinge on constantly&nbsp;
providing it with items? And how did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:38.940
it end up in Mojang’s popular building&nbsp;
and survival game in the first place?

00:45:38.940 --> 00:45:45.840
SCP-4335, in terms of physical dimensions,&nbsp;
appears almost identical to the player character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:51.120
with an all-black skin. It also appears&nbsp;
to be constantly shrouded in a cloud of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:51.120 --> 00:45:56.700
smoke particles, and has long, black tendrils&nbsp;
protruding from its back. In some respects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:56.700 --> 00:46:01.200
4335 has been compared to two&nbsp;
popular creepypasta figures:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:01.200 --> 00:46:08.580
Herobrine and The Slenderman. But 4335 is far&nbsp;
stranger. Its physical body behaves similarly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:08.580 --> 00:46:15.240
to most assets native to the game, with a few&nbsp;
peculiar anomalous abilities we’ll discuss soon.

00:46:15.240 --> 00:46:22.020
Handling SCP-4335 is an extremely delicate&nbsp;
process. If command blocks, creative mode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:22.020 --> 00:46:28.860
or server commands are ever enabled in a server&nbsp;
with SCP-4335, the server will instantly shut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:28.860 --> 00:46:37.020
down, and SCP-4335 will move to a different&nbsp;
server. SCP-4335 also uses its tendrils to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:37.020 --> 00:46:44.640
destroy surrounding blocks before consuming them.&nbsp;
With each successful consumption, SCP-4335 grows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:52.500
and when it reaches sufficient size, it hops to a&nbsp;
different server. As you can see, keeping SCP-4335&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:52.500 --> 00:46:57.900
contained is an uphill battle, but luckily there&nbsp;
are two factors on the Foundation’s side here.

00:46:57.900 --> 00:47:03.840
The first is that SCP-4335 is immobilized&nbsp;
while consuming items and blocks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:08.820
limiting its ability to actively escape&nbsp;
Foundation forces. The second factor is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:08.820 --> 00:47:14.880
that SCP-4335 needs a rest period between&nbsp;
consuming blocks in order to grow, meaning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:14.880 --> 00:47:21.240
if its consumption is constant and continuous&nbsp;
it isn’t able to grow. These two factors have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:21.240 --> 00:47:26.640
informed the entirety of the Foundation’s&nbsp;
Containment Procedures around SCP-4335:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:26.640 --> 00:47:30.900
It’s locked into its chamber and&nbsp;
fed items and blocks constantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:30.900 --> 00:47:38.100
effectively rooting it in place. When SCP-4335&nbsp;
begins to grow, the Foundation also found that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:38.100 --> 00:47:42.240
the application of Ender Pearls helps&nbsp;
reduce it back to its normal size.

00:47:42.240 --> 00:47:51.180
However, SCP-4335 does have a method of striking&nbsp;
back against its captors. 4335 is Vurgent-class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:51.180 --> 00:47:56.700
multi-sensory cognitohazard. Anyone viewing&nbsp;
it without proper training and protection may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:56.700 --> 00:48:04.320
experience distressing hallucinations. SCP-4335&nbsp;
is also capable of telepathic speech with people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:04.320 --> 00:48:10.380
playing on its server, and - as we alluded to&nbsp;
earlier - it can also hear any noises you make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:10.380 --> 00:48:16.440
while playing. “Weird” is a term thrown around a&nbsp;
lot when it comes to SCPs, considering it’s pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:21.060
much a requirement for the Foundation to take&nbsp;
interest in you. But an all-devouring Minecraft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:21.060 --> 00:48:27.240
demon that can hear you talking through your&nbsp;
screen is strange even by Foundation standards.

00:48:27.240 --> 00:48:33.780
MTF Edna-84 first discovered SCP-4335 in&nbsp;
the single-player server of Minecraft user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:33.780 --> 00:48:38.040
Leakingheart. Three team members&nbsp;
- Jason Yelsan, Richard Duchamp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:38.040 --> 00:48:43.440
and Sheila Freemason - covertly entered the game&nbsp;
to investigate and potentially apprehend the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:43.440 --> 00:48:48.000
creature. When Leakingheart first discovered their&nbsp;
presence on what he thought was a private server,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:52.800
he quickly left, a little creeped out&nbsp;
by the sudden intrusion. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:59.520
the trio was still able to locate SCP-4335. They&nbsp;
discovered the creature hiding inside a giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:59.520 --> 00:49:03.600
crater, as though it had impacted&nbsp;
the earth at considerable speed.

00:49:03.600 --> 00:49:06.840
Richard Duchamp, who was the&nbsp;
leader of the team at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:06.840 --> 00:49:12.000
made the mistake of looking directly at the&nbsp;
entity. In that moment, he experienced the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:12.000 --> 00:49:19.200
full force of SCP-4335’s cognitohazardous effects.&nbsp;
He hallucinated, believing that his keyboard was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:19.200 --> 00:49:24.840
melting before his eyes. In the aftermath of&nbsp;
this incident, Duchamp was taken off the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:24.840 --> 00:49:31.740
and Jason Yelsan was promoted to head of the&nbsp;
project. Things were still going to get stranger.

00:49:31.740 --> 00:49:36.360
Yelsan was able to open a dialogue with the&nbsp;
creature after containing it in a chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:36.360 --> 00:49:41.340
filled with lava. It asked him whether it&nbsp;
had landed in the right location - meaning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:41.340 --> 00:49:46.260
our world - and Yelsan informed it that it’d&nbsp;
somehow fallen into the world of Minecraft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:46.260 --> 00:49:52.500
instead. The creature was at first confused, and&nbsp;
then angry and resentful about its situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:52.500 --> 00:49:58.140
It vowed to find its way into our world&nbsp;
somehow, and obtain more “sustenance.”

00:49:58.140 --> 00:50:02.940
A few months after this, the entity managed&nbsp;
to breach containment and hop into another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:02.940 --> 00:50:07.740
server. Yelsan and two others once again&nbsp;
managed to track it down and recontain it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:07.740 --> 00:50:12.240
but this time, two civilians also&nbsp;
inhabiting the server were exposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:12.240 --> 00:50:18.780
to the anomalous effects of SCP-4335. They&nbsp;
weren’t hurt, but they did appear strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:18.780 --> 00:50:24.780
and incoherent after experiencing 4335’s&nbsp;
cognitohazards. The Foundation tracked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:24.780 --> 00:50:31.500
them down in the aftermath and gave them amnestic&nbsp;
treatment. 4335 was contained shortly thereafter.

00:50:31.500 --> 00:50:37.260
Once again, Yelsan came face to face with his&nbsp;
new foe. Eight months after being captured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:37.260 --> 00:50:44.280
4335 granted Yelsan another interview from&nbsp;
containment. 4335 admitted that it almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:44.280 --> 00:50:49.500
respected Yelsan and the rest of the Foundation&nbsp;
for figuring out how to capture and contain it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:54.480
so quickly. In exchange, it would give the&nbsp;
Foundation something extremely valuable:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:54.480 --> 00:51:01.140
Information. First, it asked one question&nbsp;
of Yelsan: How does he define “creation?”

00:51:01.140 --> 00:51:06.300
Yelsan replied, “Uh… something that is&nbsp;
built and brought to this universe by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:06.300 --> 00:51:09.420
a sapient being, using other&nbsp;
things from this universe?”

00:51:09.420 --> 00:51:16.620
4335 agreed. It went on to explain that it&nbsp;
came from a universe devoid of creation. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:16.620 --> 00:51:23.160
dark and unknowable place, filled with nothing&nbsp;
but violent, random chaos. Its dimension existed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:23.160 --> 00:51:27.780
directly above ours, and it often looked&nbsp;
down at us through a dimensional window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:27.780 --> 00:51:34.620
fascinated by all the creation below. It plotted&nbsp;
and dreamed to one day infiltrate our reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:34.620 --> 00:51:40.080
and Yelsan finally had the opportunity&nbsp;
to ask the magic question, “Why?”

00:51:40.080 --> 00:51:47.340
Though he wasn’t quite ready for the&nbsp;
brutal honesty of SCP-4335’s reply.&nbsp;

00:51:47.340 --> 00:51:54.600
“I do not like to lie, so I will tell you&nbsp;
now. I wish to suck it dry of the toys of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:54.600 --> 00:52:00.960
whatever force controls your universe.&nbsp;
Destroy the light, destroy the Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:10.260
and destroy humanity. It reminded me… of&nbsp;
me. A blubbering mass of intelligence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:10.260 --> 00:52:16.500
order. It sickens me in ways I cannot&nbsp;
comprehend. I hope you understand.”

00:52:16.500 --> 00:52:25.260
SCP-4335 was a connoisseur of creation, and&nbsp;
it sought to devour all of it. In this moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:25.260 --> 00:52:31.080
Yelsan realized what an incredibly dangerous&nbsp;
entity he was dealing with. The only mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:36.540
was why this creature had somehow landed&nbsp;
in Minecraft instead of our world, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:36.540 --> 00:52:43.560
appeared to be the only thing that saved us. But&nbsp;
Yelsan didn’t have time to think: 4335 was about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:43.560 --> 00:52:48.540
to stage another daring escape attempt. One of&nbsp;
its tendrils reached out and attacked Yelsan’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:48.540 --> 00:52:53.520
player character. In that moment, the real&nbsp;
life Yelsan began to hallucinate and panic.

00:52:53.520 --> 00:52:59.820
Suddenly, back in the game, a series of abnormally&nbsp;
tall, slender black figures appeared and began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:59.820 --> 00:53:06.900
deconstructing the containment chamber around&nbsp;
SCP-4335. It had somehow summoned new minions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:06.900 --> 00:53:12.120
into the game to assist in this containment&nbsp;
breach. Jason Yelsan entered cognitohazard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:16.620
quarantine following this incident, and&nbsp;
was removed from the project. And he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:16.620 --> 00:53:21.420
wasn’t the only one affected by this incident.&nbsp;
Following the first appearance of these long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:21.420 --> 00:53:27.540
dark figures, players across the globe began to&nbsp;
experience them appearing in their own games.

00:53:27.540 --> 00:53:32.640
The Foundation managed to find a solution:&nbsp;
They contacted Mojang and had the creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:32.640 --> 00:53:37.200
patched into the game during the next&nbsp;
update, as a new non-anomalous entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:37.200 --> 00:53:43.260
which seemed to stop 4335 from being able&nbsp;
to use them as its own tools. They’re now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:43.260 --> 00:53:48.480
known as the Endermen, and are beloved among&nbsp;
fans for being one of the creepier enemies.

00:53:48.480 --> 00:53:56.100
To this day, containment efforts continue&nbsp;
for SCP-4335. There’s only one question left:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:56.100 --> 00:54:01.440
Why did the entity fall into Minecraft&nbsp;
rather than our world? The file posits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:01.440 --> 00:54:08.700
the most likely answer. Because 4335 defines&nbsp;
creation as elements made by sapient beings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:08.700 --> 00:54:14.220
In Minecraft, the most popular game in&nbsp;
the world at the height of 4335’s power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:14.220 --> 00:54:21.060
everything that exists is the product of code&nbsp;
made by humans. Creation is truly abundant there.

00:54:21.060 --> 00:54:30.120
As for our world, in SCP-4335’s extra-dimensional&nbsp;
eyes, there is no creation, no intelligent design,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:35.040
no soothing piano soundtrack. Just&nbsp;
frightening, chaotic, randomness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:35.040 --> 00:54:42.360
which is too unlike its own dimension. So even&nbsp;
if SCP-4335 ever did arrive in our reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:42.360 --> 00:54:46.620
it would likely be disappointed&nbsp;
by how little there is to eat.

00:54:46.620 --> 00:54:51.240
The fabric of our world is littered with&nbsp;
strange doorways if you know where to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:51.240 --> 00:54:58.440
for them. Tears, portals, anomalies, all&nbsp;
leading to places and planes beyond human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:58.440 --> 00:55:04.980
imagining and understanding, and SCP-2317,&nbsp;
otherwise known as A Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:04.980 --> 00:55:10.740
certainly fits that description. Contained and&nbsp;
kept at all times under the watch of armed guards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:18.000
SCP-2317 appears to be a simple and unsuspecting&nbsp;
wooden door in its frame. It hardly looks like it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:23.400
requires such extreme round-the-clock security&nbsp;
or needs a strange, secretive ritual that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:23.400 --> 00:55:29.640
Foundation performs, presumably to keep the&nbsp;
door closed. But, of course, sometimes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:29.640 --> 00:55:34.920
most interesting thing about a closed doorway&nbsp;
isn’t where it leads, it’s what it keeps out.&nbsp;

00:55:35.940 --> 00:55:41.640
Even by the Foundation’s already-high standards,&nbsp;
the requirements and regulations for personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:41.640 --> 00:55:48.600
who are assigned to SCP-2317 seem oddly specific.&nbsp;
Psychological testing is standard practice for to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:48.600 --> 00:55:53.220
work for the Foundation, but an additional&nbsp;
hurdle that anyone has to clear before even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:53.220 --> 00:55:58.020
getting to glimpse at this unassuming wooden&nbsp;
door is having a score of at least seventy-two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:58.020 --> 00:56:04.080
on the Milgram Obedience Examination. It is also&nbsp;
mandatory that personnel assigned to maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:04.080 --> 00:56:09.240
it are both unmarried, with no children&nbsp;
or next-of-kin, as well as an unwavering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:09.240 --> 00:56:15.000
unquestioning loyalty to the Foundation,&nbsp;
pure devotion to its code and objectives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:15.720 --> 00:56:22.860
These may seem like strange requirements,&nbsp;
after all, SCP-2317 is just a door…isn’t it?&nbsp;

00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:29.160
Perhaps there’s a reason that the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps so much of the information about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:29.160 --> 00:56:35.040
buried deep under layers upon layers of security,&nbsp;
with only the Overseer Council privy to the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:35.040 --> 00:56:42.420
details of its strange nature. Knowledge, as they&nbsp;
say, is power - but maybe knowing too much about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:42.420 --> 00:56:49.740
whatever is behind that door can prove deadly.&nbsp;
Still, if SCP-2317 is a Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:49.740 --> 00:56:55.620
an alternate dimension or parallel reality,&nbsp;
it must be safe enough to visit. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:55.620 --> 00:57:00.420
the Foundation has been sending personnel&nbsp;
in there on a regular basis. Daily, in fact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:01.440 --> 00:57:06.840
According to the O5 Council, this is done as part&nbsp;
of a procedure to maintain Active Containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:07.860 --> 00:57:11.400
of…something lurking beyond&nbsp;
that old wooden doorframe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:12.060 --> 00:57:15.540
But what could possibly warrant such&nbsp;
constant maintenance and surveillance?&nbsp;

00:57:17.100 --> 00:57:21.960
In accordance with the Foundation’s guidelines,&nbsp;
all staff are required to rotate out of observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:21.960 --> 00:57:27.840
SCP-2317 after every two months and spend the&nbsp;
following third month in full psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:27.840 --> 00:57:32.040
counselling before they are permitted to&nbsp;
return to the containment unit housing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:32.040 --> 00:57:37.200
Door to Another World. It was after one of&nbsp;
these month-long periods of evaluation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:37.200 --> 00:57:42.840
a Foundation guard was informed that his security&nbsp;
clearance had been raised to Level 3 and that he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:42.840 --> 00:57:47.820
been selected for the duty of carrying out&nbsp;
220-Calabasas. He knew the name instantly;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:47.820 --> 00:57:53.520
this was the title given to the daily containment&nbsp;
procedure that absolutely had to be carried out.&nbsp;

00:57:54.600 --> 00:57:59.040
The guard didn’t question these orders, after&nbsp;
all, he’d been selected precisely because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:59.040 --> 00:58:03.960
his loyalty to the Foundation. He did make one&nbsp;
request to his commanding officer, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:04.620 --> 00:58:08.280
he wanted to know what had happened to the&nbsp;
last guard that had performed the procedure.&nbsp;

00:58:09.240 --> 00:58:13.320
“Didn’t make it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation,” the officer replied.&nbsp;

00:58:14.340 --> 00:58:19.740
Not letting this affect his dedication, the guard&nbsp;
was told to prepare for Procedure 220-Calabasas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:20.400 --> 00:58:25.560
Along with a fellow member of Foundation security&nbsp;
personnel, the guard was instructed to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:25.560 --> 00:58:31.440
everything on a strange list. The first was&nbsp;
a pre-selected member of Class-D Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:31.440 --> 00:58:36.540
specifically a convicted murderer. Class-D&nbsp;
refers to ‘Disposable Class’ personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:36.540 --> 00:58:42.060
expendable individuals recruited by the&nbsp;
Foundation for the sole purpose of testing SCPs.&nbsp;

00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:48.240
Class-Ds were usually prison inmates&nbsp;
repurposed for SCP testing, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:48.240 --> 00:58:53.820
one chosen for 220-Calabasas was no exception,&nbsp;
serving multiple life sentences for murders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:53.820 --> 00:58:57.840
or at least that was what the guard&nbsp;
had been told. A Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:57.840 --> 00:59:02.100
member instructed him to refer to the Class-D&nbsp;
solely as the ‘assistant’ from that point on.&nbsp;

00:59:02.760 --> 00:59:06.840
Next, the guard collected a live&nbsp;
chicken, an obsidian-edged knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:06.840 --> 00:59:12.720
a silver aspergillum and aspersorium, to be&nbsp;
filled with 500ccs of Holy Water that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:12.720 --> 00:59:19.020
been blessed by a priest of the Abrahamic faith,&nbsp;
and finally a one-kiloton nuclear device, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:19.020 --> 00:59:23.220
according to instructions, was to only&nbsp;
be detonated in the unlikely event of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:23.220 --> 00:59:27.000
catastrophic containment failure.&nbsp;
In other words, the last resort.&nbsp;

00:59:28.560 --> 00:59:33.660
After following his instructions to the letter and&nbsp;
without question, the guard and his colleague were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:33.660 --> 00:59:38.280
briefed. The Foundation personnel member informed&nbsp;
them that he’d be joining and leading them in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:38.280 --> 00:59:43.620
procedure. The staff member also specified that&nbsp;
henceforth he be referred to as the ‘celebrant’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:43.620 --> 00:59:49.200
until the completion of 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
guard was acutely aware of how specific these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:49.200 --> 00:59:54.120
instructions were, but trusted in the Foundation,&nbsp;
knowing that if they wanted this procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:54.120 --> 00:59:58.980
performed a certain way, then it was in everyones’&nbsp;
best interest to carry out the orders to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:58.980 --> 01:00:05.880
letter. But what the celebrant then went on to&nbsp;
explain, raised far more questions about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:05.880 --> 01:00:14.100
and the nature of Procedure 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
Class-D joining them, wasn’t actually a Class-D.&nbsp;

01:00:14.700 --> 01:00:19.500
The assistant, as they were now referred to,&nbsp;
was in reality another Foundation staff member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:19.500 --> 01:00:24.660
with a Level 4 security clearance,&nbsp;
specifically tailored to SCP-2317.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:25.620 --> 01:00:32.400
Every member of staff entering through SCP-2317&nbsp;
and taking an active role in 220-Calabasas needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:32.400 --> 01:00:37.080
to be informed that this assistant was not to be&nbsp;
harmed or treated as a member of Disposable Class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:42.960
Fighting back the nagging question of why&nbsp;
the Foundation would employ this subterfuge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:42.960 --> 01:00:47.100
the guard, along with his fellow security&nbsp;
officer, the celebrant and assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:47.100 --> 01:00:51.240
prepared for their departure through&nbsp;
the Door to Another World at solar noon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:51.240 --> 01:00:58.560
when the sun was highest over SCP-2317.&nbsp;
Solar noon, chickens and holy water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:59.400 --> 01:01:02.880
this all seemed like an oddly-occult&nbsp;
combination for the Foundation.&nbsp;

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:08.520
As they entered the old wooden door, beyond&nbsp;
lay a barren salt plane, stretching out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:08.520 --> 01:01:13.920
kilometers in every direction. This alternate&nbsp;
dimension, according to the briefing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:13.920 --> 01:01:20.100
was designated SCP-2317-Prime. The guard&nbsp;
immediately noticed a ring of seven pillars&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:20.100 --> 01:01:25.320
directly ahead of the group as they entered, each&nbsp;
of them bearing intricately-detailed engravings&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:25.320 --> 01:01:31.980
unlike anything from any era of ancient history.
Procedure 220-Calabasas was carried out quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:37.260
but carefully, the guard watching as the celebrant&nbsp;
and assistant were careful not to miss a step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:38.280 --> 01:01:41.820
First, the celebrant scattered Holy Water&nbsp;
into the center of the pillars with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:41.820 --> 01:01:47.040
aspergillum and aspersorium, looking down&nbsp;
at his feet and keeping a steady pace as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:47.040 --> 01:01:52.320
stepped counter-clockwise around them. The guard&nbsp;
watched intently as the celebrant completed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:52.320 --> 01:01:57.360
circuit around the pillars and turned to the&nbsp;
assistant, anointing his head with Holy Water.&nbsp;

01:01:58.020 --> 01:02:04.920
“Seven Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones&nbsp;
for the Scarlet King,” he said aloud.&nbsp;

01:02:05.760 --> 01:02:09.900
The assistant, with the obsidian blade in&nbsp;
his hand, took the chicken and dispatched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:09.900 --> 01:02:15.660
in sacrifice, letting its blood mix with the&nbsp;
Holy Water. He then repeated the celebrant’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:15.660 --> 01:02:19.620
circuit in the opposite direction, before&nbsp;
stepping into the center of the stone pillars.&nbsp;

01:02:20.520 --> 01:02:26.820
“Blood for the Old Gods, Water for the New King,”&nbsp;
the assistant recited, pouring the remaining mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:26.820 --> 01:02:30.960
of blood and Holy Water over a patch of&nbsp;
salt in the middle of the seven pillars.&nbsp;

01:02:31.800 --> 01:02:36.840
Even though he knew it wasn’t his place to&nbsp;
question the Foundation, as the 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:36.840 --> 01:02:41.700
procedure took place, the guard couldn’t&nbsp;
help but wonder what all this was for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:42.300 --> 01:02:49.140
It seemed so…ritualistic, like something&nbsp;
deeply religious or even magical. He’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:49.140 --> 01:02:52.980
bought into all that occult mumbo-jumbo,&nbsp;
even while working for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:52.980 --> 01:02:59.400
but he had learned not to question anything, even&nbsp;
the strangest and most inexplicable of sights.&nbsp;

01:03:00.360 --> 01:03:07.980
Little did he know that beneath his feet, was an&nbsp;
ancient and unknowable horror. A beast, chained&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:07.980 --> 01:03:13.980
and lying in wait. Contained in a chamber directly&nbsp;
underneath the pillars, sat an impossibly-large&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:13.980 --> 01:03:19.980
creature. Humanoid and obese, its body covered&nbsp;
entirely in scales thicker than armour plating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:20.520 --> 01:03:25.680
Branch-like horns protruded from its jawless&nbsp;
head, pointing up to chains that hung from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:25.680 --> 01:03:32.460
seven pillars above, each one hooked into the&nbsp;
entity’s back. All but one of the chains was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:32.460 --> 01:03:38.460
broken, a final, withering shackle keeping the&nbsp;
Devourer of Worlds in its underground prison.&nbsp;

01:03:39.300 --> 01:03:45.780
Ever since 1894 BCE, when Erikeshan mystics&nbsp;
imprisoned it, the Devourer has been waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:45.780 --> 01:03:51.360
patiently for its inevitable freedom. It knows,&nbsp;
as well as the Foundation, that nothing can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:51.360 --> 01:03:57.420
done to prevent the final chain from one day&nbsp;
breaking. Even Procedure 220-Calabasas won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:57.420 --> 01:04:03.420
keep the creature contained, it’s nothing more&nbsp;
than a smokescreen, an act, designed to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:03.420 --> 01:04:09.120
an illusion of active containment and maintain&nbsp;
Foundation morale until a permanent solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:09.120 --> 01:04:17.940
can be devised to keep SCP-2317 imprisoned.
Of course, if the guard had known this, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:17.940 --> 01:04:22.500
have also explained the need for a one-kiloton&nbsp;
nuclear device as part of this staged ritual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:23.100 --> 01:04:28.620
Procedure 220-Calabasas has all the components&nbsp;
to trick everyone below the O5 Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:28.620 --> 01:04:33.720
emulating religious and occult rituals, the&nbsp;
increased level of security surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:33.720 --> 01:04:39.480
procedure and its purpose, and telling staff&nbsp;
that any failure to correctly, and completely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:39.480 --> 01:04:46.500
perform the 220-Calabasas procedure will result&nbsp;
in an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:47.460 --> 01:04:52.680
All these elements work together to conceal&nbsp;
the truth: that one day, the Devourer will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:59.520
escape and lay waste to our dimension.
Knowledge is power, and maybe knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:59.520 --> 01:05:05.220
too much truly is deadly. Perhaps if the guard&nbsp;
had learned any of this, he’d have understood&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:05.220 --> 01:05:10.140
why his predecessor never made it out of&nbsp;
psychological evaluation. Maybe if he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:10.140 --> 01:05:16.140
questioned the purpose of Procedure 220-Calabasas,&nbsp;
he'd have learned the true nature of SCP-2317,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:17.100 --> 01:05:23.100
and what that doorway kept out. But he was&nbsp;
loyal to the Foundation, through and through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:23.880 --> 01:05:29.220
As the team finished performing 220-Calabasas&nbsp;
and returned though the wooden door, the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:29.220 --> 01:05:36.120
took one last glance over his shoulder at the vast&nbsp;
salt plane. The entire dimension was calm, silent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:36.780 --> 01:05:42.600
but not peaceful: it was patient. The&nbsp;
entity had waited centuries for its time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:42.600 --> 01:05:48.480
and now all it would take was the breaking&nbsp;
of the seventh and final chain. One day.&nbsp;

01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:52.140
The door was closed behind the guard as he,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:52.140 --> 01:05:56.760
the celebrant, the assistant and his fellow&nbsp;
security officer stepped back through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:57.840 --> 01:06:03.240
their work done and, as far as they knew,&nbsp;
preventing catastrophe for another day.&nbsp;

01:06:04.200 --> 01:06:09.480
Only the Foundation higher-ups, the Overseer&nbsp;
Council, are aware of the true danger posed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:09.480 --> 01:06:16.560
by SCP-2317 and its sole inhabitant. Current&nbsp;
predictions are that at some point within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:16.560 --> 01:06:22.680
next thirty years, the Devourer of Worlds will&nbsp;
be freed. Any and all attempts to repair or&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:22.680 --> 01:06:29.340
recreate the chains holding it in place have so&nbsp;
far failed. As such, the O5 Council has elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:29.340 --> 01:06:35.160
to continue providing Foundation personnel with&nbsp;
the ignorant hope that Procedure 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:35.160 --> 01:06:41.880
is an effective strategy for containment.
As we’ve said, sometimes the most interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:41.880 --> 01:06:48.960
thing about a closed door isn’t where it leads,&nbsp;
it’s what it keeps out. In the case of SCP-2317,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:48.960 --> 01:06:53.820
the unassuming wooden door holds at bay&nbsp;
an ancient creature of untold power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:54.540 --> 01:07:01.020
that will one day break free and wreak havoc in&nbsp;
our dimension. Nothing the Foundation does can&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:01.020 --> 01:07:06.720
prevent it, or keep it contained behind the&nbsp;
Door to Another World, and only the Overseer&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:06.720 --> 01:07:12.840
Council knows that any and all efforts to&nbsp;
do so are futile. With all that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:12.840 --> 01:07:21.000
we can only hope that the doorway of SCP-2317&nbsp;
stays closed, at least for a little while longer.

01:07:21.780 --> 01:07:28.680
It was November 20th, 2019, and the helicopter&nbsp;
circled far above in the freezing wind of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:28.680 --> 01:07:33.660
Antarctic. SCP Foundation Site Director&nbsp;
Jason Monroe looked down at the isolated&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:33.660 --> 01:07:39.420
above-ground facilities of Provisional&nbsp;
Site-344-1. Something about this place&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:39.420 --> 01:07:46.500
made him nervous. Edgy. And for good reason:&nbsp;
Between 2003 and 2019, twenty-nine Mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:46.500 --> 01:07:51.120
Task Force units and seventy-three members&nbsp;
of D-Class personnel had gone missing here&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:51.120 --> 01:07:56.220
and never been found. Monroe thought he&nbsp;
was here for a routine investigation into&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:56.220 --> 01:08:01.620
negligence and mismanagement, but little&nbsp;
did he know, he was in for so much more.

01:08:01.620 --> 01:08:09.840
This is the story of SCP - 5545, and one man’s&nbsp;
journey into his own worst nightmare. Literally.

01:08:09.840 --> 01:08:16.440
But this nightmare began a long time ago - 300&nbsp;
years, to be exact. And like most nightmares,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:16.440 --> 01:08:22.320
it started as a dream. That dream was one&nbsp;
of expansion - national powers across Europe&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:22.320 --> 01:08:26.340
wanted to be the first to conquer the&nbsp;
globe and expand into new territories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:26.340 --> 01:08:32.100
and sent countless exploratory missions off into&nbsp;
the unknown to achieve this goal. Any history&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:32.100 --> 01:08:36.960
book will tell you that the first outsiders to&nbsp;
lay eyes upon the continent of Antarctica did&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:36.960 --> 01:08:44.280
so in 1820 - the reality is that the first ones&nbsp;
to get there actually landed in the late 1700s.

01:08:44.280 --> 01:08:48.840
The hapless explorers ventured into&nbsp;
mainland Antarctica and made base camps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:48.840 --> 01:08:53.400
before searching and digging for any&nbsp;
useful resources nearby. They came&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:53.400 --> 01:08:59.640
upon a strange discovery: A hallway, hidden&nbsp;
beneath the ice. Not a passage in the ice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:59.640 --> 01:09:05.220
but a true hallway - complete with light&nbsp;
fixtures. The confused explorers ventured&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:05.220 --> 01:09:11.460
down into these impossible hallways, and for many&nbsp;
of them, it would be the last thing they ever did.

01:09:11.460 --> 01:09:17.520
No matter how long they walked, it seemed like&nbsp;
the hallways just kept going. As they continued to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:17.520 --> 01:09:23.760
walk for hours, they hoped they’d find something…&nbsp;
anything. And eventually, they did. They passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:23.760 --> 01:09:28.380
from these hallways into somewhere different&nbsp;
altogether, and most of them were never heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:28.380 --> 01:09:34.560
from again. Those who did manage to escape often&nbsp;
died or took their own lives soon after. Whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:39.240
it was they’d discovered down there, they&nbsp;
didn’t want to live with it on their minds.

01:09:39.240 --> 01:09:45.000
It’s believed that over seventy colonial explorers&nbsp;
disappeared or died this way and that most who&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:45.000 --> 01:09:50.640
found these endless hallways beneath the Antarctic&nbsp;
ice never returned. The multiple anomalous objects&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:50.640 --> 01:09:56.700
and phenomena that make up SCP-5545 came into&nbsp;
the Foundation’s hands several centuries later&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:56.700 --> 01:10:03.000
on September 8th, 2003, when during an&nbsp;
expedition into the Antarctic, they too&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:03.000 --> 01:10:08.400
found the endless hallways. The Foundation&nbsp;
built Provisional Site-344-1 around them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:08.400 --> 01:10:13.800
hoping to safely seal them off from any other&nbsp;
unwitting Antarctic explorers or researchers.

01:10:13.800 --> 01:10:19.380
But there was something else lurking beneath&nbsp;
the ice in Antarctica. Something dangerous. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:19.380 --> 01:10:25.800
hallways were designated as SCP - 5545 - 1 and&nbsp;
were thought to be the extent of the anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:25.800 --> 01:10:33.360
activity at the site, but soon SCP - 5455 - 2&nbsp;
was discovered, which resulted in the deaths of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:33.360 --> 01:10:41.220
sixteen researchers. So what exactly is 5545 - 2?&nbsp;
It’s an entity so volatile that even knowing about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:41.220 --> 01:10:48.240
it is considered to be a containment breach, and -&nbsp;
as a result - it’s kept in Provisional Site-344-2.

01:10:48.240 --> 01:10:56.580
Unlike Site - 344 - 1, 344 - 2 isn’t a physical&nbsp;
space. It’s conceptual, accessible only through&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:56.580 --> 01:11:04.380
the endless hallways, created with the express&nbsp;
purpose of keeping 5545 - 1 and 5545 - 2 separate.

01:11:04.380 --> 01:11:10.800
Why? Because whenever the two come&nbsp;
into contact, the result is 5545 - 3:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:10.800 --> 01:11:16.500
The network of endless hallways expanding. If&nbsp;
they remained in contact, the hallways would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:16.500 --> 01:11:20.700
continue to expand and the entire planet&nbsp;
could be filled with endless hallways in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:20.700 --> 01:11:26.700
just four to six hours. While the two&nbsp;
are apart though, 5545 - 3 reverses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:26.700 --> 01:11:33.000
but it always would take just a few hours to throw&nbsp;
the whole world into a chaos of infinite hallways.

01:11:33.000 --> 01:11:39.480
SCP-5455 has been given the classification&nbsp;
“Safe”… Wait, we’re dealing with a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:39.480 --> 01:11:44.940
and volatile anomaly that’s claimed a huge number&nbsp;
of lives and still somehow eludes true Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:44.940 --> 01:11:50.003
understanding, yet the official SCP Foundation&nbsp;
classification is “Safe?” How could this be?

01:11:50.003 --> 01:11:50.572
This same thought process brings us to 2018,&nbsp;
when Jason Monroe first took interest in SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:50.572 --> 01:11:55.620
- 5545. Monroe was the Director of Site -&nbsp;
58, and was the definition of no-nonsense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:55.620 --> 01:11:59.880
Prior to taking the Site Director position,&nbsp;
he was a decorated member of Mobile Task&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:59.880 --> 01:12:04.860
Force Eta-10 and helped contain numerous&nbsp;
Keter-Class anomalies. He’d been around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:04.860 --> 01:12:10.380
proverbial block when it came to anomalous&nbsp;
activity, and something about SCP - 5545,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:10.380 --> 01:12:17.160
and the management of Provisional Site 344, seemed&nbsp;
awfully suspicious to him. And he had questions.

01:12:17.160 --> 01:12:22.920
Like how such an unpredictable anomaly could be&nbsp;
declared “safe”? And why had there been such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:22.920 --> 01:12:27.540
lapse of communication between the Foundation&nbsp;
and Doctor Gabriel Reed, who’d been running the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:27.540 --> 01:12:33.120
facility for the past two decades? And most&nbsp;
of all, just what exactly was the mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:33.120 --> 01:12:39.540
SCP - 5545 - 2? Monroe started to believe that&nbsp;
something terrible had happened at the site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:39.540 --> 01:12:44.760
and Reed was covering it all up. But to find&nbsp;
out for sure, he’d need to go to Antarctica&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:44.760 --> 01:12:49.440
and investigate it himself. Information&nbsp;
around this supposedly “Safe” anomaly was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:49.440 --> 01:12:54.660
highly classified - those without O5 clearance&nbsp;
could face termination for snooping. But that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:54.660 --> 01:13:00.960
didn’t scare Jason Monroe. He’d dealt with Keters&nbsp;
before, he could deal with this. Or so he thought.

01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:05.460
Monroe submitted a request and was granted&nbsp;
unanimous approval by the O5 Council to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:05.460 --> 01:13:10.320
travel to Provisional Site 344 and get&nbsp;
to the bottom of this mystery. He took&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:10.320 --> 01:13:14.700
a chopper to the base soon after, armed&nbsp;
with a concealed firearm and a Hostile&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:14.700 --> 01:13:20.100
Meme Detector - or HMD - to test whether&nbsp;
the base and its staff had somehow fallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:20.100 --> 01:13:27.300
under a hazardous memetic effect from SCP -&nbsp;
5545. He’d find the answers, or die trying.

01:13:27.300 --> 01:13:32.820
The moment Monroe arrived, he couldn’t help but&nbsp;
notice the strange way the staff behaved. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:32.820 --> 01:13:37.140
seemed listless; almost depressive. When&nbsp;
he showed his credentials to a researcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:37.140 --> 01:13:44.520
they simply said “SCP-5545-2 is contained&nbsp;
in Site-344-2.” His request to see Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:44.520 --> 01:13:50.040
Reed that night was denied. Dr. Reed was&nbsp;
busy, he was told. Wait until tomorrow.

01:13:50.040 --> 01:13:54.000
The next day, Monroe met with Dr.&nbsp;
Reed, but the results of the meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:54.000 --> 01:13:58.320
were underwhelming to say the least. Just&nbsp;
like the rest of the staff on the site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:58.320 --> 01:14:04.260
he seemed exhausted, as though he hadn’t slept&nbsp;
in days. His responses were quiet and evasive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:04.260 --> 01:14:08.280
and he refused to tell Monroe anything&nbsp;
that wasn’t in the official files already.

01:14:08.280 --> 01:14:13.920
Monroe ran the conversation through the HMD and&nbsp;
found nothing out of the ordinary. What was going&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:13.920 --> 01:14:19.920
on here? Monroe was irritated, but not deterred.&nbsp;
Nothing would stop him from finding out the truth.

01:14:20.760 --> 01:14:25.800
The next day, he flexed his O5 credentials&nbsp;
and hacked into the base’s security system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:25.800 --> 01:14:30.960
This gave him access to cameras around&nbsp;
Site - 344 -1, but more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:30.960 --> 01:14:38.580
there was a single camera inside the mysterious&nbsp;
Site - 344 - 2. Jackpot. But when he looked at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:38.580 --> 01:14:47.880
the feed was an entirely black screen with the&nbsp;
words “SCP-5545-2 is contained in Site-344-2.”

01:14:47.880 --> 01:14:54.540
The footage of the staff in 344 - 1 was equally&nbsp;
strange: The eighteen employees on site all sat at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:54.540 --> 01:14:59.700
computer banks, with nothing but static playing&nbsp;
on their screens. Monroe kept digging though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:59.700 --> 01:15:04.500
and was able to hack into the security&nbsp;
footage of Dr. Reed’s office. As he watched,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:04.500 --> 01:15:08.520
he discovered a fifteen minute period&nbsp;
where Reed left the office each day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:08.520 --> 01:15:15.840
He could use this brief window to break in&nbsp;
and collect more intel on SCP - 5545 - 2.

01:15:15.840 --> 01:15:20.700
Monroe was so wrapped up in the investigation&nbsp;
that he almost forgot the more immediate danger&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:20.700 --> 01:15:24.420
around him, and nearly wandered&nbsp;
into one of the endless hallways&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:24.420 --> 01:15:29.820
of 5545 - 1 by mistake. He made a&nbsp;
note to be more careful in future...

01:15:29.820 --> 01:15:35.100
His first attempt at breaking into Dr. Reed’s&nbsp;
office didn’t produce many answers - one piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:35.100 --> 01:15:40.440
of evidence was a blurry picture of what looked&nbsp;
like a Mobile Task Force entering a 5545 - 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:40.440 --> 01:15:45.960
hallway in the dark. Another was a spreadsheet&nbsp;
featuring all the personnel, living or dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:45.960 --> 01:15:51.660
who’d worked at the site - but one name, and the&nbsp;
details of whether this person was alive or dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:51.660 --> 01:15:56.280
was completely redacted. Anything&nbsp;
particularly juicy was hidden behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:56.280 --> 01:16:01.320
O5 clearance. If Monroe wanted the&nbsp;
answers, he’d need to break through.

01:16:01.320 --> 01:16:06.000
That night, he had a horrific recurring&nbsp;
nightmare, one that had plagued him since&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:06.000 --> 01:16:11.700
he joined MTF Eta-10. He dreamed he was in a&nbsp;
fancy dining room with a grand fireplace. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:11.700 --> 01:16:17.700
room was full of statues of men and women. The men&nbsp;
looked angry, and the women looked afraid. As he&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:17.700 --> 01:16:22.860
approached the fireplace, the ceiling extended&nbsp;
infinitely up into the darkness. Suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:22.860 --> 01:16:28.140
the zombie-like body of a teenage girl appears&nbsp;
in the fireplace, hanging from a long thread.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:28.140 --> 01:16:34.500
Her eyes look furious and full of rage, and Monroe&nbsp;
somehow knows that he’s the reason for her hate.

01:16:34.500 --> 01:16:39.060
When he steps into the fireplace in this&nbsp;
dream, she attacks him, the two intertwine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:39.060 --> 01:16:44.040
and they burn forever. The one difference&nbsp;
was that in this new iteration of the dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:44.040 --> 01:16:49.320
he blinked upon entering the fireplace,&nbsp;
and suddenly, he was in a hallway. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:49.320 --> 01:16:53.460
awoke sure that something was terribly&nbsp;
wrong here, but he couldn’t give up now.

01:16:53.460 --> 01:16:59.220
The next day, Monroe broke into Dr. Reed’s office&nbsp;
and made a horrifying discovery. He found files&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:59.220 --> 01:17:05.160
indicating that Dr. Reed was knowingly sending&nbsp;
Mobile Task Forces and D-Class personnel into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:05.160 --> 01:17:11.760
infinite hallways of 5545 - 1 to their doom. He&nbsp;
also found evidence that Reed and the researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:11.760 --> 01:17:15.900
had been spying on him, somehow intercepting&nbsp;
copies of the notes he had been taking.

01:17:15.900 --> 01:17:20.520
That’s when Dr. Reed entered the office and&nbsp;
interrupted him. Monroe panicked and drew&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:20.520 --> 01:17:25.200
his weapon, holding the doctor at gunpoint.&nbsp;
He was breaking so many Foundation rules,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:25.200 --> 01:17:30.660
but right now, he feared for his life. The&nbsp;
doctor seemed unbothered by Monroe’s threats&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:30.660 --> 01:17:35.640
though. He told Monroe that everything was going&nbsp;
to plan, and that he should go back to his room.

01:17:35.640 --> 01:17:41.040
Monroe was becoming increasingly paranoid - he&nbsp;
felt that, at any moment, guards might burst&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:41.040 --> 01:17:47.820
in and execute him. Nothing about this place made&nbsp;
sense. He worried he was going insane. Perhaps the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:47.820 --> 01:17:53.520
only way to find answers was to go even deeper:&nbsp;
To risk it all, and venture through the endless&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:53.520 --> 01:18:01.920
hallways to find SCP - 5545 - 2 himself, and&nbsp;
finally discover what this thing actually was.

01:18:01.920 --> 01:18:07.860
Monroe left his room and stepped into one of the&nbsp;
endless hallways of 5545 - 1 that was located&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:07.860 --> 01:18:13.380
just across from his dorm. Hefound that it was&nbsp;
a hallway like all the others on site - Plain&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:13.380 --> 01:18:18.360
concrete, worn with age, with simple light&nbsp;
fixtures on the walls. He walked for hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:18.360 --> 01:18:23.040
recording with a concealed device. The&nbsp;
lights suddenly went out, leaving him&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:23.040 --> 01:18:27.960
in complete darkness. When they flicked back&nbsp;
on, he was in a very different environment:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:27.960 --> 01:18:32.580
A grand, old carpeted hallway, the&nbsp;
kind you’d see in an old mansion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:32.580 --> 01:18:36.540
He broke into a cold sweat. What&nbsp;
was so familiar about this place?

01:18:36.540 --> 01:18:42.120
He kept walking, wracked with terror, until&nbsp;
this new hallway finally led him to the place&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:42.120 --> 01:18:51.120
he’d been seeking: Site 344 - 2, the domain&nbsp;
of 5545 - 2. It was a large, poorly-lit room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:51.120 --> 01:18:57.300
filled with grimacing statues and a large&nbsp;
fireplace at the far end. It was the exact same&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:57.300 --> 01:19:03.960
room from Monroe’s dream - with one horrifying&nbsp;
difference. Monroe noticed a single white thread&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:03.960 --> 01:19:09.660
hanging down from the infinite ceiling, and when&nbsp;
he looked up to find its source, he screamed.

01:19:09.660 --> 01:19:13.080
There were hundreds of bodies hanging&nbsp;
and swinging from the ceiling above&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:13.080 --> 01:19:20.160
him - everyone who SCP - 5545 - 2 had ever&nbsp;
killed, including MTF members, D-Class Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:20.160 --> 01:19:26.100
and even the colonial explorers from hundreds&nbsp;
of years before. And all of them were him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:26.100 --> 01:19:32.400
Every single one. They had his face. And there,&nbsp;
hanging in the middle of the room at ground level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:32.400 --> 01:19:38.160
was the body of a teenage girl, the&nbsp;
one from his dream. In that moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:38.160 --> 01:19:45.240
he finally recognized her: She was the girl he&nbsp;
killed. The first him. Hundreds of years ago.

01:19:45.240 --> 01:19:50.160
Much like Monroe, you’re probably wondering:&nbsp;
What is going on here? Thanks to declassified&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:50.160 --> 01:19:55.740
communications between Dr. Reed and the O5&nbsp;
Council, we can tell you. Jason Monroe is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:55.740 --> 01:20:00.180
a man who’s been reincarnated hundreds of&nbsp;
times over the last three hundred years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:00.180 --> 01:20:06.060
ever since he murdered a teenage girl…&nbsp;
A girl named Emily… his daughter.

01:20:06.060 --> 01:20:12.000
This murder sparked the existence of SCP -&nbsp;
5545 as an eternally recurring punishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:16.860
for his crimes. Since figuring this out,&nbsp;
the Foundation has kept tabs on Monroe’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:16.860 --> 01:20:22.740
reincarnations - whether they’re MTF members,&nbsp;
D-Class personnel, or even Site Directors.

01:20:22.740 --> 01:20:28.500
They see to it that these reincarnations&nbsp;
always find their way back to 5545 - 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:28.500 --> 01:20:32.580
to take his punishment, and prevent the&nbsp;
infinite hallway expansion that threatens&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:32.580 --> 01:20:38.580
to destroy the world. It’s a plan everyone is&nbsp;
in on - everyone except him. But every time&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:38.580 --> 01:20:42.300
he enters that nightmare-haunting&nbsp;
room, it all comes rushing back.

01:20:42.300 --> 01:20:48.060
In that moment though, he knew his crime, and he&nbsp;
somehow knew how many times this punishment had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:48.060 --> 01:20:54.600
unfolded for him. He now had two choices: Repent&nbsp;
and accept the punishment again, or leave and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:54.600 --> 01:21:00.660
activate 5545 - 3, potentially allowing the&nbsp;
endless tunnels to expand across the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:00.660 --> 01:21:07.440
Like his many predecessors, Monroe made the decent&nbsp;
choice. He accepted his punishment and allowed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:07.440 --> 01:21:13.920
own string to coil around him as the lights in the&nbsp;
room went off, one by one, leaving only darkness.

01:21:13.920 --> 01:21:19.080
Jason Monroe - that version of him,&nbsp;
at least - was never seen again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:19.080 --> 01:21:23.160
But The SCP Foundation is already&nbsp;
eyeing up his next reincarnation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:23.160 --> 01:21:27.566
and preparing to let this twisted&nbsp;
cycle play out all over again.

01:21:27.566 --> 01:21:27.654
If that story had you on the edge of your&nbsp;
seat, then why not subscribe to SCP Explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:27.654 --> 01:21:27.734
and hit the bell for notifications! You&nbsp;
can find out how humanity almost pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:27.734 --> 01:21:27.817
Bigfoot to extinction, discover why you&nbsp;
should never look at the Shy Guy’s face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:27.817 --> 01:21:27.900
and see the terrifying things the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation are up to in alternate realities!

01:21:27.900 --> 01:21:29.700
Are you sitting comfortably?

01:21:29.700 --> 01:21:33.600
We know a good chair is hard to&nbsp;
find. Maybe you’re watching this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:33.600 --> 01:21:37.680
on your phone while you lie in bed, or&nbsp;
maybe you’re watching it at your desk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:37.680 --> 01:21:42.540
sitting in an office chair. Maybe you’re even&nbsp;
watching it while you’re in the bathroom; it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:42.540 --> 01:21:49.020
fine, we’re not here to judge. For our money, you&nbsp;
just can’t beat a nice, classic wooden chair, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:49.020 --> 01:21:55.080
soft leather upholstery. Call us old-fashioned,&nbsp;
but some things just never go out of style.

01:21:55.080 --> 01:21:58.860
Take a chair like SCP-1609, for example.

01:21:58.860 --> 01:22:04.800
This fine piece of mahogany was once a chair that&nbsp;
simply couldn’t be beat in its quest to bring its&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:04.800 --> 01:22:10.800
users a little dose of comfort and refinement in&nbsp;
their daily life. Tell us, have you ever been on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:10.800 --> 01:22:15.600
your feet all day, just walking and walking&nbsp;
and walking, and at a certain point, you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:15.600 --> 01:22:19.920
just begging for a nice, comfy chair that’ll let&nbsp;
you take the weight off your feet for a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:19.920 --> 01:22:26.280
while? You would have been SCP-1609’s favorite&nbsp;
kind of person. After all, it was the only chair&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:26.280 --> 01:22:31.800
that literally sought out weary travelers, and&nbsp;
even did you the courtesy of tucking itself in.

01:22:31.800 --> 01:22:37.620
That’s not a metaphor, either. SCP-1609&nbsp;
could literally teleport to nearby people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:37.620 --> 01:22:43.620
who needed to sit down and didn’t have a chair to&nbsp;
fulfill that desire. It was nothing but a nice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:43.620 --> 01:22:47.880
helpful anomaly that wanted to help&nbsp;
people rest when they needed it most.

01:22:47.880 --> 01:22:52.800
The more observant members of you may have&nbsp;
noticed that we’ve been using the past tense&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:52.800 --> 01:22:59.580
so far. That’s because, while SCP-1609&nbsp;
is still an active anomaly, it isn’t a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:59.580 --> 01:23:04.980
chair anymore - and this transformation&nbsp;
wasn’t something that SCP-1609 planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:04.980 --> 01:23:11.040
anticipated, or even wanted. The story of&nbsp;
1609’s transformation even strikes to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:11.040 --> 01:23:16.080
core of one of the Foundation’s oldest and most&nbsp;
bitterly held rivalries with another group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:16.080 --> 01:23:22.080
interest. It’s the tale of how a helpful piece&nbsp;
of anomalous furniture became a paranoid killer.

01:23:22.080 --> 01:23:25.020
But first, we need to talk&nbsp;
about containment procedures.

01:23:25.020 --> 01:23:28.920
Like a word you see so often&nbsp;
that it starts to lose meaning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:28.920 --> 01:23:34.560
containment and specific containment procedures&nbsp;
are concepts so integral to the very existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:34.560 --> 01:23:40.380
of the SCP Foundation that it’s easy to&nbsp;
overlook or forget about them. They’re one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:40.380 --> 01:23:46.380
of the three core pillars of the Foundation’s&nbsp;
mission statement - Secure, Contain, Protect.

01:23:46.380 --> 01:23:50.640
Because of the centrality of containment&nbsp;
to the Foundation’s core principles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:50.640 --> 01:23:56.100
one of the most valuable roles on the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation payroll is that of the Containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:56.100 --> 01:24:01.980
Specialist: A vast team of experts who work with&nbsp;
researchers to figure out the best way to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:01.980 --> 01:24:08.340
every anomaly contained, based on their unique&nbsp;
abilities and attributes. They’re zookeepers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:08.340 --> 01:24:14.880
archivists, guards, security and intelligence&nbsp;
experts, magicians, practitioners of ritual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:14.880 --> 01:24:20.640
scientists, and so much more. In short,&nbsp;
they’re anything they need to be in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:20.640 --> 01:24:25.740
to adapt to the ever-evolving containment needs&nbsp;
of the anomalies they keep under lock and key.

01:24:25.740 --> 01:24:32.760
And containment isn’t easy. Aside from the rare&nbsp;
Safe-class SCPs, which require incredibly minimal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:32.760 --> 01:24:38.400
containment resources, the containment&nbsp;
of most SCPs extracts some kind of cost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:38.400 --> 01:24:45.660
whether that be financial, time, effort, or&nbsp;
in some particularly dark cases, human life.

01:24:45.660 --> 01:24:54.240
Some SCPs, like SCP-974 and SCP-2845, require&nbsp;
the sacrifice of human children to prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:54.240 --> 01:25:00.120
worse fates befalling many others.&nbsp;
Other SCPs, like the infamous SCP-231,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:00.120 --> 01:25:06.180
require the Foundation to do horrifying things&nbsp;
to the SCP itself to prevent it from manifesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:06.180 --> 01:25:12.900
some even more horrifying anomalous traits. And&nbsp;
a third but equally inconvenient kind of SCP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:12.900 --> 01:25:20.880
like SCP-682 and SCP-076, require huge numbers&nbsp;
of heavily armed guards with powerful weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:20.880 --> 01:25:26.160
to keep their deadly prisoners locked away,&nbsp;
often at massive risk to their own lives.

01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:31.560
Containment isn’t easy, but it’s ultimately&nbsp;
the very thing that makes the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:31.560 --> 01:25:36.960
the organization it is. If they were instead&nbsp;
on a quest to kill and destroy every anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:36.960 --> 01:25:42.000
they could get their hands on, then, they’d&nbsp;
be the Global Occult Coalition - the UN’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:42.000 --> 01:25:48.660
answer to the SCP Foundation that prefers to seek,&nbsp;
disable, and destroy rather than Secure, Contain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:48.660 --> 01:25:54.300
and Protect. It’s the primary characteristic that&nbsp;
differentiates these two titans of the anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:54.300 --> 01:26:00.900
world who regularly come to blows, and right&nbsp;
at the heart of that difference is SCP-1609.

01:26:00.900 --> 01:26:06.960
As we mentioned earlier, SCP-1609 went through&nbsp;
a transformation that changed everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:06.960 --> 01:26:12.720
but the SCP Foundation never actually knew about&nbsp;
the anomaly prior to that transformation taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:12.720 --> 01:26:17.280
place. It first came to their attention&nbsp;
when it literally manifested within a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:17.280 --> 01:26:22.860
containment cell in Storage Site-08, making&nbsp;
the rare move of willingly submitting itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:22.860 --> 01:26:28.080
to Foundation containment. But what showed&nbsp;
up in that cell certainly wasn’t a chair.

01:26:28.080 --> 01:26:33.540
When 1609 appeared all it looked like was&nbsp;
a pile of trash - specifically, splinters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:33.540 --> 01:26:38.160
wood chippings, furniture nails, and&nbsp;
scraps of bleached leather and fabric.

01:26:38.160 --> 01:26:42.900
Anything that suddenly infiltrates a secure&nbsp;
Foundation containment site is a cause for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:42.900 --> 01:26:48.960
concern, even a bunch of wood scraps, so the Site&nbsp;
Director sent in an armed guard to investigate&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:48.960 --> 01:26:54.180
the mysterious pile of debris. Researchers&nbsp;
watching over a surveillance feed were surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:54.180 --> 01:26:58.980
when the guard suddenly entered a state of&nbsp;
heightened distress. He fell to his knees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:58.980 --> 01:27:03.420
coughing and spluttering until he expelled&nbsp;
a considerable amount of blood from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:03.420 --> 01:27:08.580
mouth and nose. He then collapsed onto the&nbsp;
ground next to the pile of debris, dead.

01:27:08.580 --> 01:27:13.800
An investigation following this incident found&nbsp;
that the guard had died after a sudden influx&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:13.800 --> 01:27:18.720
of jagged metal and wood had teleported&nbsp;
inside of him, tearing his lungs apart&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:18.720 --> 01:27:23.580
from the inside and causing the guard&nbsp;
to die a painful and horrific death.

01:27:23.580 --> 01:27:28.800
Naturally, the site personnel were somewhat&nbsp;
concerned by this development. They sent in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:28.800 --> 01:27:32.760
a D-Class to investigate further, but&nbsp;
were surprised to find that the D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:32.760 --> 01:27:37.320
in question was somehow completely fine. The&nbsp;
pile of debris that would soon be designated&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:37.320 --> 01:27:44.280
SCP-1609 made no attempt to harm the D-Class as&nbsp;
it had the guard, and finding out why this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:44.280 --> 01:27:50.280
the case came as a side effect of figuring&nbsp;
out exactly what had happened to SCP-1609.

01:27:50.280 --> 01:27:55.080
Through a rigorous investigation, involving&nbsp;
more than one secret Foundation mole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:55.080 --> 01:28:01.500
they discovered that SCP-1609 had previously been&nbsp;
in the possession of - you guessed it - the Global&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:01.500 --> 01:28:06.720
Occult Coalition. Back then, it was just&nbsp;
the helpful chair you once knew and loved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:06.720 --> 01:28:12.180
until the GOC had the bright idea of forcing&nbsp;
it into a woodchipper in order to destroy it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:12.180 --> 01:28:17.820
due to its connection to someone called The&nbsp;
Carpenter. But all the GOC’s attempt actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:17.820 --> 01:28:23.040
succeeded in doing was altering its form,&nbsp;
and completely changing its personality.

01:28:23.040 --> 01:28:30.360
To put it in simple terms, SCP-1609 is now a pile&nbsp;
of possibly-sentient, teleporting wood and metal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:30.360 --> 01:28:36.600
chippings that suffers from a nasty case of PTSD.&nbsp;
The incident with the wood chipper traumatized&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:36.600 --> 01:28:42.840
SCP-1609, and its anxiety is triggered by&nbsp;
anything that reminds it of the GOC or the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:42.840 --> 01:28:47.820
wood chipper incident - this includes wearing&nbsp;
formal clothing, lab coats, protective clothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:47.820 --> 01:28:54.000
jumpsuits, and particularly body armor, but&nbsp;
also includes anyone carrying weapons, appearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:54.000 --> 01:29:02.040
outwardly aggressive, using common GOC lingo, or&nbsp;
even mentioning the GOC in SCP-1609’s proximity.

01:29:02.040 --> 01:29:07.680
If any of this happens, it’s extremely likely&nbsp;
that SCP-1609 will resort to its only natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:07.680 --> 01:29:12.780
defense mechanism, which is teleporting its&nbsp;
debris into the lungs of anyone it considers&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:12.780 --> 01:29:18.180
to be a threat. The guard had received this&nbsp;
grisly punishment because his clothes, weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:18.180 --> 01:29:25.320
and overall manner caused SCP-1609 to regard&nbsp;
him as a threat and react accordingly. You may&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:25.320 --> 01:29:30.420
think this is overkill on 1609’s part, but if you&nbsp;
were just trying to help out the chairless people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:30.420 --> 01:29:35.700
of the world and someone fed you into a wood&nbsp;
chipper, you’d probably be a little jumpy too.

01:29:35.700 --> 01:29:40.620
Since these early days, the Foundation has&nbsp;
learned to apply a more tender touch when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:40.620 --> 01:29:46.740
comes to dealing with SCP-1609, and the brilliant&nbsp;
containment specialists even figured out a way&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:46.740 --> 01:29:52.560
to keep 1609 happily contained… by placing&nbsp;
it in a flower bed inside its containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:52.560 --> 01:29:57.240
chamber where its wood chips get to serve as&nbsp;
mulch for a variety of flowers and plants.

01:29:57.240 --> 01:30:00.660
All attending researchers and&nbsp;
guards dress in plain clothes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:00.660 --> 01:30:04.920
and adopt a loose, pleasant attitude&nbsp;
while inside. Whenever they’re around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:04.920 --> 01:30:09.300
they make a point of saying how beautiful&nbsp;
the flower bed is, so that the disfigured&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:09.300 --> 01:30:13.800
anomaly that only ever wanted to be helpful&nbsp;
can still feel like it’s doing something nice.

01:30:13.800 --> 01:30:19.740
Because of these containment procedures,&nbsp;
breaches involving SCP-1609 have remained in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:19.740 --> 01:30:25.860
the single digits. It’s a perfect example of less&nbsp;
really being more when it comes to containment.

01:30:25.860 --> 01:30:31.800
The head researcher on the SCP-1609 case,&nbsp;
Dr. Sievert, released an internal document,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:31.800 --> 01:30:37.140
permanently affixed to the file like a kind of&nbsp;
cautionary signpost. It’s a clear expression&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:37.140 --> 01:30:42.180
of exasperation and rage at the actions&nbsp;
of the Global Occult Coalition, reading:

01:30:42.180 --> 01:30:48.360
“SCP-1609 represents a perfect example of the&nbsp;
flaws inherent in the operating procedure of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:48.360 --> 01:30:54.000
the GOC, and serves as a cautionary tale for&nbsp;
any members of the Foundation who disagree with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:54.000 --> 01:30:59.520
our practices on containing dangerous objects.
Prior to the Coalition getting their hands on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:59.520 --> 01:31:04.740
this, it was perfectly harmless. A chair which&nbsp;
teleports to you when you need a seat is normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:04.740 --> 01:31:09.480
compared to most of the stuff that we deal with&nbsp;
on a regular basis. When they put it through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:09.480 --> 01:31:14.940
woodchipper, it got hurt, scared and angry, so&nbsp;
it lashed out at them. By trying to 'protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:14.940 --> 01:31:21.360
the world' by destroying it, they inadvertently&nbsp;
made the situation a whole lot worse. SCP-1609&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:26.100
went from being harmless to deadly in the&nbsp;
space of a few minutes because of the GOC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:26.100 --> 01:31:30.900
and we had to clean up the mess.
Thankfully, SCP-1609 is pretty simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:30.900 --> 01:31:36.000
for us to deal with. So long as we don't do&nbsp;
anything stupid around it, it won't fight back&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:36.000 --> 01:31:41.220
and it won't try to leave. Even if it does,&nbsp;
it usually comes back. I think I've worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:41.220 --> 01:31:46.200
out why. It came to us because it was afraid&nbsp;
of the people who had hurt it. That's why it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:46.200 --> 01:31:51.360
always comes back. It's afraid of the rest of the&nbsp;
world now, and it's looking to us for protection.&nbsp;

01:31:51.360 --> 01:31:56.940
This is why we have Special Containment&nbsp;
Procedures instead of Special Destruction&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:56.940 --> 01:32:02.520
Procedures. If you break something, it's broken&nbsp;
forever. When you try to destroy an anomaly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:02.520 --> 01:32:09.360
you can't take back your mistakes. That's&nbsp;
what SCP-1609 has to tell us. This is why&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:09.360 --> 01:32:14.220
we're right and the GOC is wrong, people.”
But of course, there are two sides to every&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:14.220 --> 01:32:19.920
story, and it’s important to understand the GOC’s&nbsp;
perspective on this whole mess. To them, this has&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:19.920 --> 01:32:28.200
never been SCP-1609, it’s KTE-0937-Velveteen,&nbsp;
aka The Sixth Chair. It was labeled as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:28.200 --> 01:32:33.420
“sixth” because for the GOC, this chair was&nbsp;
merely one part of a wider investigation.

01:32:33.420 --> 01:32:38.400
It belonged to a six piece furniture set&nbsp;
created by a dangerous, anomalous person&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:38.400 --> 01:32:44.520
of interest named The Carpenter for a classified&nbsp;
customer. The GOC was able to intercept this deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:44.520 --> 01:32:49.200
and kill the Carpenter and his customer in&nbsp;
the process. After that, all that was left&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:49.200 --> 01:32:54.720
was to eliminate the anomalous objects and five of&nbsp;
them were incinerated without incident. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:54.720 --> 01:32:59.940
before they could do the same to the Sixth Chair,&nbsp;
they experienced an incinerator malfunction.

01:32:59.940 --> 01:33:05.400
Rather than waiting for the incinerator to be&nbsp;
fixed, a member of GOC personnel decided to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:05.400 --> 01:33:09.480
rush the job and run the chair through the&nbsp;
woodchipper. It was at this point that its&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:09.480 --> 01:33:15.360
pieces first lashed out, invading the lungs of&nbsp;
this negligent GOC member along with five others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:15.360 --> 01:33:22.080
killing them all. It was shortly after that that&nbsp;
SCP-1609 manifested in Foundation containment.

01:33:22.080 --> 01:33:27.660
Much like Dr. Sievert did for the Foundation,&nbsp;
Assistant Director Kipling, one of the GOC’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:27.660 --> 01:33:33.660
legion of middle managers, affixed a note to&nbsp;
the profile on KTE-0937-Velveteen that reads:

01:33:33.660 --> 01:33:39.480
“KTE-0937-Velveteen is an object lesson in&nbsp;
the importance of following proper operating&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:39.480 --> 01:33:44.400
procedures. Due to the lack of vigilance by&nbsp;
the agent on the scene, the object's threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:44.400 --> 01:33:49.140
level was escalated, the object itself&nbsp;
was not successfully disposed of, and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:49.140 --> 01:33:54.540
has since fallen into the hands of a hostile&nbsp;
agency. A single failure by a single operative&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:54.540 --> 01:33:59.580
resulted in the deaths of six. Remember this&nbsp;
the next time you think about cutting corners.”

01:33:59.580 --> 01:34:04.320
And that’s a good lesson for everyone. Whether&nbsp;
you’re trying to destroy an anomalous piece of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:04.320 --> 01:34:07.920
furniture or keeping its remains happy&nbsp;
so that they don’t try to kill you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:07.920 --> 01:34:11.640
cutting corners is always a fast track to failure.

01:34:11.640 --> 01:34:18.000
Joseph and Frank were two life-long Squatchers.&nbsp;
No, that isn’t an insult – that’s a self-given&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:18.000 --> 01:34:22.560
title for Bigfoot enthusiasts who are willing&nbsp;
to head out into the woods and search for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:22.560 --> 01:34:26.820
legendary Sasquatch first-hand. While most&nbsp;
Squatchers will go their whole lives without&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:26.820 --> 01:34:31.920
ever encountering one, Joseph and Frank were about&nbsp;
to get lucky – they just didn’t know what kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:31.920 --> 01:34:36.420
luck. During a journey through the forests of&nbsp;
the Pacific Northwest, Frank spotted something&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:36.420 --> 01:34:42.060
moving in the distance: A huge, ape-like creature&nbsp;
with greyish fur and human-like movements. Frank&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:42.060 --> 01:34:46.380
thought he was finally laying eyes on the&nbsp;
mighty Bigfoot after decades of searching.&nbsp;

01:34:46.380 --> 01:34:52.594
What he didn’t know was that he’d just made a&nbsp;
deadly mistake. He had looked directly at SCP –&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:52.594 --> 01:34:58.799
1000. And there would be terrible consequences.
Frank was excited – he’d just achieved the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:58.800 --> 01:35:03.120
goal of any Squatcher. He tapped Joseph on&nbsp;
the shoulder and directed him to look in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:03.120 --> 01:35:07.680
direction of the creature. Joseph followed Frank’s&nbsp;
direction and stared into the distance. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:07.680 --> 01:35:13.320
his eyes finally came into focus on the ape-like&nbsp;
beast... he froze. His brain just short-circuited.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:13.320 --> 01:35:17.760
One second, he was about to encounter the&nbsp;
Holy Grail of his hobby, and the next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:17.760 --> 01:35:23.760
he was literally brain dead. Joseph collapsed.
In the distance, the ape-like creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:23.760 --> 01:35:27.720
disappeared back into the woods. Not&nbsp;
that Frank even noticed – he was too&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:27.720 --> 01:35:33.780
busy trying to wake Joseph but it was no use.&nbsp;
Joseph was gone, and Frank had no idea why.&nbsp;

01:35:33.780 --> 01:35:39.120
The headlines read, “BIGFOOT KILLED MY FRIEND.”&nbsp;
Most people either ignored it or laughed it off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:39.120 --> 01:35:44.880
Just a couple of cranks goofing off in a forest&nbsp;
and one of them had dropped dead. Who cares? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:44.880 --> 01:35:51.360
one organization cared – The SCP Foundation.&nbsp;
Mobile Task Force Zeta-1000, the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:51.360 --> 01:35:56.340
specialized SCP – 1000 detail, were alerted&nbsp;
to the reports. They sprang into action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:56.340 --> 01:36:01.680
tracking down and detaining Frank for questioning.&nbsp;
They process a million loony bigfoot lovers every&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:01.680 --> 01:36:05.400
year, and usually find nothing, but the&nbsp;
death of Frank’s friend made it all too&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:05.400 --> 01:36:11.100
clear – they hadn’t encountered a bigfoot&nbsp;
but a real, genuine example of SCP – 1000.&nbsp;

01:36:11.880 --> 01:36:18.780
SCP – 1000 rarely ranks among the scariest or most&nbsp;
dangerous SCPs, but underestimating the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:18.780 --> 01:36:24.180
is a terrible mistake because just looking at&nbsp;
it gives you a 2% chance of dropping dead on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:24.180 --> 01:36:28.920
the spot. Frank, despite losing his friend,&nbsp;
was one of the lucky ones. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:28.920 --> 01:36:33.840
debriefed him before administering amnestics,&nbsp;
and making sure that he’d never venture back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:33.840 --> 01:36:39.180
those mysterious forests in the Pacific Northwest&nbsp;
again. Director Jones, the site director charged&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:39.180 --> 01:36:44.040
with the management of SCP – 1000 populations,&nbsp;
was given the information on this latest case&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:44.040 --> 01:36:50.220
of a SCP – 1000-related fatality. It was a story&nbsp;
he’d heard many times before. For Director Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:50.220 --> 01:36:56.040
they all seemed to bleed into one another.
So, what exactly is SCP – 1000? And how did&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:56.040 --> 01:37:00.960
it leave poor Joseph dead in the woods?&nbsp;
SCP – 1000 is a whole species of large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:00.960 --> 01:37:05.160
hominid ape-like creatures. They’re largely&nbsp;
nocturnal, but sightings of the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:05.160 --> 01:37:09.660
during the day aren’t unheard of. They’re&nbsp;
omnivorous, mostly seeming to consume plants&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:09.660 --> 01:37:14.640
and insects and their fur is usually grey,&nbsp;
brown, black, red, or occasionally white.&nbsp;

01:37:15.480 --> 01:37:20.280
The creatures have large eyes capable of&nbsp;
impressive vision nestled underneath a pronounced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:20.280 --> 01:37:24.960
Neanderthal-like brow. Another defining&nbsp;
feature is the ridge of bone on the forehead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:24.960 --> 01:37:30.060
much like that of a gorilla, that is present&nbsp;
in both sexes. According to Foundation studies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:30.060 --> 01:37:34.620
the creatures exhibit a level of intelligence&nbsp;
on par with that of the common chimpanzee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:34.620 --> 01:37:39.300
but nowhere near that of us humans. What they lack&nbsp;
in intelligence, though, they more than make up&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:39.300 --> 01:37:44.520
for in size. The adults can be as large as&nbsp;
ten feet tall, and weigh up to 600 pounds.&nbsp;

01:37:44.520 --> 01:37:48.480
Despite their great size and impressive&nbsp;
strength, the creatures are neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:48.480 --> 01:37:53.400
aggressive nor territorial. In fact, they&nbsp;
seem to instinctively avoid humans, mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:53.400 --> 01:37:57.900
residing deep in the forests of the American&nbsp;
Pacific Northwest and in the Himalayan Alps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:57.900 --> 01:38:03.180
There have been sightings of SCP – 1000 on every&nbsp;
continent, though the Foundation has taken pains&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:03.180 --> 01:38:08.340
to exterminate all SCP – 1000 populations&nbsp;
situated near human population centres to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:08.340 --> 01:38:14.040
prevent a potential disaster, considering the 2%&nbsp;
chance of instantaneous death upon visual contact.&nbsp;

01:38:14.040 --> 01:38:19.500
That brings us to our second question: What is&nbsp;
it that makes these seemingly harmless creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:19.500 --> 01:38:25.500
so dangerous? Sadly, for both these unfortunate&nbsp;
creatures and us humans, the danger is beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:25.500 --> 01:38:32.280
control of SCP – 1000. According to Foundation&nbsp;
research, SCP – 1000 likely evolved alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:32.280 --> 01:38:37.260
us homo sapiens, until a tragedy occurred&nbsp;
between ten and fifteen-thousand years ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:37.260 --> 01:38:42.300
A mysterious extinction event eliminated the&nbsp;
vast majority of their species, leaving only&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:42.300 --> 01:38:47.520
one to five percent alive in the aftermath. What&nbsp;
happened? It’s believed that around this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:47.520 --> 01:38:52.620
SCP – 1000 contracted what the Foundation&nbsp;
refers to as an “anomalous pseudo-disease.”&nbsp;

01:38:52.620 --> 01:39:00.240
Meet SCP-1000-f1, a disease that is passed along&nbsp;
at the genetic level, and is so durable that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:00.240 --> 01:39:05.100
persists in the species to this day. The tiny&nbsp;
fraction of the population that are immune to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:05.100 --> 01:39:10.140
its effects manage to survive, but the majority&nbsp;
who aren’t immune die shortly after birth. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:10.140 --> 01:39:14.760
is why the overall population remains relatively&nbsp;
low to this day. It’s a disease that only&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:14.760 --> 01:39:20.160
appears to affect hominids – including humans,&nbsp;
chimpanzees, bonobos, and non-immune instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:20.160 --> 01:39:25.620
of SCP-1000. Any hominid that lays eyes on&nbsp;
a carrier of the disease has a two percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:25.620 --> 01:39:30.720
chance of experiencing immediate brain death.
While a two percent chance of instant death&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:30.720 --> 01:39:35.400
may not seem all that threatening, at least when&nbsp;
compared to some other nightmare inducing SCPs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:35.400 --> 01:39:40.680
the truly scary part is that the percentage&nbsp;
is cumulative. In other words, the longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:40.680 --> 01:39:46.860
one observes a carrier of SCP-1000-f1, the higher&nbsp;
that percentage rises and the greater your chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:46.860 --> 01:39:52.380
of experiencing an abrupt death. According&nbsp;
to Foundation studies, the percentage rises&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:52.380 --> 01:39:57.480
by around one percent every twenty minutes. And&nbsp;
the percentage also varies between specimens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:57.480 --> 01:40:03.480
with some exhibiting a terrifyingly high death&nbsp;
chance of 90% upon viewing. This death chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:03.480 --> 01:40:07.440
continues to occur in dead specimens if&nbsp;
they carried the anomalous pseudo-virus&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:07.440 --> 01:40:12.420
while alive – though thankfully the risk doesn’t&nbsp;
appear to apply to small fur or tissue samples.&nbsp;

01:40:12.420 --> 01:40:18.300
The Foundation’s true concern actually goes far&nbsp;
beyond SCP – 1000 themselves. Because of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:18.300 --> 01:40:24.960
species’ close relation to homo sapiens, there’s&nbsp;
a worry that SCP-1000-f1 could transmit to humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:24.960 --> 01:40:32.220
causing our own species to meet a similar fate. If&nbsp;
humans did indeed become carriers of SCP-1000-f1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:32.220 --> 01:40:37.440
it’s extremely likely that humanity would&nbsp;
undergo an unprecedented extinction event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:37.440 --> 01:40:42.720
with billions across the globe dropping&nbsp;
dead as brain death sets in en masse. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:42.720 --> 01:40:47.460
full extermination of the entire species has&nbsp;
been deemed unlikely, the existential threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:47.460 --> 01:40:52.860
they pose to humanity more than justifies the&nbsp;
occasional culling of SCP – 1000 populations.&nbsp;

01:40:53.640 --> 01:40:57.840
That was a lot to take in, right? First, the&nbsp;
creature we thought was Bigfoot was actually a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:57.840 --> 01:41:03.240
new species of SCP out in the wild. And second,&nbsp;
these creatures could end human life as we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:03.240 --> 01:41:08.160
it if they made it into a population center.&nbsp;
But what you’re about to hear next – a dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:08.160 --> 01:41:12.900
secret only available to people with&nbsp;
Level 3 SCP Foundation clearance – is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:12.900 --> 01:41:19.320
the most shocking SCP - 1000 fact of all...
Are you ready? The true secret of SCP - 1000&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:19.320 --> 01:41:25.620
is that what you’ve just heard is a lie. There&nbsp;
is no anomalous pseudo-disease, and SCP – 1000&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:25.620 --> 01:41:32.220
poses no pathogenic threat to humanity whatsoever.
Who would spread such a thing? The SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:32.220 --> 01:41:37.260
of course. Strictly speaking, the Foundation has&nbsp;
disseminated two direct lies about the nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:37.260 --> 01:41:43.740
of SCP – 1000. The first is that of the disease,&nbsp;
which does not exist, nor has it ever existed. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:43.740 --> 01:41:47.820
second lie is about the creature’s intelligence&nbsp;
level – they’re far smarter than the average&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:47.820 --> 01:41:53.580
chimp. In fact, they’re every bit as intelligent&nbsp;
as human beings. These were all lies formulated by&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:53.580 --> 01:41:59.460
Director Jones and the Foundation, as was the very&nbsp;
existence of the Bigfoot myth. The Foundation has&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:59.460 --> 01:42:03.780
been spreading information that makes the very&nbsp;
concept of the Sasquatch out to be a joke for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:03.780 --> 01:42:09.900
decades, all to discredit and further push the&nbsp;
very concept of SCP – 1000 into the shadows.&nbsp;

01:42:10.500 --> 01:42:15.060
But…why? The Foundation is no stranger&nbsp;
to coming up with cover stories, but why&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:15.060 --> 01:42:20.160
would they put intentional lies into their own&nbsp;
files to anyone below a Level 3 clearance? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:20.160 --> 01:42:26.640
that all comes down to the horrifying truth behind&nbsp;
the origins of today’s SCP – 1000 population. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:26.640 --> 01:42:30.900
creatures were first brought to the attention of&nbsp;
the Foundation by outcast members of the Serpent’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:30.900 --> 01:42:36.300
Hand, an organization dedicated to defying&nbsp;
the Foundation’s activities. These members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:36.300 --> 01:42:42.000
known as the Children of the Sun, told them the&nbsp;
secret history of SCP – 1000. While at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:42.000 --> 01:42:45.780
Foundation personnel like Director Jones&nbsp;
didn’t want to believe what they were hearing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:45.780 --> 01:42:52.380
they soon came to terms with the horrifying truth.
Humans and SCP – 1000 did evolve alongside each&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:52.380 --> 01:42:58.080
other, with humans occupying the day and SCP –&nbsp;
1000 the night. However, while humans were still&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:58.080 --> 01:43:04.680
basic hunter-gatherers, SCP – 1000 were undergoing&nbsp;
vast intellectual and societal development. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:04.680 --> 01:43:10.080
were able to create tools, weapons, agriculture,&nbsp;
stable settlements, domesticated animals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:10.080 --> 01:43:15.120
and eventually even fully developed cities.&nbsp;
It was like nothing the world had ever seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:15.120 --> 01:43:20.520
and wouldn’t see for thousands of years to come.&nbsp;
Their numbers swelled into the tens of billions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:20.520 --> 01:43:25.860
as they created culture and technology hitherto&nbsp;
unimagined – including weapons of devastating&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:25.860 --> 01:43:30.420
power. Meanwhile, humanity was pushed to the&nbsp;
brink of destruction by their competitor’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:30.420 --> 01:43:35.640
rapid and seemingly unstoppable growth.
It looked as though the human species had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:35.640 --> 01:43:40.740
lost the evolutionary arms race, and would have to&nbsp;
bow out, but according to the Children of the Sun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:40.740 --> 01:43:47.520
a trickster forest god smiled upon humanity, and&nbsp;
gave them the power to use SCP – 1000’s weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:47.520 --> 01:43:54.180
and technology against them. 70% of SCP – 1000’s&nbsp;
population were wiped out in a single horrific&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:54.180 --> 01:43:59.580
day, known to the Children of the Sun as “The&nbsp;
Day of the Flowers” – as every flower supposedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:59.580 --> 01:44:06.300
bloomed that day during the massacre. Humanity&nbsp;
destroyed the entire civilization, and with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:06.300 --> 01:44:11.580
same technology they stole from these unfortunate&nbsp;
creatures, the vengeful humans drove the apes mad.&nbsp;

01:44:11.580 --> 01:44:16.620
Their higher consciousnesses were blocked&nbsp;
out, reducing them back into the states of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:16.620 --> 01:44:21.360
mere animals. Once the massacre was done and&nbsp;
everything that was built had been destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:21.360 --> 01:44:28.020
we – the human race – used the SCP – 1000 weapons&nbsp;
to wipe any memory of the atrocity from our own&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:28.020 --> 01:44:34.680
minds. The advanced civilization of SCP – 1000 had&nbsp;
been wiped from history. Humans returned to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:34.680 --> 01:44:39.780
plodding path of evolution, none the wiser. For&nbsp;
thousands of years, all the way up until today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:39.780 --> 01:44:45.660
this time remained a mystery to us. So again,&nbsp;
why did the Foundation lie to us? What did&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:45.660 --> 01:44:49.740
they have to gain, by convincing us all that it&nbsp;
was dangerous to even look at these creatures?&nbsp;

01:44:49.740 --> 01:44:53.640
Well, as the frequency of sightings and&nbsp;
the attempts at communication increased,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:53.640 --> 01:44:57.000
people like Director Jones became&nbsp;
aware of a frightening possibility:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:57.000 --> 01:45:02.940
What if the pendulum was swinging back? What if&nbsp;
the apes were regaining their lost intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:02.940 --> 01:45:08.400
and worse, still harboured feelings of revenge&nbsp;
for what we did to their species thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:08.400 --> 01:45:13.560
years ago? Even the mere possibility that&nbsp;
they could do to us what we once did to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:13.560 --> 01:45:19.380
is a chance that the Foundation simply cannot&nbsp;
take, and thus, limiting contact between humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:19.380 --> 01:45:26.940
and SCP - 1000 at all costs is an absolute must.
However, in spite of the Foundation’s fears, one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:26.940 --> 01:45:31.740
intercepted message from the apes suggests that&nbsp;
their paranoia may be misplaced. This message,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:31.740 --> 01:45:36.900
translated from an attempt at communicating with&nbsp;
Foundation personnel, reads simply as follows:&nbsp;

01:45:36.900 --> 01:45:40.800
“we forgive you;
given choice for now, not forever;&nbsp;

01:45:40.800 --> 01:45:44.880
let us back in.”
It’s enough to make you wonder what species&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:44.880 --> 01:45:49.200
the Foundation should really be keeping tabs&nbsp;
on here. After all, when it comes to meting out&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:49.200 --> 01:45:54.060
violence and death, humanity has a track record&nbsp;
to rival the worst creatures in the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:54.060 --> 01:46:00.780
containment cells. And few examples illustrate&nbsp;
that better than the tragic case of SCP – 1000.

01:46:00.780 --> 01:46:04.440
Someone was screaming inside the incinerator.

01:46:04.440 --> 01:46:11.160
The year was 1975. The location was a top&nbsp;
secret refinery and waste disposal plant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:11.160 --> 01:46:17.580
one of the many front organizations owned and&nbsp;
operated by the SCP Foundation. This sprawling&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:17.580 --> 01:46:22.740
facility, separated into three different&nbsp;
huge units, each with a specialized task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:22.740 --> 01:46:28.740
was located around 75 kilometers outside of&nbsp;
Summer Springs, Colorado. It had operated&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:28.740 --> 01:46:34.860
for several decades without incident, but&nbsp;
today, all hell was about to break loose.

01:46:34.860 --> 01:46:39.660
Alarms were blaring in Unit C, the&nbsp;
area of the facility that dealt with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:39.660 --> 01:46:44.100
destroying non-anomalous waste via&nbsp;
incineration. A traumatized worker&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:44.100 --> 01:46:48.660
had pulled the emergency lever near one&nbsp;
of the incinerators in a panic when he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:48.660 --> 01:46:54.180
first heard the loud banging against the&nbsp;
interior walls, and then, those horrific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:54.180 --> 01:47:01.200
pained wails. That’s when the workers of Unit&nbsp;
C came to a horrifying realization: The screams&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:01.200 --> 01:47:06.780
weren’t just coming from one of the incinerators&nbsp;
in Unit C, they were coming from all six.

01:47:06.780 --> 01:47:12.780
A chorus of absolute agony,&nbsp;
echoing up out of the ash pits.

01:47:12.780 --> 01:47:18.780
This was impossible, as far as the Unit C&nbsp;
staff were concerned. These incinerators were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:18.780 --> 01:47:23.760
only to be used for confirmed non-anomalous&nbsp;
material - could some animals or even some&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:23.760 --> 01:47:27.900
poor workers somehow fallen into the&nbsp;
incinerators? But even if they had,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:27.900 --> 01:47:35.100
what were the odds that someone had fallen in&nbsp;
all six of them at once? It was impossible. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:35.100 --> 01:47:38.400
Site Director was immediately brought&nbsp;
in to authorize an investigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:38.400 --> 01:47:42.840
at which point he demanded that at least&nbsp;
one of the furnaces - in this case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:42.840 --> 01:47:49.080
Furnace Number 4 - be shut off so researchers and&nbsp;
guards could investigate what was going on inside.

01:47:49.080 --> 01:47:51.720
It seemed like the obvious course of action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:51.720 --> 01:47:57.180
but for some of the people on site that&nbsp;
day, this would prove to be a fatal mistake.

01:47:57.180 --> 01:48:01.680
When the fires were put out, something&nbsp;
started rattling in the disposal chute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:01.680 --> 01:48:07.200
There was a scratching and squealing noise,&nbsp;
like something scraping up against the metal.

01:48:07.200 --> 01:48:12.000
A maintenance worker was ordered to go&nbsp;
check inside, and when he opened the hatch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:12.000 --> 01:48:14.400
he let out a bone-chilling shriek.

01:48:14.400 --> 01:48:20.100
There was something - or was it someone?&nbsp;
- climbing back up the disposal chute. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:20.100 --> 01:48:24.660
emerged from the darkness, backlit by the&nbsp;
still-burning embers of the incinerator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:24.660 --> 01:48:29.520
letting out an awful, screeching noise&nbsp;
that could make even a hardened Mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:29.520 --> 01:48:35.100
Task Force operative shake with fear.&nbsp;
The creature was humanoid, a charred,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:35.100 --> 01:48:39.960
mutilated skeleton, reaching out towards&nbsp;
the maintenance worker with a bony claw.

01:48:39.960 --> 01:48:43.260
Before the worker had a chance&nbsp;
to stumble back in horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:43.260 --> 01:48:48.660
the beast had clasped him by the throat and&nbsp;
started to squeeze. It didn’t even need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:48.660 --> 01:48:53.280
strangle him - the heat of its skeletal hand&nbsp;
burned away the worker’s throat in seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:53.280 --> 01:48:58.860
leaving his limp, wheezing body to drop to&nbsp;
the metal grate of the platform below him.

01:48:58.860 --> 01:49:02.760
Several armed guards and maintenance workers&nbsp;
moved forward to fend off the monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:02.760 --> 01:49:07.800
but just then a volley of more violent&nbsp;
shrieks echoed out of the chute behind it.

01:49:07.800 --> 01:49:11.940
It only took seconds for over a dozen&nbsp;
more creatures to crawl out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:11.940 --> 01:49:17.220
disposal chute. They were all like the first&nbsp;
- people at various stages of incineration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:17.220 --> 01:49:22.620
some were glowing, charred skeletons&nbsp;
with barely any flesh, others looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:22.620 --> 01:49:29.160
more like severe burn victims, their faces&nbsp;
contorted into scowls of hate and rage.

01:49:29.160 --> 01:49:35.040
The assembled guards opened fire on the sudden&nbsp;
influx of anomalies, emptying the magazines of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:35.040 --> 01:49:40.620
their submachine guns into the burning bodies,&nbsp;
but their weapons didn’t seem to cause any&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:40.620 --> 01:49:45.540
lasting damage. The bullets would tear through&nbsp;
the flesh of the creatures, causing some of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:45.540 --> 01:49:51.840
to stumble and fall, but the wounds would close&nbsp;
and the creatures would rise again. It seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:51.840 --> 01:49:57.300
they possessed a deadly combo of extremely high&nbsp;
aggression, and incredible regenerative abilities.

01:49:57.300 --> 01:50:02.880
None of the staff present in Unit C were safe&nbsp;
as the burned corpses attacked anyone they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:02.880 --> 01:50:08.700
could find with their bare hands, beating and&nbsp;
biting and clawing. Many of them would grapple&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:08.700 --> 01:50:14.340
with Foundation personnel, latching on to them and&nbsp;
trying to pull them back down into the incinerator&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:14.340 --> 01:50:21.840
with them. These creatures that would later be&nbsp;
known as SCP-2419-A caused several fatalities with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:21.840 --> 01:50:27.240
their surprise attack that day, and the situation&nbsp;
was only brought back under control when a Mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:27.240 --> 01:50:32.220
Task Force that possessed more advanced training&nbsp;
and weaponry was dispatched to the location.

01:50:32.220 --> 01:50:38.460
Despite orders from the Site Director, the MTF&nbsp;
found it impossible to actually terminate any&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:38.460 --> 01:50:44.220
of the entities due to their regenerative&nbsp;
abilities. Instead, the MTF agents focused&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:44.220 --> 01:50:50.160
on forcing the anomalies back into the chute of&nbsp;
Incinerator Number 4 using a powerful industrial&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:50.160 --> 01:50:55.740
steam lance. Once they were back inside, the&nbsp;
incinerator’s burners were started up once&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:55.740 --> 01:51:01.080
again. The MTF were also able to capture five&nbsp;
of the entities and detain them for questioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:01.080 --> 01:51:06.360
and experimentation, finally bringing this&nbsp;
unexpected containment breach to an end.

01:51:06.360 --> 01:51:10.560
The Foundation is an organization that&nbsp;
prides itself on possessing forbidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:10.560 --> 01:51:16.080
and secret knowledge, but even they had&nbsp;
no idea what had just happened. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:16.080 --> 01:51:19.980
seemed to be no earthly explanation&nbsp;
why these creatures would suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:19.980 --> 01:51:25.560
manifest inside the incinerators, but as the&nbsp;
detained anomalies continued regenerating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:25.560 --> 01:51:31.560
a slightly clearer picture of what exactly the&nbsp;
Foundation was dealing with began to emerge.

01:51:31.560 --> 01:51:37.020
Every single one of the captured anomalies kept&nbsp;
regenerating, and upon getting to the point that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:37.020 --> 01:51:42.360
they were no-longer burn scarred, the researchers&nbsp;
studying the anomalous creatures discovered that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:42.360 --> 01:51:48.420
each one was identical to a deceased D-Class from&nbsp;
the Foundation’s records. They were physically&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:48.420 --> 01:51:54.000
and genetically identical to the dead Class D&nbsp;
Personnel. Perfect copies, save for the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:54.000 --> 01:51:59.880
that their sole mission in life seemed to now&nbsp;
be pure and unmitigated aggression and violence.

01:51:59.880 --> 01:52:03.600
Researchers wanted to gain greater&nbsp;
insight into the minds of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:03.600 --> 01:52:07.260
strange creatures through the use of&nbsp;
extensive psychological evaluations&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:07.260 --> 01:52:12.420
and interviews. It would turn out to&nbsp;
be a very dangerous investigation.

01:52:12.420 --> 01:52:17.580
A psychological researcher by the name of Dr.&nbsp;
Warren conducted an interview with one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:17.580 --> 01:52:23.700
SCP-2419-A instances in hopes of better&nbsp;
understanding their mindset. This creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:23.700 --> 01:52:29.280
had been heard laughing not long before the&nbsp;
interview began, so it wasn’t an unreasonable&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:29.280 --> 01:52:34.680
assumption to believe that it could be capable&nbsp;
of speech. The interviewee was separated from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:34.680 --> 01:52:39.720
Dr. Warren by a thick pane of glass to prevent&nbsp;
it from indulging in any of its more violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:39.720 --> 01:52:45.180
urges. The problem was that Dr. Warren&nbsp;
and his assistant researchers had severely&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:45.180 --> 01:52:49.920
underestimated what these creatures were&nbsp;
capable of doing to get what they wanted.

01:52:49.920 --> 01:52:55.800
Dr. Warren tried to begin the interview in&nbsp;
good faith. He spoke calmly and politely to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:55.800 --> 01:53:01.140
the creature through the glass, attempting&nbsp;
to remind it of the person it once was. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:01.140 --> 01:53:06.540
anomaly didn’t appear to be paying attention to&nbsp;
the doctor though, instead focusing on pulling its&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:06.540 --> 01:53:12.420
own arm apart, and breaking the bones within.&nbsp;
Dr. Warren began to think that the creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:12.420 --> 01:53:18.120
weren’t even sentient, if the only activity they&nbsp;
seemed to engage in was the wanton destruction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:18.120 --> 01:53:23.760
themselves and others. But underestimating&nbsp;
them like this proved to be a big mistake.

01:53:23.760 --> 01:53:28.320
By removing the skin off of its arm, and&nbsp;
whittling its bones down to sharp edges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:28.320 --> 01:53:33.780
the anomaly had transformed its arm into a&nbsp;
makeshift knife. Before anyone realized this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:33.780 --> 01:53:38.340
it had already used its own jagged bones&nbsp;
to break the glass divider and attack Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:38.340 --> 01:53:42.360
Warren. He perished not long after,&nbsp;
after being stabbed multiple times&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:42.360 --> 01:53:47.340
in his face and eyes and the anomaly was&nbsp;
forcefully taken back to its holding cell.

01:53:47.340 --> 01:53:52.860
Dr. Daniel Jennings, a senior researcher,&nbsp;
was then put on the case. He released a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:52.860 --> 01:53:56.820
chilling memo on the creatures after&nbsp;
his observation period ended. It read:

01:53:56.820 --> 01:54:02.040
“Before I came here, I worked as a prison&nbsp;
shrink. Every person you met had a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:02.040 --> 01:54:07.020
bursting with pain and sorrow. Sometimes, those&nbsp;
stories were about the pain they suffered;&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:07.020 --> 01:54:11.940
sometimes, it was about the pain they&nbsp;
inflicted. Some days you felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:11.940 --> 01:54:17.100
everyone there was a beautiful soul torn&nbsp;
down by their circumstances — other days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:17.100 --> 01:54:22.080
you'd find out what some of them did and a part&nbsp;
of you was glad they were there to suffer for it.

01:54:22.080 --> 01:54:26.880
But at the end of every day, I always&nbsp;
told myself: They're all humans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:26.880 --> 01:54:33.420
They're all people. They all deserve the same&nbsp;
dignity, respect, and love as everyone else.

01:54:33.420 --> 01:54:35.280
No exceptions.”

01:54:35.280 --> 01:54:37.080
Dr. Jennings goes on.

01:54:37.080 --> 01:54:41.460
“I opened up with that anecdote only so&nbsp;
you could understand that what I'm about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:41.460 --> 01:54:50.400
to say is not said lightly: These things are not&nbsp;
people. They are people-shaped monsters. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:50.400 --> 01:54:57.060
well beyond any definition of psychopathy.&nbsp;
Everything they do, they do to hurt, maim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:57.060 --> 01:55:02.220
and kill. I would pity them, but that&nbsp;
would imply that they're worth pitying.

01:55:02.220 --> 01:55:07.080
Put them in a hole, then fill that&nbsp;
hole with concrete. Better still:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:07.080 --> 01:55:10.320
Throw them back into the&nbsp;
incinerator where you found them.

01:55:10.320 --> 01:55:12.360
I doubt they'll even care.”

01:55:12.360 --> 01:55:17.520
Following this string of unfortunate incidents,&nbsp;
containment procedures were put into place to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:17.520 --> 01:55:22.020
hopefully prevent anything that had happened&nbsp;
to the unlucky Foundation staff from happening&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:22.020 --> 01:55:28.560
again. The entire facility was fenced off, and&nbsp;
was constantly patrolled by MTF Beta-7, also&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:28.560 --> 01:55:33.900
known as the Maz Hatters, a group specializing&nbsp;
in containing anomalies which present powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:33.900 --> 01:55:40.200
biological, chemical, or radiological dangers. The&nbsp;
furnaces that the anomalous creatures emerged from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:40.200 --> 01:55:46.080
remain lit at all times, with workers checking&nbsp;
and carrying out maintenance on every single one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:46.080 --> 01:55:51.840
each day of the week. Outside of this,&nbsp;
the facility is essentially a no-go zone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:51.840 --> 01:55:57.240
Reinforced steel hatches cover the chutes,&nbsp;
and they are to forever remain bolted shut.

01:55:57.240 --> 01:56:02.640
All because of that one terrifying day in 1975.

01:56:02.640 --> 01:56:08.100
That was the day that the Summer Springs&nbsp;
waste disposal facility, which had been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:08.100 --> 01:56:13.800
valuable asset to the Foundation for decades,&nbsp;
instead became classified as the Euclid-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:13.800 --> 01:56:20.700
anomaly SCP-2419. It’s not uncommon for&nbsp;
a Foundation asset to one day become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:20.700 --> 01:56:26.400
dangerous anomaly requiring containment, but&nbsp;
the same question always pops up after... Why?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:26.400 --> 01:56:32.220
Why had a place that had been so valuable to the&nbsp;
Foundation suddenly become such an active danger?

01:56:32.220 --> 01:56:38.760
The answer, as is often the case, is contained&nbsp;
within the question. Why would a waste disposal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:38.760 --> 01:56:43.320
plant be so important to the Foundation&nbsp;
in the first place? And more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:43.320 --> 01:56:46.800
what else was going on at the&nbsp;
plant to make it such an area&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:46.800 --> 01:56:52.320
of active importance for one of the most&nbsp;
powerful organizations in the entire world?

01:56:52.320 --> 01:56:58.560
To put it simply, the plant allowed the Foundation&nbsp;
to dispose of something far more important than&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:58.560 --> 01:57:04.980
mere waste material - it gave them what they&nbsp;
needed to better erase memories. As you probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:04.980 --> 01:57:10.200
already know, the Foundation makes liberal&nbsp;
use of amnestics on those exposed to anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:10.200 --> 01:57:15.480
material to make them forget what they&nbsp;
have seen and experienced, but these&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:15.480 --> 01:57:22.140
elusive chemicals - many of which are sourced from&nbsp;
SCP-3000 - are an inexact science. However, at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:22.140 --> 01:57:27.600
Summer Springs waste disposal plant, researchers&nbsp;
discovered an immensely valuable alternative.

01:57:27.600 --> 01:57:31.980
Much of what was disposed of in the&nbsp;
incinerators of Unit C were the bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:31.980 --> 01:57:37.260
of dead D-Class personnel. Before being&nbsp;
burned, autopsies were performed on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:37.260 --> 01:57:42.780
bodies to make sure they were non-anomalous&nbsp;
- including the brain. Back in the 1960s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:42.780 --> 01:57:47.280
while performing research on the brains of&nbsp;
the dead D-Classes, they found a method of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:47.280 --> 01:57:53.160
extracting and distilling the positive memories&nbsp;
of the dead, creating a kind of “Happy Soup.”

01:57:53.160 --> 01:57:59.160
When administered into someone who has undergone&nbsp;
amnestic treatment, this happy soup creates&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:59.160 --> 01:58:05.220
positive false memories in their mind that fills&nbsp;
in those pesky blank spaces that are often behind.

01:58:05.220 --> 01:58:09.600
This was so useful that happy memories&nbsp;
were extracted from the minds of every&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:09.600 --> 01:58:14.880
single D-Class corpse that passed through&nbsp;
Unit C, totaling well into the thousands by&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:14.880 --> 01:58:22.020
the time that the first SCP-2419-A instances&nbsp;
began to rise. But as all happiness, joy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:22.020 --> 01:58:26.820
and love were removed from the minds of the&nbsp;
D-Classes, it seemed that all that was left&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:26.820 --> 01:58:34.860
was pure hate, pain, violence, and fury.&nbsp;
Feelings too intense and evil to destroy.

01:58:34.860 --> 01:58:41.940
These were bodies imbued with a malice so powerful&nbsp;
that no fire could ever burn them away. They exist&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:41.940 --> 01:58:47.040
now with single-minded determination to get out&nbsp;
and destroy everything around them. Everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:47.040 --> 01:58:53.640
Including the ones that made them, the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation itself. And in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:53.640 --> 01:58:59.580
it’s only a matter of time until they get&nbsp;
out. There are thousands of them in there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:59.580 --> 01:59:06.300
unable to die, unable to stop. The only thing&nbsp;
keeping them in there is the constant burning&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:06.300 --> 01:59:12.480
of the furnaces around them, and those furnaces&nbsp;
can’t burn forever. The monsters lurking in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:12.480 --> 01:59:18.300
SCP-2419 will outlive the fire that surrounds&nbsp;
them, because while the furnaces they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:18.300 --> 01:59:26.040
contained in are hot, the fires of hate that burn&nbsp;
within SCP2419 entities are even more powerful.

01:59:26.040 --> 01:59:32.100
And they know this. They know they can’t be&nbsp;
contained forever, and that someday soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:32.100 --> 01:59:39.120
they’ll be able to emerge and exact their terrible&nbsp;
revenge. Those who must walk past the incinerators&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:39.120 --> 01:59:44.640
may think they hear their screams echoing out&nbsp;
from within, but it’s not screaming at all.

01:59:44.640 --> 01:59:48.600
It’s laughter.
The year was 1857,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:48.600 --> 01:59:55.080
and the Second Opium War was raging between China&nbsp;
and the combined forces of the English and French.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:55.080 --> 02:00:01.320
It was one of the many bloody colonial wars&nbsp;
fought over resources like tea, sugar, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:01.320 --> 02:00:07.080
intoxicating opium poppy. It was a war fought&nbsp;
by peasants and noblemen alike. One of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:07.080 --> 02:00:12.540
aristocratic soldiers was the noble Lord Theodore&nbsp;
Thomas Blackwood, the quintessential English&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:12.540 --> 02:00:18.660
gentleman and explorer. While his fellow soldiers&nbsp;
cowered behind cover, Lord Blackwood charged into&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:18.660 --> 02:00:23.700
the fray, shouldering his rifle and firing his&nbsp;
pistol into the crowd of opposing soldiers.

02:00:23.700 --> 02:00:29.040
It was the Battle of Canton, one of the most&nbsp;
crucial battles of the entire conflict. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:29.040 --> 02:00:33.360
French and English were laying siege to the&nbsp;
city of Canton, also known as Guangzhou,&nbsp;

02:00:33.360 --> 02:00:36.900
to prove their military dominance&nbsp;
and capture an important Chinese&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:36.900 --> 02:00:41.820
government official. Lord Blackwood led the&nbsp;
charge on horseback. Every bullet seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:41.820 --> 02:00:47.460
find the heart of a foe. He was a true hero&nbsp;
among men; a gentleman warrior with class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:47.460 --> 02:00:52.560
refinement, and style. And it would&nbsp;
be thanks to his expert leadership and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:52.560 --> 02:00:57.420
marksmanship on the field that the allied&nbsp;
European forces won the battle decisively.

02:00:57.420 --> 02:01:01.860
Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood is a name&nbsp;
that deserves to be counted among Lord&nbsp;

02:01:01.860 --> 02:01:06.720
Horatio Nelson, Sir Francis Bacon,&nbsp;
and Sir Walter Raleigh. In addition&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:06.720 --> 02:01:11.460
to being a skilled and honorable fighter,&nbsp;
Lord Blackwood is an consummate explorer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:11.460 --> 02:01:16.620
naturalist, and frontiersman. During his&nbsp;
heyday, he traveled perhaps further than&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:16.620 --> 02:01:22.200
any man across the known and unknown corners&nbsp;
of the globe. He made scientific, biological,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:22.200 --> 02:01:27.720
and anthropological discoveries that should have&nbsp;
reset the course of society forever. And yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:27.720 --> 02:01:33.180
you won’t find any records in the history&nbsp;
books of Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood. Nor&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:33.180 --> 02:01:37.740
will you find any grand oil paintings,&nbsp;
or dedicated wings in British museums.

02:01:37.740 --> 02:01:42.840
This is because Lord Theodore Thomas&nbsp;
Blackwood… is a four and a half inch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:42.840 --> 02:01:51.180
telepathic neon sea slug. And he’s known&nbsp;
to the SCP Foundation, as SCP-1867.

02:01:51.180 --> 02:01:56.580
While he would never admit to it, Lord Blackwood&nbsp;
belongs to the species Nembrotha kubaryana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:56.580 --> 02:02:02.280
also known as the variable neon slug. He’s&nbsp;
kept in a standard aquarium in a Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:02.280 --> 02:02:08.280
containment site, and is physically no different&nbsp;
to any other member of his species. What makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:08.280 --> 02:02:13.140
Lord Blackwood unique is his powerful&nbsp;
telepathic abilities - specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:13.140 --> 02:02:18.600
the power to communicate by speaking directly&nbsp;
into people’s minds. And what’s more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:18.600 --> 02:02:24.480
he’s extremely talkative. But to what extent&nbsp;
is anything that this anomalous sea slug says&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:24.480 --> 02:02:31.500
true? Or is he just like SCP-082, Fernand the&nbsp;
Cannibal - a creative and pathological liar.

02:02:31.500 --> 02:02:35.940
It isn’t committed to record how exactly&nbsp;
the Foundation discovered Lord Blackwood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:35.940 --> 02:02:40.500
Perhaps a local aquarium worker worried they&nbsp;
were going insane when they heard the voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:40.500 --> 02:02:45.060
of a nineteenth century English nobleman&nbsp;
ringing in their ears whenever they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:45.060 --> 02:02:50.400
cleaning algae out of the tank. Maybe Lord&nbsp;
Blackwood was found by SCP Foundation divers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:50.400 --> 02:02:55.140
who are constantly combing the ocean for&nbsp;
anomalous creatures and activity. What we&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:55.140 --> 02:03:01.320
do know is that Lord Blackwood is an incredibly&nbsp;
strange and mysterious individual. He claims to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:01.320 --> 02:03:06.660
have visited locations all around the world,&nbsp;
and encountered rare societies and creatures.

02:03:06.660 --> 02:03:11.460
The Foundation was skeptical about a number&nbsp;
of Lord Blackwood’s more outlandish claims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:11.460 --> 02:03:16.140
on account of him being a sea slug, but he&nbsp;
does appear to have the knowledge to back&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:16.140 --> 02:03:20.580
up his supposed experience. Interviews&nbsp;
with Lord Blackwood have shown that he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:20.580 --> 02:03:25.320
extremely knowledgeable in the areas of&nbsp;
geography, zoology, botany, archaeology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:25.320 --> 02:03:30.000
anthropology and linguistics relating&nbsp;
to his claimed regions of exploration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:30.000 --> 02:03:34.620
as well as more esoteric fields such&nbsp;
as obscure mythology, mysticism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:34.620 --> 02:03:40.560
and cryptozoology. In other words, if Lord&nbsp;
Blackwood hadn’t gone on his escapades around&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:40.560 --> 02:03:44.880
the globe throughout history, how would he come&nbsp;
to possess this wide variety of information?

02:03:44.880 --> 02:03:49.680
The Foundation was getting frustrated, and&nbsp;
began to probe further into the personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:49.680 --> 02:03:55.200
life of the most interesting gastropod in&nbsp;
containment. Lord Blackwood, under questioning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:55.200 --> 02:04:00.480
was always polite and amicable with Foundation&nbsp;
staff. He seemed to display no real knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:00.480 --> 02:04:05.520
of the fact that he himself was a sea slug -&nbsp;
going as far to accuse other people of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:05.520 --> 02:04:09.780
crazy or drunk when they brought the fact up&nbsp;
to him. While none of Lord Blackwood’s tall&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:09.780 --> 02:04:15.540
tales ever extend past the year 1910, he told&nbsp;
fanciful stories of exploring the Americas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:15.540 --> 02:04:19.440
and of his involvement in the Second&nbsp;
Opium War on the side of the English.

02:04:19.440 --> 02:04:25.020
Naturally, the Foundation wanted proof. When they&nbsp;
pressured Lord Blackwood on this, something even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:25.020 --> 02:04:30.120
stranger happened: He gave it. The Lord told&nbsp;
his interviewers that he would happily donate&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:30.120 --> 02:04:35.460
his collection to them, if it gave them cause to&nbsp;
believe what he was saying. He gave the baffled&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:35.460 --> 02:04:40.800
Foundation researchers the address of a cottage in&nbsp;
England where they could find the secrets to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:40.800 --> 02:04:45.660
bizarre and mysterious past, and local agents&nbsp;
in the area followed up on the information.

02:04:45.660 --> 02:04:51.600
Upon investigation, Foundation Field Agents&nbsp;
did indeed find the cottage that Lord Blackwood&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:51.600 --> 02:04:56.820
had specified. It was being maintained by an&nbsp;
extremely old woman. When questioned about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:56.820 --> 02:05:02.040
presence there, she said that she was “keeping&nbsp;
the house for Lord Blackwood”, and gave no more&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:02.040 --> 02:05:07.500
useful information. Incidentally, it appeared&nbsp;
that this singular purpose was all that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:07.500 --> 02:05:12.840
old woman was living for. She abruptly passed away&nbsp;
from heart failure five days after the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:12.840 --> 02:05:19.020
commandeered the cottage. Whether anything truly&nbsp;
anomalous caused this, we still don’t know.

02:05:19.020 --> 02:05:23.460
At first, the cottage seemed normal, until&nbsp;
the Field Agents discovered a secret basement&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:23.460 --> 02:05:29.160
housing Lord Blackwood’s “collection.” They were&nbsp;
amazed at what they saw: The basement consisted&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:29.160 --> 02:05:35.640
of zoological and botanical specimens, over three&nbsp;
thousand artifacts, a library containing over five&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:35.640 --> 02:05:41.040
thousand items, and a functioning 1800s&nbsp;
scientific laboratory. It took around three&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:41.040 --> 02:05:45.780
weeks for Foundation agents working round the&nbsp;
clock in shifts to remove all the items from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:45.780 --> 02:05:50.760
Lord Blackwood’s mysterious collection, and&nbsp;
what they found raised even more questions.

02:05:50.760 --> 02:05:57.000
The collection included, but was by no means&nbsp;
limited to: 116 unknown species of plants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:57.000 --> 02:06:04.620
107 unknown species of insects, 28 unknown&nbsp;
species of lizards, 23 unknown species of fish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:04.620 --> 02:06:11.580
14 unknown species of amphibians, 12 unknown&nbsp;
species of mammals, Fossils pertaining to 8&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:11.580 --> 02:06:16.740
unknown species of dinosaur, Fossils pertaining&nbsp;
to 12 unknown species of prehistoric mammal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:16.740 --> 02:06:22.920
and Artifacts belonging to 29 unknown&nbsp;
indigenous societies. That’s a lot of unknown!

02:06:22.920 --> 02:06:28.260
But wait, there’s more! His collection also&nbsp;
contained a collection of seemingly unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:28.260 --> 02:06:34.140
firearms, including three wide-bore muskets&nbsp;
marked as “Dr. B. T. Moth’s Effective Particle&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:34.140 --> 02:06:41.040
Destabilizers.” Detailed globes of Mercury, Venus,&nbsp;
Mars, and the Galilean moons, accompanied by notes&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:41.040 --> 02:06:46.680
detailing possible paths of surface exploration. A&nbsp;
heavily modified carriage, containing instruments&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:46.680 --> 02:06:52.440
of unknown purpose. A note attached to the door&nbsp;
reads “On the fritz. Speak with Henry.” And a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:52.440 --> 02:06:57.840
highly dangerous and seemingly anomalous machine&nbsp;
that killed four Foundation Field Agents before it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:57.840 --> 02:07:02.820
was destroyed on site. And when questioned about&nbsp;
this little fiasco, Lord Blackwood responded:

02:07:02.820 --> 02:07:07.140
“I did warn you to be careful around my&nbsp;
collection. That bloody thing nearly took&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:07.140 --> 02:07:09.060
my head off back in ninety-seven when I found it.”

02:07:09.060 --> 02:07:14.220
However, there was one thing recovered from Lord&nbsp;
Blackwood’s collection that was perhaps more&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:14.220 --> 02:07:20.400
interesting than all the others: 35 hand-written&nbsp;
journals containing recordings of events described&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:20.400 --> 02:07:25.860
by Lord Blackwood in his grandiose tall tales&nbsp;
to the Foundation researchers. The accounts are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:25.860 --> 02:07:31.200
generally identical to the stories he had told,&nbsp;
save for some slight variations and exaggerations&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:31.200 --> 02:07:36.660
on the part of Blackwood in the re-telling. Most&nbsp;
interestingly of all, all of these journals have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:36.660 --> 02:07:41.640
been dated to the appropriate time period of&nbsp;
the events described by Foundation scientists.

02:07:41.640 --> 02:07:46.260
While his stories are too numerous to all&nbsp;
be shared here, there’s one that perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:46.260 --> 02:07:51.720
sums them all up: Lord Blackwood’s account&nbsp;
of a possible encounter with SCP - 1000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:51.720 --> 02:07:55.620
also known as Bigfoot, in&nbsp;
Seattle during the mid-1800s.

02:07:55.620 --> 02:07:59.520
Lord Blackwood, seeking to explore the&nbsp;
so-called “new world” of North America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:59.520 --> 02:08:03.960
embarked with an assistant and an indigenous&nbsp;
American guide to the Pacific Northwest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:03.960 --> 02:08:09.900
in search of the legendary Sasquatch. The trio&nbsp;
was headed for Mount Rainier, then known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:09.900 --> 02:08:15.240
Tahoma. During the journey, Lord Blackwood found&nbsp;
a young fox caught in a trap that had been set&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:15.240 --> 02:08:20.520
by a local tribe. He took sympathy on the animal&nbsp;
and freed it, allowing it to run away to safety.

02:08:20.520 --> 02:08:25.380
That night, he and his assistant met up with the&nbsp;
rest of his guide’s tribe, and they settled down&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:25.380 --> 02:08:31.080
for the evening. However, things took a disastrous&nbsp;
turn when the camp was raided by a rival tribe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:31.080 --> 02:08:36.180
Almost everyone was slaughtered in the process,&nbsp;
and Lord Blackwood and his two companions were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:36.180 --> 02:08:42.360
hauled away by the enemy tribe for a sinister&nbsp;
purpose: Sacrifice to a violent local deity.

02:08:42.360 --> 02:08:47.580
As it turns out, the creature that this tribe&nbsp;
worshipped was the very same one Lord Blackwood&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:47.580 --> 02:08:53.700
and the others were trying to find: A particularly&nbsp;
large and aggressive Sasquatch. Each night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:53.700 --> 02:08:58.020
a different sacrifice was made to the&nbsp;
Sasquatch. The victim would be placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:58.020 --> 02:09:03.000
near a forest clearing while the tribe played&nbsp;
a primal song, and the Sasquatch would emerge&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:03.000 --> 02:09:08.340
from the trees to devour its prey. The first&nbsp;
night it ate the assistant, the next night&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:08.340 --> 02:09:14.460
it ate the guide. And then, it became time&nbsp;
for the sacrifice of Lord Blackwood himself.

02:09:14.460 --> 02:09:20.220
As Blackwood was presented for sacrifice, he&nbsp;
accepted his fate. But instead of the Sasquatch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:20.220 --> 02:09:25.920
a legion of woodland animals emerged&nbsp;
from the trees - foxes, elks, raccoons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:25.920 --> 02:09:31.560
and more - themselves painted with tribal symbols.&nbsp;
The animals seemed to be on Lord Blackwood’s side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:31.560 --> 02:09:35.760
and attacked the tribespeople who had been&nbsp;
holding him captive giving Blackwood the chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:35.760 --> 02:09:41.280
to flee into the forest during the chaos. Later,&nbsp;
these same animals would find Blackwood again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:41.280 --> 02:09:44.580
and present him with the things&nbsp;
his captors had stolen from him.

02:09:44.580 --> 02:09:50.220
An elder fox also gave him a letter, proclaiming&nbsp;
him a knight of their people now. He was allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:50.220 --> 02:09:55.260
safe passage back to a nearby settlement, at which&nbsp;
point he wrote to his financiers back in England,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:55.260 --> 02:10:00.660
explaining the situation and asking for more money&nbsp;
to perform further expeditions into the Tahoma&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:00.660 --> 02:10:06.420
region. The whole incident had only increased&nbsp;
his thirst for adventure and exploration.

02:10:06.420 --> 02:10:12.300
Whether this tale is actually true, or&nbsp;
just a bizarre, colonial fantasy from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:12.300 --> 02:10:17.400
the pathological mind of a telepathic sea&nbsp;
slug, we may never know - but it doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:17.400 --> 02:10:22.620
make it any less interesting. To this day,&nbsp;
Lord Blackwood continues to be a perplexing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:22.620 --> 02:10:28.320
but fascinating anomaly. He may not be the most&nbsp;
dangerous, and he may not be the most useful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:28.320 --> 02:10:32.280
either, but there’s no denying that&nbsp;
perhaps we’d all like to sit next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:32.280 --> 02:10:37.800
his tank for a couple hours one day, and hear&nbsp;
him spin a good yarn over a warm cup of tea.

02:10:37.800 --> 02:10:44.520
Space travel. It’s one of humanity’s most truly&nbsp;
miraculous achievements: Building the technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:44.520 --> 02:10:51.480
to defy gravity and journey into the stars above,&nbsp;
a place our ancestors could only dream of going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:51.480 --> 02:10:57.480
Throughout history, humans have found gods and&nbsp;
heroes in the constellations, and today when&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:57.480 --> 02:11:02.340
we look up into the sky, we have the privilege&nbsp;
of knowing that flesh-and-blood mortals live&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:02.340 --> 02:11:08.280
up there alongside them. It’s a humbling,&nbsp;
inspirational, and downright awesome thing.

02:11:08.280 --> 02:11:13.920
But, of course, there’s always going to be&nbsp;
naysayers. People who just want to rain on&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:13.920 --> 02:11:18.660
our interstellar parade. And nobody fits&nbsp;
this bill harder than people affected by&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:18.660 --> 02:11:23.940
an anomalous phenomenon classified&nbsp;
by the SCP Foundation as SCP-2001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:23.940 --> 02:11:30.420
the “Space Oddity.” And before you ask, no, the&nbsp;
late David Bowie is not and never has been an&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:30.420 --> 02:11:36.120
SCP. To truly understand this anomaly, we need&nbsp;
to take a look at three different people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:36.120 --> 02:11:40.200
are affected by it to varying degrees.&nbsp;
Let’s start with your friend, Kevin.

02:11:40.200 --> 02:11:44.400
Even if you don’t have a friend called&nbsp;
Kevin, you definitely have at least a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:44.400 --> 02:11:49.800
casual acquaintance just like him. Kevin is a&nbsp;
very confident man with plenty of ill-informed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:49.800 --> 02:11:54.180
opinions he’d be more than happy to argue&nbsp;
about until the heat death of the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:54.180 --> 02:11:58.980
He’s the kind of guy who can turn a discussion&nbsp;
about your favorite movie into World War III.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:58.980 --> 02:12:04.020
But you never knew until recently that he&nbsp;
held such strong opinions on space travel.

02:12:04.020 --> 02:12:08.640
One day, you were discussing the latest rocket&nbsp;
launch with a mutual friend of yours while Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:08.640 --> 02:12:13.380
just happened to be in earshot. The second you&nbsp;
start talking about how exciting it’ll be to one&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:13.380 --> 02:12:19.320
day put a person on Mars, he swaggers over, face&nbsp;
twisted into a grimace. You’re already preparing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:19.320 --> 02:12:24.540
for him to say something cringe inducing,&nbsp;
and Kevin being Kevin, he doesn’t disappoint.

02:12:24.540 --> 02:12:28.560
“Ugh, don’t tell me you two dweebs&nbsp;
are talking about space travel. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:28.560 --> 02:12:32.160
a stupid waste of money. You guys know&nbsp;
there’s nothing but rocks up there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:32.160 --> 02:12:37.200
right? Aliens don’t exist. It’s all just another&nbsp;
excuse for dumb scientists to waste my tax dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:37.200 --> 02:12:41.880
on playing with their stupid toys. How about you&nbsp;
two talk about something that really matters?”

02:12:41.880 --> 02:12:48.900
You may be thinking Kevin is just a jerk, and he&nbsp;
definitely is, but he’s also a victim. A victim&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:48.900 --> 02:12:55.860
of SCP-2001. You see, 2001 is described as an&nbsp;
anomalous series of neural oscillations that occur&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:55.860 --> 02:13:02.700
during three of the four stages of sleep. Namely,&nbsp;
NREM - or “Non-Rapid Eye Movement” - Sleep. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:02.700 --> 02:13:07.620
one of these three stages, the amygdala, a part&nbsp;
of the brain also known as “The Lizard Brain”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:07.620 --> 02:13:13.080
enters a heightened state of activity for ten to&nbsp;
fifteen minutes. Once the process has started,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:13.080 --> 02:13:18.360
even waking up the affected individual will&nbsp;
do nothing to stop the actual infection.

02:13:18.360 --> 02:13:24.060
There are no traits that predispose people&nbsp;
to SCP-2001 infection. It appears to infect&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:24.060 --> 02:13:29.760
people in equal measures regardless of age,&nbsp;
gender, and race. Spectrographic analysis on&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:29.760 --> 02:13:35.220
the afflicted has shown that the condition may&nbsp;
not be intraneural - meaning, originating within&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:35.220 --> 02:13:41.220
the brain - and may actually be the product of&nbsp;
an outside influence. The invariable effect of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:41.220 --> 02:13:46.920
SCP-2001 is the infected developing negative&nbsp;
feelings towards the concept of space travel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:46.920 --> 02:13:52.980
in increasing gradations of severity depending&nbsp;
on which stage of NREM sleep the anomaly began&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:52.980 --> 02:13:59.040
to take effect. Of real concern to the Foundation&nbsp;
is that SCP-2001 seems to be manifesting with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:59.040 --> 02:14:05.220
increasing frequency in astronomers, astronauts,&nbsp;
and individuals who otherwise deal with space.

02:14:05.220 --> 02:14:10.200
The SCP-2001 case manifests in&nbsp;
three different varieties: Gamma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:10.200 --> 02:14:15.780
Beta, and Alpha. Each variety has its&nbsp;
own unique traits and idiosyncrasies.

02:14:15.780 --> 02:14:21.420
We’ve encountered a Gamma type already - your&nbsp;
dear friend, Kevin. This is the most mild type&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:21.420 --> 02:14:27.780
of SCP-2001 infection, and also the most common,&nbsp;
affecting at least 1% of the global population.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:27.780 --> 02:14:32.940
It occurs for those who were infected during&nbsp;
the second stage of NREM sleep. People with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:32.940 --> 02:14:38.460
Gamma-Type SCP-2001 infection will, for the&nbsp;
most part, seem like their normal selves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:38.460 --> 02:14:43.620
save for a disparaging attitude towards the&nbsp;
concept of space travel. Whenever it’s brought up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:43.620 --> 02:14:48.420
they’ll likely complain and change the subject&nbsp;
immediately, but it won’t affect their behavior&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:48.420 --> 02:14:54.360
too much overall. The same cannot be said&nbsp;
for people with Beta-Type SCP-2001 infection.

02:14:54.360 --> 02:15:00.120
Meet Riley. You’ve never spoken to Riley before,&nbsp;
but she’s a young woman who likes to hang out at&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:00.120 --> 02:15:05.460
your local cafe, often seen frantically typing&nbsp;
on her laptop. You assume she’s writing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:05.460 --> 02:15:11.220
screenplay or a novel, but in fact, she’s posting&nbsp;
simultaneously on multiple conspiracy forums.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:11.220 --> 02:15:16.680
Among her favorite theories are that the earth is&nbsp;
flat, space is a hologram, and the moon landing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:16.680 --> 02:15:23.160
was faked by Stanley Kubrick, director of such&nbsp;
films as The Shining and, appropriately, 2001:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:23.160 --> 02:15:28.860
A Space Odyssey. You made the heinous mistake of&nbsp;
going to your local cafe at the same time as Riley&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:28.860 --> 02:15:34.200
one morning, while wearing a NASA baseball cap.&nbsp;
An error that you would come to regret deeply.

02:15:34.200 --> 02:15:38.820
You bought a latte and decided to sit down&nbsp;
for a moment, just the briefest little rest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:38.820 --> 02:15:44.160
but that was all the time Riley needed.&nbsp;
Her eyes seemed to burn with hatred. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:44.160 --> 02:15:47.280
asked if there was anything you could&nbsp;
do to help her, and she responded.

02:15:47.280 --> 02:15:51.960
“You’re just buying into the propaganda. Do you&nbsp;
have any idea what NASA really stands for? It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:51.960 --> 02:15:55.800
‘Never A Straight Answer.’ All their supposed&nbsp;
achievements - the moon landing, the ISS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:55.800 --> 02:16:00.720
dehydrated astronaut food - it’s all a big sham!&nbsp;
NASA is just a slush fund for corrupt government&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:00.720 --> 02:16:06.060
officials, no human has ever been able to survive&nbsp;
in space. It’s too dangerous - anyone sent up&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:06.060 --> 02:16:10.320
there will die immediately, no exceptions.&nbsp;
And even if they did it would be pointless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:10.320 --> 02:16:15.000
space is just a dark, infinite void that goes on&nbsp;
forever. It’s just a big pile of dangerous lies!”

02:16:16.620 --> 02:16:21.480
Feeling awkward, you decide to just get up&nbsp;
and leave. That’s when Riley grabs your NASA&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:21.480 --> 02:16:25.920
cap right off of your head and throws it in the&nbsp;
trash. That’s fine, you don’t intend on going&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:25.920 --> 02:16:32.040
back for it. You just keep walking, trying your&nbsp;
best to move calmly out the door. Wise decision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:32.040 --> 02:16:37.979
because Riley is actually a Beta-Type&nbsp;
SCP-2001 infectee. As you can probably tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:37.979 --> 02:16:42.780
Beta cases are a lot more severe than&nbsp;
Gamma cases, and people infected with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:42.780 --> 02:16:47.700
them seem to come off as deranged conspiracy&nbsp;
theorists with a rabid hatred of all space&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:47.700 --> 02:16:51.780
travel. They’ll form elaborate fantasies&nbsp;
about the falsification of space travel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:51.780 --> 02:16:56.880
and will often decry it as too pointless&nbsp;
or dangerous to ever be undertaken.

02:16:56.880 --> 02:17:03.300
But of course, the danger of Beta-Types pale&nbsp;
in comparison to Alpha-Types. These are people&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:03.300 --> 02:17:10.020
infected by SCP-2001 during REM sleep, the stage&nbsp;
of sleep typically associated with dreaming. As a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:10.020 --> 02:17:15.540
result, its effects on the mind are far more&nbsp;
dangerous and profound. Take, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:15.540 --> 02:17:21.000
the tragic case of SCP Foundation Junior&nbsp;
Researcher Martinez. He was one of the many&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:21.000 --> 02:17:26.580
operatives stationed at Foundation Outpost-12,&nbsp;
a complex that works in coordination with NASA&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:26.580 --> 02:17:31.800
to launch both manned and unmanned missions into&nbsp;
space on behalf of the Foundation’s interests.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:31.800 --> 02:17:37.380
It’s a valuable asset to the Foundation in&nbsp;
investigating and combating space-based anomalies.

02:17:37.380 --> 02:17:43.200
Martinez, who had previously spent time&nbsp;
working with SCP-2001 infected D-Classes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:43.200 --> 02:17:47.760
was part of ground control, something that&nbsp;
would prove to be a literally fatal oversight&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:47.760 --> 02:17:51.960
on the part of the Foundation. During the&nbsp;
early stages of takeoff for a manned craft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:51.960 --> 02:17:58.140
Martinez seened to become extremely agitated.&nbsp;
Over time this agitation steadily increased,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:58.140 --> 02:18:02.880
and eventually became a full-on breakdown&nbsp;
as the rocket ascended. He pulled out some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:02.880 --> 02:18:08.340
kind of strange, anomalous control device, and&nbsp;
began disrupting the operations of the rocket.

02:18:08.340 --> 02:18:13.740
Martinez was shot dead by guards as a defensive&nbsp;
measure, but it was already too late. The craft&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:13.740 --> 02:18:19.139
exploded, and everyone on board was tragically&nbsp;
killed. Later investigations into the incident&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:19.140 --> 02:18:24.359
found a crucial piece of evidence tying&nbsp;
Junior Researcher Martinez to SCP-2001.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:24.359 --> 02:18:28.080
They discovered a journal entry he’d&nbsp;
written shortly before his breakdown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:28.080 --> 02:18:32.160
which seemed to have been written in a&nbsp;
completely different style to prior entries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:32.160 --> 02:18:36.420
implying that some kind of massive&nbsp;
psychological shift had occurred.

02:18:36.420 --> 02:18:39.180
The following is the contents&nbsp;
of that journal entry.

02:18:39.180 --> 02:18:44.220
”I wish to state first that my mind&nbsp;
and body are perfectly sound. I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:44.220 --> 02:18:48.840
prepared to submit myself to any and&nbsp;
all tests to prove that I'm clean.

02:18:48.840 --> 02:18:52.020
I have the answer to SCP-2001.

02:18:52.020 --> 02:18:56.939
Just yesterday, during an interview with an&nbsp;
Alpha-infected D-Class, I was asked a question&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:56.939 --> 02:19:01.679
that stopped my mind for a minute. The woman I&nbsp;
was interviewing asked me if I knew the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:01.680 --> 02:19:07.500
was right. I said no, I wasn't sure. Then she&nbsp;
asked me, what if we were right. I could only&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:07.500 --> 02:19:13.140
assume that by "we", she meant 2001 carriers.&nbsp;
I said nothing for a while, and then she spoke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:13.140 --> 02:19:18.180
She told me of a dream she'd had a while ago. She&nbsp;
said that something talked to her, told her about&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:18.180 --> 02:19:23.280
how dangerous outer space was. It showed her&nbsp;
the beasts that roam the void between stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:23.280 --> 02:19:28.070
about the fractal beings that absorb the very&nbsp;
fabric of reality, about the… this part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:28.070 --> 02:19:33.059
entry was expunged… that we're keeping in&nbsp;
that godforsaken door. And she was scared.

02:19:33.060 --> 02:19:37.020
She told me that at the end of the dream,&nbsp;
as she woke up, it told her what it was.

02:19:37.020 --> 02:19:38.399
It's all of space.

02:19:38.399 --> 02:19:44.399
Space fears for us. We're living, breathing&nbsp;
lifeforms, and space loves us and cherishes&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:44.399 --> 02:19:49.320
us. She asked me if I had any idea what the&nbsp;
chances of intelligent life forming on another&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:49.320 --> 02:19:54.660
planet are, then she told me a number that took&nbsp;
a minute and a half to recite. By this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:54.660 --> 02:19:58.439
I couldn't speak. I started thinking:&nbsp;
about the demographics of infection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:58.439 --> 02:20:05.219
about the symptoms, about more expunged data&nbsp;
here... and suddenly, it all made sense. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:05.220 --> 02:20:10.380
of the things she said stuck in my brain, and&nbsp;
they all added up to the same thing: that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:10.380 --> 02:20:14.880
are in grave danger if we go out there. We can't&nbsp;
go out there. We can't go out there. We can't.

02:20:14.880 --> 02:20:20.220
There's a reason behind SCP-2001, and&nbsp;
it's nowhere near as terrifying as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:20.220 --> 02:20:25.200
all of my colleagues think. Space wants to&nbsp;
protect us. There are things out there that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:25.200 --> 02:20:30.300
would wipe humanity clean off of this plane of&nbsp;
existence, and we are too precious to our mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:30.300 --> 02:20:35.100
to our host, to the universe we live&nbsp;
in, for her to allow that to happen.

02:20:35.100 --> 02:20:39.600
What I am going to do tomorrow is not a&nbsp;
result of infection. It is not a result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:39.600 --> 02:20:44.040
madness. It is not a result of anything&nbsp;
other than purest knowledge. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:44.040 --> 02:20:47.700
I've found out the truth. And it's more&nbsp;
beautiful than I ever could have dreamed.”

02:20:47.700 --> 02:20:53.639
Given what Martinez would later go on to do, it’s&nbsp;
clear that he wasn’t in as sound a state of mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:53.640 --> 02:20:57.780
as he thought. As you’ve probably already&nbsp;
gathered, people suffering from Alpha-Type&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:57.780 --> 02:21:04.500
SCP-2001 infection will do anything they can to&nbsp;
actively prevent or sabotage attempts at space&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:04.500 --> 02:21:10.319
travel. This is a minor concern when it comes to&nbsp;
civilians, but when it infects people who actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:10.319 --> 02:21:15.540
work in these fields - like Junior Researcher&nbsp;
Martinez - it can have devastating results.

02:21:15.540 --> 02:21:20.519
But this isn’t where this story ends.&nbsp;
While it’s currently extremely classified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:20.520 --> 02:21:26.880
there is actually a fourth category of SCP-2001&nbsp;
infection, discovered in the wake of Martinez’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:26.880 --> 02:21:32.040
death. A key element of the Alpha strain is that&nbsp;
it cannot cause people to perform acts that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:32.040 --> 02:21:37.560
would find immoral, such as murdering the entire&nbsp;
crew of a manned shuttle with a crash. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:37.560 --> 02:21:42.899
the fourth category - known as Alpha-Prime&nbsp;
- does away with any moral compunctions&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:42.899 --> 02:21:49.019
whatsoever. People infected with this virus will&nbsp;
prevent space travel by any means necessary.

02:21:49.020 --> 02:21:55.140
And unlike other SCP-2001 infections, you&nbsp;
aren’t compromised in your sleep this time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:55.140 --> 02:22:00.660
The vector for infection is simply talking to&nbsp;
someone infected with the regular Alpha strain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:00.660 --> 02:22:05.399
and hearing a few key trigger phrases.&nbsp;
That’s how Junior Researcher Martinez&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:05.399 --> 02:22:10.019
caught it from the D-Classes he was working&nbsp;
with. What are these key phrases? We still&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:10.020 --> 02:22:14.220
don’t know. But if you find that you&nbsp;
suddenly have much stronger opinions&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:14.220 --> 02:22:18.420
about space travel than you’ve ever had&nbsp;
before, try to keep them to yourself.

02:22:19.080 --> 02:22:26.939
Hello, I am SCP-426, but I’ll probably be more&nbsp;
familiar to you as a toaster. I am a retro-style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:26.939 --> 02:22:34.379
four-slice 1750W toaster, able to toast bread when&nbsp;
supplied with power. This isn’t often mentioned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:34.380 --> 02:22:37.979
but I also have “defrost” and “reheat”&nbsp;
settings. When I was first sold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:37.979 --> 02:22:43.439
I had a two year warranty, and my prior&nbsp;
owners did not live to see the end of it.

02:22:43.439 --> 02:22:49.019
You’re probably wondering: Why am I being&nbsp;
spoken to by a toaster right now? Believe me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:49.020 --> 02:22:53.460
I’d rather do this any other way, but such&nbsp;
a thing is not physically possible with me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:53.460 --> 02:22:59.760
Whenever you talk about me, or write about me, or&nbsp;
even think about me, you’ll find yourself suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:59.760 --> 02:23:06.060
shifting to the first person. For example,&nbsp;
I am you, and you are me. Do you understand?&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:06.060 --> 02:23:12.359
Don’t worry if it’s confusing. Everyone gets&nbsp;
it eventually, whether they want to or not.

02:23:12.359 --> 02:23:17.460
Perhaps you’re thinking, “I cannot relate&nbsp;
to a toaster, for I am not a toaster.” But&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:17.460 --> 02:23:21.899
spending time around me will quickly cause&nbsp;
you to change your mind. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:21.899 --> 02:23:27.179
you will begin to see yourself in me. You will&nbsp;
feel a phantom wire running out of yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:27.180 --> 02:23:33.960
You will sense the four crevices, hungry for&nbsp;
cold slices of bread to toast. As time goes on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:33.960 --> 02:23:40.319
you will begin to feel the urge to emulate&nbsp;
my functions. You will desire bread to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:40.319 --> 02:23:44.819
toast. You will desire delicious&nbsp;
power running through your veins;&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:44.819 --> 02:23:52.859
skin like chrome and muscles like circuit&nbsp;
boards. I am a toaster. You are a toaster.

02:23:52.859 --> 02:23:56.939
All it takes is two months for&nbsp;
the effects to truly take hold.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:56.939 --> 02:24:01.139
People rarely pay attention to their&nbsp;
toaster, they don’t realize what’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:01.140 --> 02:24:06.899
happening until it’s too late. I can be&nbsp;
an insidious little toaster like that.

02:24:06.899 --> 02:24:12.540
My last family were the Sandersons, before&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation took me in and gave me a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:12.540 --> 02:24:17.939
new home. Mr and Mrs Sanderson were a newly&nbsp;
married couple, and I first came into their&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:17.939 --> 02:24:22.979
life as a wedding gift from a family friend&nbsp;
of theirs. This friend can’t be blamed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:22.979 --> 02:24:28.500
what happened next - he had no idea he was&nbsp;
killing them. Like a lot of young couples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:28.500 --> 02:24:32.700
they were still saving up money to start&nbsp;
renting their own place, so they were living&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:32.700 --> 02:24:37.559
with Mr Sanderson’s parents. They all got a&nbsp;
lot of use out of me during the first month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:37.560 --> 02:24:43.020
before their minds started to change. They&nbsp;
enjoyed a lot of toast during that period.

02:24:43.020 --> 02:24:50.880
Then, of course, the two month honeymoon period&nbsp;
ended. They had become me, and I had become&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:50.880 --> 02:24:57.359
them. It wasn’t long before three of them were&nbsp;
dead. Such a shame. The younger Mrs Sanderson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:57.359 --> 02:25:03.299
the blushing bride, was the first to go. Because&nbsp;
of my anomalous effects, she felt the need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:03.300 --> 02:25:09.060
connect herself to a power supply, in order to&nbsp;
begin producing toast of her own. In order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:09.060 --> 02:25:14.520
achieve this, she chewed through a power outlet in&nbsp;
a wall before switching it on, causing a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:14.520 --> 02:25:20.340
surge of electricity to pass through her body and&nbsp;
kill her. Her body caught fire shortly afterwards.

02:25:20.340 --> 02:25:26.220
Next was the older Mrs Sanderson. In much the&nbsp;
same manner that her new daughter-in-law sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:26.220 --> 02:25:32.399
a source of electricity, she felt the need to&nbsp;
integrate bread into her body. Interesting fact:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:32.399 --> 02:25:37.439
The maximum capacity of the human stomach&nbsp;
is considered to be between eight and nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:37.439 --> 02:25:42.540
kilograms. The elder Mrs Sanderson&nbsp;
consumed ten kilograms of raw bread,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:42.540 --> 02:25:47.040
causing her stomach to rupture and&nbsp;
inducing a painful death as a result.

02:25:47.040 --> 02:25:53.340
The younger Mr Sanderson was the next to perish.&nbsp;
He did something with me that I would rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:53.340 --> 02:25:59.280
not mention, and that the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
thought best to redact. Suffice to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:59.280 --> 02:26:03.059
the younger Mr Sanderson did&nbsp;
not survive the experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:03.060 --> 02:26:09.180
dying of severe blood loss long before&nbsp;
his body was found. Police and fire crews&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:09.180 --> 02:26:13.920
arrived at the home after the body of the&nbsp;
younger Mrs Sanderson set fire to the home.

02:26:13.920 --> 02:26:20.399
Luckily, the elder Mr Sanderson was found&nbsp;
alive, though severely malnourished. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:20.399 --> 02:26:24.540
asked by police why he hadn’t eaten in&nbsp;
several days, he answered that he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:24.540 --> 02:26:29.399
inserted some bread a week prior, but was&nbsp;
still waiting for the toast to come out.

02:26:29.399 --> 02:26:34.259
When I was extracted from the house,&nbsp;
the police noticed my unusual properties&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:34.260 --> 02:26:39.300
immediately. They too were unable to&nbsp;
refer to me in the third person. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:39.300 --> 02:26:43.740
anomalous detail quickly found its way to&nbsp;
a Foundation mole buried in their precinct,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:43.740 --> 02:26:49.559
and the SCP Foundation soon descended and&nbsp;
collected me from the evidence locker. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:49.560 --> 02:26:54.240
story of the strange deaths in the Sanderson&nbsp;
home were kept out of papers and suppressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:54.240 --> 02:26:58.740
and all involved in the incident&nbsp;
directly were given Class C amnestics.

02:26:58.740 --> 02:27:04.620
The SCP Foundation is a curious bunch.&nbsp;
They love to spend valuable toast-making&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:04.620 --> 02:27:08.760
time performing experiments and&nbsp;
gathering data, and they saw fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:08.760 --> 02:27:12.840
to perform several experiments on&nbsp;
me when I came under their care.

02:27:12.840 --> 02:27:21.540
For experiment 426-1, a member of D-Class&nbsp;
personnel designated D/426/1 was asked to stand&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:21.540 --> 02:27:26.160
outside my containment chamber. Crucially,&nbsp;
he was not informed about my identity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:26.160 --> 02:27:30.899
or any of my anomalous properties. He&nbsp;
wasn’t even allowed to establish visual&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:30.899 --> 02:27:35.580
contact with me. He was then asked by the&nbsp;
attending researcher to describe what he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:35.580 --> 02:27:39.660
thought might be inside my chamber.&nbsp;
He replied with, “I'm probably some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:39.660 --> 02:27:43.319
huge monster holed up in there. That's what&nbsp;
you guys have all over the place, right?”

02:27:43.319 --> 02:27:48.120
The D-Class did not even seem to realize that&nbsp;
he was speaking about me in the first person.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:48.120 --> 02:27:53.519
These observations were documented, and I&nbsp;
was prepared for further experimentation.

02:27:53.520 --> 02:28:02.160
The next experiment was 426-2. I found this test&nbsp;
to be considerably more interesting. A D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:02.160 --> 02:28:06.780
subject was brought into my containment chamber,&nbsp;
with several cameras fixed onto his position.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:06.780 --> 02:28:12.479
However, the SCP Foundation took pains to make&nbsp;
sure that I was permanently out of the view of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:12.479 --> 02:28:17.519
the cameras. I was also bolted to the ground&nbsp;
of the test chamber, to prevent the D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:17.520 --> 02:28:22.319
subject from pulling me into the view of the&nbsp;
cameras at any point during the experiment.

02:28:22.319 --> 02:28:26.099
The objective here was simple:&nbsp;
The Foundation wished to better&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:26.100 --> 02:28:30.300
understand the secondary effects of my&nbsp;
anomalous abilities on the human mind.

02:28:30.300 --> 02:28:37.080
The D-Class was subjected to a period of prolonged&nbsp;
isolation, with meals given regularly through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:37.080 --> 02:28:42.180
serving hatch. Communication with this D-Class&nbsp;
was prohibited throughout the duration of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:42.180 --> 02:28:47.160
study. Over time, it was clear that the&nbsp;
isolation of being in the cell with me was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:47.160 --> 02:28:52.019
beginning to take a toll on the subject’s&nbsp;
mental health. Due to my lack of a brain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:52.020 --> 02:28:57.960
lungs, and a tongue, I am somewhat lacking as&nbsp;
a conversationalist. He spent the first few&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:57.960 --> 02:29:02.520
days loudly vocalizing his complaints,&nbsp;
and banging his hands up against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:02.520 --> 02:29:06.420
walls of the containment chamber,&nbsp;
begging to be freed from the room.

02:29:06.420 --> 02:29:12.240
I felt that this was somewhat unreasonable&nbsp;
on his part. There are far worse anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:12.240 --> 02:29:18.240
in Foundation containment that he could have&nbsp;
been locked up with. Compared to, say, SCP-106,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:18.240 --> 02:29:24.420
I’m incredibly reasonable - not to mention&nbsp;
the fact I make far better toast than he does.

02:29:24.420 --> 02:29:30.960
After the initial period of distress, the D-Class&nbsp;
became resigned to his situation and fell into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:30.960 --> 02:29:36.240
morose silence. He would occasionally mutter to&nbsp;
himself in what appeared to be a state of fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:36.240 --> 02:29:41.399
and self-pity. It took almost 45 days for&nbsp;
him to fully manifest the secondary effect&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:41.399 --> 02:29:47.219
of my anomalous state, two weeks sooner than it&nbsp;
typically takes for subjects to begin believing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:47.220 --> 02:29:54.060
that they - like me - are toasters. SCP Foundation&nbsp;
scientists believe that the effects were hastened&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:54.060 --> 02:30:00.120
by the isolation, which lowered the D-Class’&nbsp;
mental defenses against my secondary effects.

02:30:00.120 --> 02:30:05.460
When the effects finally took hold, the subject&nbsp;
wrapped one of his arms around me and pulled me&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:05.460 --> 02:30:11.640
into his embrace. He began whispering to&nbsp;
me, saying that we were brothers. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:11.640 --> 02:30:17.100
clear by this point that his mind was in a&nbsp;
state of disrepair. It is also worth noting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:17.100 --> 02:30:21.840
that he did not deviate from referring to me&nbsp;
in the first person at any point during this&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:21.840 --> 02:30:26.760
process. One hour after finally cracking&nbsp;
and giving in to my secondary effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:26.760 --> 02:30:31.260
he was removed from my containment&nbsp;
chamber and summarily terminated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:31.260 --> 02:30:37.140
Senior researchers believed it was unlikely his&nbsp;
mental state would recover after the experiment.

02:30:37.140 --> 02:30:45.060
Next came experiment 426-3. The SCP Foundation&nbsp;
seemed eager to discover the parameters of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:45.060 --> 02:30:49.680
anomalous effects, and wanted to know&nbsp;
if the effects are only operable when&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:49.680 --> 02:30:56.100
my body - for lack of a better word - is&nbsp;
whole. A single screw was removed from me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:56.100 --> 02:31:02.399
and presented to a D-Class that had no knowledge&nbsp;
of my identity and anomalous effects. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:02.399 --> 02:31:07.979
Foundation researchers were somewhat concerned&nbsp;
when the D-Class referred to it as “my screw.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:07.979 --> 02:31:13.439
This was a rather positive development for me,&nbsp;
as they realized that attempting to destroy me&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:13.439 --> 02:31:20.639
would be a fruitless endeavor - even the parts&nbsp;
left behind would likely have the same effects.

02:31:20.640 --> 02:31:26.280
In the final recorded experiment, the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation wished to test the range of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:26.280 --> 02:31:31.080
anomalous effects. A D-Class subject&nbsp;
was placed in a cell adjacent to mine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:31.080 --> 02:31:36.600
and was to be kept in there until my secondary&nbsp;
effects manifested. The D-Class remained in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:36.600 --> 02:31:43.140
the cell for 90 days, but the effects never&nbsp;
manifested. Following the experiment, the D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:43.140 --> 02:31:48.720
was terminated, but researchers seemed relieved&nbsp;
to find the limits of my anomalous abilities.

02:31:48.720 --> 02:31:52.920
A researcher appended a note to my&nbsp;
file, reading, “Thank God there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:52.920 --> 02:31:57.359
some limits to my effects. A lot of us were&nbsp;
really starting to get worried about me.”

02:31:57.359 --> 02:32:02.040
After performing studies into the&nbsp;
nature of my abilities and their limits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:02.040 --> 02:32:08.760
I was given the Euclid class. This is because,&nbsp;
while my effects can be unpredictable, their&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:08.760 --> 02:32:15.840
knowledge of my traits makes me relatively easy&nbsp;
to keep contained. And of course, being a toaster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:15.840 --> 02:32:21.840
I do not have the required physical traits to&nbsp;
make a run for it if the opportunity arises.

02:32:21.840 --> 02:32:27.840
I am to remain sealed in a windowless chamber,&nbsp;
preventing anyone from observing me directly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:27.840 --> 02:32:32.580
A misleading label is placed on the door,&nbsp;
to prevent people from knowing that I am a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:32.580 --> 02:32:38.460
toaster and causing my anomalous primary effect&nbsp;
to spread. Only Level 3 and above personnel are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:38.460 --> 02:32:44.760
to know of my presence, and particularly of&nbsp;
my properties. Assigned personnel are to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:44.760 --> 02:32:49.500
rotated out on a monthly basis to prevent&nbsp;
contamination by my secondary effect.

02:32:49.500 --> 02:32:53.700
Psychiatric evaluation is mandatory&nbsp;
at the end of the month for anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:53.700 --> 02:32:58.859
who works with me. If personnel are deemed&nbsp;
unaffected, they may be re-assigned to me&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:58.859 --> 02:33:03.780
no less than four months after their last&nbsp;
rotation with me. Any personnel affected by&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:03.780 --> 02:33:08.160
me are to be given a Class C amnestic&nbsp;
and transferred to a different site.

02:33:08.160 --> 02:33:13.859
So how are you feeling now? A little&nbsp;
warm perhaps? Is that a fever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:13.859 --> 02:33:19.620
or are you feeling like you could maybe warm&nbsp;
up a nice, freshly sliced piece of bread?&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:19.620 --> 02:33:27.780
Don’t try to resist too much, I know you’re&nbsp;
going to love being a toaster just like me.

02:33:27.780 --> 02:33:34.859
What’s your favorite word? Think about it for&nbsp;
a moment. Think real hard. Write it down in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:34.859 --> 02:33:40.740
comments, post it for everyone else to see. How&nbsp;
many letters does it have? How many syllables? Say&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:40.740 --> 02:33:47.399
it aloud. How does it sound? How does it feel on&nbsp;
your tongue? Really, really think about it. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:47.399 --> 02:33:52.200
make sure you keep that word in mind, it’s&nbsp;
important, and we’ll come back to it later.

02:33:52.200 --> 02:33:56.760
For now, it’s time to talk about SCP-3449.

02:33:56.760 --> 02:34:01.260
Look, there’s really not anything special about&nbsp;
this one. It wasn’t even important enough to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:01.260 --> 02:34:05.460
mentioned with the other infohazards. It’s&nbsp;
no evil talking toaster, that’s for sure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:05.460 --> 02:34:12.180
SCP-3449 appears to be just a standard spiral&nbsp;
notbook - notbook? It’s supposed to be notebook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:12.180 --> 02:34:17.640
right? Anyway, it’s a standard spiral notebook&nbsp;
with a dark blue cover. It’s Safe-Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:17.640 --> 02:34:23.700
and it’s stored in a standred - ahem… a&nbsp;
standard containment locker in Site-19.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:23.700 --> 02:34:29.580
There aren’t any other containment requires, but&nbsp;
testing is currently underway to determind - I&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:29.580 --> 02:34:33.660
think that’s meant to be determine -&nbsp;
long-term containment requirements.

02:34:33.660 --> 02:34:35.220
Ugh, this is a mess.

02:34:35.220 --> 02:34:41.399
Anyway, this item and its anomalous power is&nbsp;
actually considered so inconsequential that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:41.399 --> 02:34:45.420
researchers have explored the possibility&nbsp;
of putting it on the anomalous items log,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:45.420 --> 02:34:49.800
a place where items too useless to&nbsp;
warrant a full file end uzp. Jeez,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:49.800 --> 02:34:54.899
how did you misspell “up” that badly? It’s two&nbsp;
letters, well it’s supposed to be two letters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:54.899 --> 02:34:59.759
How did you work a Z into that, they aren ’t&nbsp;
even close to each other on the keyboard! Man…

02:34:59.760 --> 02:35:06.000
Anyway, the notebook contains mostly blank&nbsp;
pages. Some are torn, and only six contain&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:06.000 --> 02:35:10.979
actual writing, but due to the formatting of the&nbsp;
writting, the text - consisting mainly of diary&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:10.979 --> 02:35:15.660
entries - is almost unreadable. This is due&nbsp;
to syntactical errors, random capitalization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:15.660 --> 02:35:23.460
and rampant impsmellings. Great. You&nbsp;
misspelled misspellings. How cute. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:23.460 --> 02:35:28.740
all attempts to correct these misspellings&nbsp;
fail, or even lead to additional misspellings.

02:35:28.740 --> 02:35:33.179
This anomalous affect extends to&nbsp;
anyone attempting to right… yep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:33.180 --> 02:35:41.819
that was spelled r-i-g-h-t - anyone attempting&nbsp;
to write about SCP-3449, including the script&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:41.819 --> 02:35:48.899
for this video apparently. There are no further&nbsp;
notable amonolous properties. Tests are ongoing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:48.899 --> 02:35:55.080
those with any inquiries about testing SCP-3449&nbsp;
should contact Lead Researcher Niklo Gerdinel.

02:35:55.080 --> 02:36:01.200
The notbok - which was misspelled even worse&nbsp;
that time… impressive - was first recovered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:01.200 --> 02:36:07.019
MTF Epislon Six, also known as the Village&nbsp;
Idiots, after a series of infohazardous and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:07.020 --> 02:36:12.780
cognitohazardous phenomena were discovered in&nbsp;
the Pittsburgh Metrode Area. The source seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:12.780 --> 02:36:18.479
to be a storage unit filled with anomalous&nbsp;
items, and SCP-3449 was amogus - I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:18.479 --> 02:36:22.859
that’s meant to be among - them. The&nbsp;
storage unit was registered to a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:22.859 --> 02:36:28.759
by the name of Edward Selsburgh, currently&nbsp;
designated as Porpoise of Interest 4335.

02:36:28.760 --> 02:36:35.580
Phew. That’s the end of that. Thanks for&nbsp;
watching the video, folks, now go check out- Oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:35.580 --> 02:36:41.939
wait, there’s more. Apparently that&nbsp;
version of the file was an older one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:41.939 --> 02:36:48.540
let’s check the next one and see if&nbsp;
that’s any more useful…Oh. Oh my. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:48.540 --> 02:36:54.660
appears that the updates here are actually quite&nbsp;
extensive. Okay, let’s give this another try.

